{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings","id":232331,"title":"Changeling 2.0 Brainspew 1: Kiths/Seemings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-17T20:35:16-07:00","id":232331,"title":"Changeling 2.0 Brainspew 1: Kiths/Seemings","content":"I'll start off this experiment with a brainspew, to show you where we're thinking.<br /> <br /> We're sort of reversing the roles of Kiths and Seemings. When making a character, you pick a Kith, then you refine it with a Seeming. So, for example, if you're playing a Draconic, you're Draconic first. Then, you look at the Seemings. You might be a Draconic Fairest, a Draconic Ogre, a Draconic Elemental, a Draconic Darkling, or a Draconic Beast... each with its own slight stylistic difference. We're talking the difference between a majestic gold dragon, and a creepy black dragon.<br /> <br /> 1) We will have a lot of Kiths. Not necessarily as many as all the 1e books combined, but that's a function of this model. Some old Kiths are kind of like facets of the same Kith now.<br /> <br /> 2) Kiths will get a lot of space. They each will actually only need a small amount of wordcount. Basically a few sentence description, a short paragraph advantage, and a little section describing the six variants.<br /> <br /> 3) In this model, Seemings will let you flavor your affinity for Contracts. Some Seemings will favor certain Contracts. Some will be unable to learn other Contracts.<br /> <br /> 4) This also lets us use Kiths as a method of minor, often implied social organization.<br /> <br /> 5) This means you can have a Motley full of a single Kith, each with a different aspect.<br /> <br /> 6) This frontloads some of the choice. We're okay with that though, since a) this is part of building the mythology of your Durance (a new foundation of focus), and b) in our experience, choosing Kiths tends to be a big part of character creation anyway.<br /> <br /> 7) We can balance out Kith advantages by making all of them a little more robust, since they're front-facing advantages. Kith advantages won't be &quot;you get 9-again on a dice pool you'll never roll&quot;. Yawn. They'll be &quot;you can do something that adds drama to the story.&quot;<br /> <br /> 8) In play, most of us found that players were more interested than their Kiths than their Seemings. I really like the idea of letting Seeming flavor your Kith, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> 9) If you haven't noticed, I like numbered lists.<br /> <br /> Consider yourself spewed.<br /> <br /> Again, I might not answer every question or address every concern. But I will read and consider all of them.<br /> <br /> I want to note the things I mentioned in my previous post, asking about the previews. Please take these into consideration. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts\"> Changeling: The Lost, Second Edition Previews Thoughts - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Excuse a little bluntness here. But I'm experimenting with how I'm going to Open Develop Changeling 2.0. So, right now I'm knee deep in work. I'm working on Forsaken 2e, Mage 2e, Requiem: Secrets of the Covenants, Beast: The Primordial, Promethean 2e, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand 2.0, Dark Ages V20, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":".  Added notes to help frame the conversation. 08-18-2014, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T20:47:37-07:00","id":232353,"title":"","content":"This sounds great. The funny thing is, while I'd thought like... the only Changeling I ever got to play was a Bright One, and the obvious thought is, how do you do that with a Darkling? I figured there was no way, but the answer came almost immediately... if Bright Ones as Fairest are beacons of beautiful light... then Darklings would hunger for the light to fill part of the void inside of them. Ogres would be perhaps light as a painful and terrible blinding thing... Elementals are obvious... Beasts would be phosphorescence. Wizened would be like... lamp carriers or such. Light as a tool.<br /> <br /> I want to know more, and I'll think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T20:48:29-07:00","id":232356,"title":"","content":"I'm loving the sound of all this. My Fairest Gristlegrinder likes the sound of this an awful lot. And stronger blessings? I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T20:54:46-07:00","id":232363,"title":"","content":"i) Are overarching seeming blessings and curses still a thing, or is each kith just getting a seeming-specific extra element?<br /> <br /> ii) How broad is the Contract lockout for seemings planned to be?<br /> <br /> iii) I feel like Beasts and Elementals are likely to be the most affected by the change to kiths-first, since those two seemings were most strongly defined/subdivided by their kiths (Wizened had almost as many corebook kiths, but had a more coherent core that the kiths mostly added a trade to). Swimmerskins and Waterborn seem like the easiest to map to the kith-primary approach, but things like Hunterhearts and Manikins seem a little more particular to their seemings, imagery-wise, than could be easily generalized or incorporated into a broader seeming-neutral kith. Forgetting &quot;every 1e book&quot; for a moment, are there likely to be fewer kiths in 2e's basic listing than were in the 1e corebook?<br /> <br /> iiia) If not, is this likely to owe more to preservation of existing kiths or generation of more wholesale-new general archetypes alongside merging conceptually-similar kiths from 1e?<br /> <br /> iiib) If so, how broadly can we expect kiths to work for different seemings?<br /> <br /> iv) Is multi-kithing or an analog still a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-17-2014, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T20:58:27-07:00","id":232368,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I really care about which comes first, but I think I like the core idea of separate Seeming and Kith. Once the two are separate, which one is &quot;core&quot; and which is &quot;refinement&quot; is largely irrelevant from anything but a presentation standpoint. I'd only say keep Seeming first Kith second because I don't see a reason to change it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I like some Contracts being locked away. Why? Some Contracts having more hoops to jump through? Cool (like Court Contracts). Flat out no? Seems iffy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:02:42-07:00","id":232371,"title":"","content":"By and large, this reflects a trend that the forums and personal play have revealed again and again. The 3-Dot Dual Kith Merit is enormously popular since it allowed Kiths to cross Seeming boundaries. It also brings to mind certain kiths like Shadowsoul and a few others that often seemed like they were trying to allow a Seeming to tap into other seeming's archetypes, so again, good points there.<br /> <br /> I had a concern(How do you handle kith archetypes that seem inherently inclined toward a particular seeming, even with the new batch?), but I answered it myself(players will do the rule of cool, be it optimization, miming, just throwing stuff together, so variety will still exist), so....yeah, I'd call it a solid choice. Instead of picking a Fireheart and feeling stuck within being the tower of fire or needing to buy Dual Kith, I can decide if I want to be a salamander or a phoenix(Beast), Balrog or Jack o' Latern scarecrow(Darkling), Seraph(Fairest), Djinn(Fairest or Ogre), Eldjotnar(Ogre), or imp(Wizened) as well as the man-shaped inferno(Elemental).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Gonna echo Satchel's first and second questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2014, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:05:56-07:00","id":232375,"title":"","content":"Hmm\u2026 nice. Obviously, some of the existing Kiths will need to be broadened in concept; in particular, the Beast and Elemental Kiths were conceived specifically with the Beast and Elemental Seeming in mind, and don\u2019t generalize as nicely as some of the others do. <br /> <br /> Or rather, I wouldn\u2019t mind seeing the Beast and Elemental Seemings (but not Kiths) go away, with \u201cI\u2019m a beast\u201d or \u201cI\u2019m an elemental\u201d being handled by choosing an animal-like or element-like Kith that\u2019s either a Fairest (the noble stag or lion), a Darkling (a rat or some other nocturnal creature), a Wizened (CtD\u2019s Pooka come to mind), or an Ogre (a bull or panther).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:09:20-07:00","id":232379,"title":"","content":"Eh, I wouldn't do away with Beast or Elemental seemings. It's easier to make a Ripperhand Kith that translates well into Beasts(Predatory animals ala Hunterheart) or Darklings(Razorhands), as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:10:13-07:00","id":232380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232363#post232363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i) Are overarching seeming blessings and curses still a thing, or is each kith just getting a seeming-specific extra element?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not settled on it. We haven't even really discussed it. I am leaning toward Seemings flavoring Contracts, but not providing overarching advantages and penalties. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232363#post232363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ii) How broad is the Contract lockout for seemings planned to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not settled on it. We're actually discussing it right now. I can't do a great job of explaining it unless I explain the whole Contract philosophy. That'll take me some time. But in short: <br /> <br /> Contracts will probably not be levels 1-5. They'll probably be individual powers, flavored by your Seeming. So like, Contract of Vainglory means something different to Fairest than it means to Ogres. <br /> <br /> My current pitch is that every Contract can be used by five Seemings. One Seeming favors it. One Seeming is barred (or distinctly limited like an inferior arcanum) from it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232363#post232363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">iii) I feel like Beasts and Elementals are likely to be the most affected by the change to kiths-first, since those two seemings were most strongly defined/subdivided by their kiths (Wizened had almost as many corebook kiths, but had a more coherent core that the kiths mostly added a trade to). Swimmerskins and Waterborn seem like the easiest to map to the kith-primary approach, but things like Hunterhearts and Manikins seem a little more particular to their seemings, imagery-wise, than could be easily generalized or incorporated into a broader seeming-neutral kith. Forgetting &quot;every 1e book&quot; for a moment, are there likely to be fewer kiths in 2e's basic listing than were in the 1e corebook?</div> </div> </div> </div>There should be more. I don't know which of my team is going to focus mostly on Kiths at this juncture. I need to find where their strengths are, and how much wordcount they need for a given Kith to really stand strong. But my goal is to have more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232363#post232363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">iiia) If not, is this likely to owe more to preservation of existing kiths or generation of more wholesale-new general archetypes alongside merging conceptually-similar kiths from 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to give a lot of space to Kiths. This isn't really a thing of not giving stuff away yet; but it's going to come down to the writer's own ability. If they want to merge a lot of old Kiths, I could see the virtue in it. If they want to just rehash as much as possible within our new paradigm, that's cool too. This is one of those places where I'm not going to give a lot of strong direction; I want the writer to do what feels best when they're sitting at their desk actually digesting content.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232363#post232363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">iiib) If so, how broadly can we expect kiths to work for different seemings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand this question. I THINK I do, but I'm not sure. I think most Kiths will fit well with all Seemings. If they don't, I could see not including one in a given Kith's potential. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232363#post232363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">iv) Is multi-kithing or an analog still a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be. It's not something we've went into at length yet. But it's something we'll talk about soon. I want a nice, compelling option if we go for one. Ironically, the Kith/Seeming switch eliminated a lot of the dual kith questions we've had going in. A lot of players looking to dual kith were really settled by choosing a different Seeming's flavor for an existing Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:11:07-07:00","id":232382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232353#post232353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds great. The funny thing is, while I'd thought like... the only Changeling I ever got to play was a Bright One, and the obvious thought is, how do you do that with a Darkling? I figured there was no way, but the answer came almost immediately... if Bright Ones as Fairest are beacons of beautiful light... then Darklings would hunger for the light to fill part of the void inside of them. Ogres would be perhaps light as a painful and terrible blinding thing... Elementals are obvious... Beasts would be phosphorescence. Wizened would be like... lamp carriers or such. Light as a tool.<br /> <br /> I want to know more, and I'll think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. This became a thing for me once I started considering Kiths. Most really sing with a few Seemings without even thinking about it at length. Once I looked over about twenty Kiths, it was a no-brainer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:14:25-07:00","id":232387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232375#post232375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm\u2026 nice. Obviously, some of the existing Kiths will need to be broadened in concept; in particular, the Beast and Elemental Kiths were conceived specifically with the Beast and Elemental Seeming in mind, and don\u2019t generalize as nicely as some of the others do.<br /> <br /> Or rather, I wouldn\u2019t mind seeing the Beast and Elemental Seemings (but not Kiths) go away, with \u201cI\u2019m a beast\u201d or \u201cI\u2019m an elemental\u201d being handled by choosing an animal-like or element-like Kith that\u2019s either a Fairest (the noble stag or lion), a Darkling (a rat or some other nocturnal creature), a Wizened (CtD\u2019s Pooka come to mind), or an Ogre (a bull or panther).</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast and Elemental are actually one of my big challenges conceptually right now. As I keep considering more and more content, I'm finding that the two overlap in a lot of ways. It's a case of something where I could merge them, I could change them, or I could just leave them the same. But just leaving them the same doesn't address the cognitive issues I'm hitting as I play at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:34:17-07:00","id":232399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232380#post232380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I understand this question. I THINK I do, but I'm not sure. I think most Kiths will fit well with all Seemings. If they don't, I could see not including one in a given Kith's potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question, for the sake of clarity, is essentially &quot;if 2e kiths are subject to some degree of collapsing from the 1e kiths (again using the aquatic kiths as an example) and this means a net reduction from the 39 kiths in 1e Core, are these liable to be concomitantly broader in terms of what the kith's thematic space is, with a hefty proportion of the kith's expression of a particular aesthetic/thematic coming from which seeming it's filtered through, as it did when people made characters with kiths from different seemings' lists in 1e's paradigm?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which you've pretty much answered satisfactorily; thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:44:04-07:00","id":232407,"title":"","content":"So is no seeming still a thing? What happens if you happen to be one will that get any mention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:46:31-07:00","id":232410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232368#post232368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I really care about which comes first, but I think I like the core idea of separate Seeming and Kith. Once the two are separate, which one is &quot;core&quot; and which is &quot;refinement&quot; is largely irrelevant from anything but a presentation standpoint. I'd only say keep Seeming first Kith second because I don't see a reason to change it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this idea, though it's interesting to think about since this sounds like one of the more radical changes, compared with how Vampire, Mage and Werewolf didn't change that sort of fundamental mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:51:27-07:00","id":232414,"title":"","content":"A minor thing; please give us a water-breathing kith with no bullshit around it. No &quot;drowning in air,&quot; no Glamour spend, no &quot;hold breath longer,&quot; just let us breathe underwater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:52:31-07:00","id":232415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232407#post232407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is no seeming still a thing? What happens if you happen to be one will that get any mention?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see why not. I guess you could just be straight-up Kith, with no Seeming flavor. Like the elemental essence of that Kith. Sure. <br /> <br /> I'll toss it by the team, see what they think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:54:48-07:00","id":232417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232414#post232414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A minor thing; please give us a water-breathing kith with no bullshit around it. No &quot;drowning in air,&quot; no Glamour spend, no &quot;hold breath longer,&quot; just let us breathe underwater.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will note this in the outline. I totally agree it should be a thing. <br /> <br /> Although, part of me thinks we should maybe have a couple of Kiths that freely water breathe, as a passing part of their Kith, not being their Kith advantage or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T22:08:09-07:00","id":232436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232415#post232415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't see why not. I guess you could just be straight-up Kith, with no Seeming flavor. Like the elemental essence of that Kith. Sure.<br /> <br /> I'll toss it by the team, see what they think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it was a merit that gave you neither. You got a clarity bonus for it but other than that it was basically an I wasn't physically changed by it. My character has it so I was wondering.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T22:10:32-07:00","id":232438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232414#post232414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A minor thing; please give us a water-breathing kith with no bullshit around it. No &quot;drowning in air,&quot; no Glamour spend, no &quot;hold breath longer,&quot; just let us breathe underwater.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that one actually bugged me. <br /> <br /> If Seeming is going to be more in the nature of association why is there so much concern about overlap? Yes, some Beast and Elemental Kiths seem especially exclusive, but they're hardly alone. On the Record: I LOVE the idea of emphasising Kiths over Seemings, especially because I happen to like playing some interesting Kiths, I don't see the point of removing some of the more idiosyncratic Kiths because some player will find a way to make a Brewer an Elemental. But, it does raise an interesting question that has come up in several of my games: Kithless. What happens if you get your kith stripped from you or aspects of your Kith? It works fairly well in 1e, but less so with this proposed model. <br /> <br /> Okay, I know this discussion isn't on contracts, but it's been a bugbear for me as a CtL ST for years, if the usual 5 tier system is going to be abandoned will there be ways to craft Custom Clauses for afinity contracts? I'm not going to lie, I often thought that Ogres and Darklings never got enough contract love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T22:29:09-07:00","id":232459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232387#post232387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast and Elemental are actually one of my big challenges conceptually right now. As I keep considering more and more content, I'm finding that the two overlap in a lot of ways. It's a case of something where I could merge them, I could change them, or I could just leave them the same. But just leaving them the same doesn't address the cognitive issues I'm hitting as I play at them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see the issue here, those are less coherent Seemings and more just collections of important Kiths. I mean, you play a Beast because you want to play a Cat character, or a Snake character, or whatever. You play an Elemental because you want to play a Water character, or a Fire character, or a Tree character. If kiths are detached from those and you can play your Cat character as a Fairest, your Fire character as a Wizened, or what have you - the whole thing gets turned on its head. Of course the big thing here is the Contracts. You want your associated [insert Animal] Contract, or your [insert Element] Contract... can those be tied to Kith instead of to Seeming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T22:42:01-07:00","id":232464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232459#post232459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can see the issue here, those are less coherent Seemings and more just collections of important Kiths. I mean, you play a Beast because you want to play a Cat character, or a Snake character, or whatever. You play an Elemental because you want to play a Water character, or a Fire character, or a Tree character. If kiths are detached from those and you can play your Cat character as a Fairest, your Fire character as a Wizened, or what have you - the whole thing gets turned on its head. Of course the big thing here is the Contracts. You want your associated [insert Animal] Contract, or your [insert Element] Contract... can those be tied to Kith instead of to Seeming?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they could be tied to a more &quot;nature&quot; Seeming without much trouble. And &quot;Be a Shark&quot; would be a function of a Kith, instead of a Beast Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T22:46:02-07:00","id":232465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232380#post232380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am leaning toward Seemings flavoring Contracts, but not providing overarching advantages and penalties.<br /> <br /> Contracts will probably not be levels 1-5. They'll probably be individual powers, flavored by your Seeming. So like, Contract of Vainglory means something different to Fairest than it means to Ogres.<br /> <br /> My current pitch is that every Contract can be used by five Seemings. One Seeming favors it. One Seeming is barred (or distinctly limited like an inferior arcanum) from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, but because it feels like an elephant in the room, I gotta ask:<br /> <br /> Compare and contrast this with Werewolf 2e's Gift system, where the Shadow Gifts are an essential theme and each Renown has its own take on that Gift?<br /> <br /> It's already not a direct copy (some Seemings are barred from the Contract), but it's a pretty obvious comparison to make. I think it'd be worth making sure Changeling does its own thing there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T22:51:15-07:00","id":232468,"title":"","content":"This is really appropriate move, I think. The concept of Kith being more important was always hanging out in the subtext (and sometimes the supertext) of the 1e books, and it's definitely how I've seen it played, so I'm glad to see it made explicit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">If for no other reason than I <i>always </i>mistakenly call them Kiths instead of Seemings...<br /> Despite <i>never </i>having played CtD...</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T22:59:50-07:00","id":232474,"title":"","content":"Would it reduce the Dissonance to change the two Seemings (beast and Elemental) Into something like Primal? A Primal Draconian could be a dragon made of moss just as likely as it is to be an idealized, and typical, Dragon out of a high fantasy novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T23:23:16-07:00","id":232490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232465#post232465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, but because it feels like an elephant in the room, I gotta ask:<br /> <br /> Compare and contrast this with Werewolf 2e's Gift system, where the Shadow Gifts are an essential theme and each Renown has its own take on that Gift?<br /> <br /> It's already not a direct copy (some Seemings are barred from the Contract), but it's a pretty obvious comparison to make. I think it'd be worth making sure Changeling does its own thing there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying, but 1)I think this actually emphasizes Seemings in a way that, while the Seeming Contracts did okay, really makes it a strong thematic element throughout the entire experience, and 2)Deals with some of the weirdness of differentiating the individual clauses from the total contracts.<br /> <br /> Plus, if we're honest, this sort of thing is popping up all over the place, in Demon with Embeds and Mage with path-colored Arcana Attainments. If it's a good idea, of course people are going to go for it everywhere.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, there's a good reason to keep the Beast and Elemental Seemings-while kiths can be colored without them, Contracts aren't so easy to shoo aside on the matter. A beast-y kith needs beast-y contracts. EDIT: A beast-y contract that doesn't run the risk of also being an elemental one, me thinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2014, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T23:44:48-07:00","id":232515,"title":"","content":"I never really thought about it; but now I do I realise I've had characters who've been defined by their Kith, but I've never played characters defined by their Seeming. So clearly this concept is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Do you have plans for a &quot;knight in shining amour&quot; and an &quot;innocent maiden&quot; kith? I always felt that those were two massive faerie tale archetypes missing from the cannon line up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings#post232331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) In this model, Seemings will let you flavor your affinity for Contracts. Some Seemings will favor certain Contracts. Some will be unable to learn other Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say this bit makes me nervous, especially the bit about lock-out. I can't comment knowledgeably until I know more about what you're intending, but I always liked the fact that in changeling you could play a living snowman with fire-magic.<br /> <br /> Kith and Seeming are a product of your durance. The ability to learn contracts that clash with a Kith felt, to me, symbolic of taking back control of your life and your body from your keeper. A Snowskin who learns Elements (fire) or a Darkling who learns Elements (sunlight) is making a powerful statement; or just really really needs to avoid being burned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232353#post232353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds great. The funny thing is, while I'd thought like... the only Changeling I ever got to play was a Bright One, and the obvious thought is, how do you do that with a Darkling? I figured there was no way, but the answer came almost immediately... if Bright Ones as Fairest are beacons of beautiful light</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how in cartoons when it's pitch black you can often see eyes? To me that's a Darkling Bright One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T00:24:35-07:00","id":232551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232474#post232474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it reduce the Dissonance to change the two Seemings (beast and Elemental) Into something like Primal? A Primal Draconian could be a dragon made of moss just as likely as it is to be an idealized, and typical, Dragon out of a high fantasy novel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it would. But frankly, I know there'll be a ton of pushback. <br /> <br /> I actually like that idea. It's pretty much what I'm debating pitching to the group for consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T00:40:17-07:00","id":232561,"title":"","content":"This will eliminate some people's reasons for dual-kithing. I'll be completely honest, if I could have built my Wizened Chatalaine/Telluric as a Telluric Wizened instead, she'd have ended up more in the place I wanted her when I began (not that I'm sad about where her story is, but.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T00:45:07-07:00","id":232565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232551#post232551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would. But frankly, I know there'll be a ton of pushback.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sure you're right; so let me say that personally I'm ok with the idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T00:47:44-07:00","id":232569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232551#post232551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think it would. But frankly, I know there'll be a ton of pushback.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also for it. The thing those share is the sense that you're not longer even a PERSON... which is more appropriate for a Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T00:53:33-07:00","id":232571,"title":"","content":"This is probably way too early for this at this point in dev, but one of the things I want addressed is Cold Iron and what it is. Partway through the line, there was a retcon that it was iron that had never been heated by human agency, which kept it appropriately rare, I suppose, but was weird on way too many levels. Just for starters, how do you actually make anything but a crude club out of that?<br /> <br /> For another, it was weird internally in the line, too -- the corebook had a vignette where a (later enchanted) human managed to grab a bit of wrought-iron fence that, from its effects, was implied to, through a stroke of luck have been Cold Iron. It's weirdly lucky even if Cold Iron is something more sensible, but when you can only get it from meteorites (Because you have to heat ore to extract usable iron) and any way humans actually work iron makes it no longer &quot;Cold&quot;, it's... yeah.<br /> <br /> I'll give my books a (re)read and see if I can think of anything else, but separating Kith and Seeming seems good, and fits my long-planned C:tL character (a clockwork dancing doll who, shaped by her Durance but also trying to reject the role her Keeper put on her, has gone heavily into mechanical engineering, clockwork, and kinetic sculpture) a bit better, since in everything except that Doll = Elemental, Fairest (possibly transferring to something appropriate under Wizened if she can manage it) seemed more appropriate for her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2836-nezumi","name":"Nezumi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:01:25-07:00","id":232575,"title":"","content":"This would definitely address the concern I voiced earlier. On a conceptual level, I heartily approve! The next question is what that would mean in terms of mechanics: I\u2019m assuming that your choice of Seeming still provides a strength and a weakness as well as favored and disfavored Contracts; if you merge Beast and Elemental into Primal, what would its strength and weakness look like? The contracts favored by Beasts and Elementals would be favored by Primal; what sorts of Contracts would be \u201cdisfavored\u201d? <br /> <br /> BTW, I\u2019m not too hot on the notion of shutting the door on Contracts due to your choice of Seeming; I\u2019d rather have something like <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Ruling/Common/Inferior setup, where Contracts that somehow conflict with your Seeming are more expensive or otherwise discouraged but not flat-out forbidden. <br /> <br /> Back to Beasts and Elementals: if for some reason you decide that reducing the number of Seemings from six to five is a bad idea, you might consider splitting the concept of Primal along some other dividing line besides Beast and Elemental \u2014 though I can\u2019t think of what that might be off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:06:53-07:00","id":232581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232575#post232575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would definitely address the concern I voiced earlier. On a conceptual level, I heartily approve! The next question is what that would mean in terms of mechanics: I\u2019m assuming that your choice of Seeming still provides a strength and a weakness as well as favored and disfavored Contracts; if you merge Beast and Elemental into Primal, what would its strength and weakness look like? The contracts favored by Beasts and Elementals would be favored by Primal; what sorts of Contracts would be \u201cdisfavored\u201d?<br /> <br /> BTW, I\u2019m not too hot on the notion of shutting the door on Contracts due to your choice of Seeming; I\u2019d rather have something like <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Ruling/Common/Inferior setup, where Contracts that somehow conflict with your Seeming are more expensive or otherwise discouraged but not flat-out forbidden.<br /> <br /> Back to Beasts and Elementals: if for some reason you decide that reducing the number of Seemings from six to five is a bad idea, you might consider splitting the concept of Primal along some other dividing line besides Beast and Elemental \u2014 though I can\u2019t think of what that might be off the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm leaning toward a more &quot;inferior arcanum&quot; route. Not sure. Honestly, the reason for the 'lockout' was that a lot of Contracts really don't seem intuitive to one Seeming. <br /> <br /> What I might do instead is only include five Seemings in a given Contract. But you can get like a one-point Merit that basically allows you to buy a Contract as if you were another Seeming. That'd prevent lockout, and act as a sort of 'cost increase' for non-affinity Contracts. It'd also let you just take another Seeming's effect for a given Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:07:51-07:00","id":232582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nezumi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232571#post232571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably way too early for this at this point in dev, but one of the things I want addressed is Cold Iron and what it is. Partway through the line, there was a retcon that it was iron that had never been heated by human agency, which kept it appropriately rare, I suppose, but was weird on way too many levels. Just for starters, how do you actually make anything but a crude club out of that?<br /> <br /> For another, it was weird internally in the line, too -- the corebook had a vignette where a (later enchanted) human managed to grab a bit of wrought-iron fence that, from its effects, was implied to, through a stroke of luck have been Cold Iron. It's weirdly lucky even if Cold Iron is something more sensible, but when you can only get it from meteorites (Because you have to heat ore to extract usable iron) and any way humans actually work iron makes it no longer &quot;Cold&quot;, it's... yeah.<br /> <br /> I'll give my books a (re)read and see if I can think of anything else, but separating Kith and Seeming seems good, and fits my long-planned C:tL character (a clockwork dancing doll who, shaped by her Durance but also trying to reject the role her Keeper put on her, has gone heavily into mechanical engineering, clockwork, and kinetic sculpture) a bit better, since in everything except that Doll = Elemental, Fairest (possibly transferring to something appropriate under Wizened if she can manage it) seemed more appropriate for her.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah... Totally not germane to the topic. But, if you want to start topics to talk about these things, I'll give them consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:10:42-07:00","id":232588,"title":"","content":"I would like to reiterate my support for this concept, so far. I'll give this topic a reread when it's not 2:00 AM and see if I can think of more useful stuff to add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2836-nezumi","name":"Nezumi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:11:26-07:00","id":232589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232387#post232387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast and Elemental are actually one of my big challenges conceptually right now. As I keep considering more and more content, I'm finding that the two overlap in a lot of ways. It's a case of something where I could merge them, I could change them, or I could just leave them the same. But just leaving them the same doesn't address the cognitive issues I'm hitting as I play at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>(A brainspew of my own half-formed idea.)<br /> <br /> Perhaps rather than Elemental/Beast the divide could be Inanimate/Animate. (I recall DA: Fae had something similar with the Inanimae. I need to go grab that book out of storage).<br /> <br /> The Inanimate embody the unliving concepts in Arcadia - the metal and stone of building blocks and gateways, the fire and light illuminating the cities, the clouds and wind gusts and the rains and flowing rivers.<br /> <br /> The Animate were formed the populations of living things - all the flowers, trees, birds and animals in the forests. The flesh-eating plants and the rabid attack-hounds guarding the Fae castles. The decorative birds in the cages. The thick-furred companions sleeping at their master's feet.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.<br /> <br /> Edit: Changelings making up those animate/inanimate objects that aren't just Gentry-constructs, in case that wasn't clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 08-18-2014, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:12:26-07:00","id":232591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232551#post232551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think it would. But frankly, I know there'll be a ton of pushback.<br /> <br /> I actually like that idea. It's pretty much what I'm debating pitching to the group for consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As long as there are still distinct [Element] and [Animal] Contracts as appropriate for the specific kiths/characters (so my Fireheart can invest in elemental flame powers, and my Windwing can invest in knowing the magic of birds, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:14:17-07:00","id":232593,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s the sort of thing I was thinking of: as long as the rules don\u2019t say \u201csorry; because the designers didn\u2019t see much reason to connect Seeming X to Contract Y, you can\u2019t either, even though you\u2019ve got this brilliant character concept that relies on it\u201d, I\u2019m happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:22:19-07:00","id":232596,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m also assuming that multiple Kiths is dead? Or can you still take a Merit that lets you combine two Kiths? I\u2019d personally lean toward the former, with advice on how to create your own Kith (including how to hybridize two existing Kiths) for someone who wants something in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:23:34-07:00","id":232598,"title":"","content":"Of course we don't know how Contracts are going to work yet - I know there was a fandom push at one point to just make Goblin Vows the default mechanics for a more freeform system that works of favor exchanges with the &quot;force&quot; you're dealing with, rather than spend fuel-stat for power a, b, c, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T03:50:58-07:00","id":232634,"title":"","content":"But David does; and I was riffing off of his comment in terms of my response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T04:13:06-07:00","id":232657,"title":"","content":"Oh, David -- you <i>must</i> let me talk Beasts with you sometime. They are my absolute favorite Seeming, and I think that they are quite distinct from Elementals (which are, in my mind, closer to the Wizened than the Beasts, but the Elementals have always been the hardest for me to grasp.)<br /> <br /> Find another author who loves Elementals (I know at least one of the authors does, I can't recall which one it is) and talk to them about it. If you can't wrap your head around them, find people who love them and figure out what they love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1403-dymphna","name":"Dymphna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T05:38:48-07:00","id":232723,"title":"","content":"Dymphna: at the risk of starting an argument, what is it that you love about the Beast Kith? In particular, what do you fear would be lost if it were to be merged alongside the Elemental Seeming into a Primal Seeming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T06:29:10-07:00","id":232784,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in this concept. Unlike some of the other posters, I have actually created characters far more defined by their Seeming than their Kith. That could be because I'm an Ogre fan, however. Ogres, whether they be Gristlegrinders, Bloodbrutes, Gargantuans, even a Witchtooth or what have you, all have a pretty strong Seeming theme to fall back on. They feel more united in their Seeming than Elementals, Beasts, or Wizened certainly. An Airtouched and a Fireheart or a Soldier and a Chatelaine might not share much common ground at first glance, but Ogres almost certainly do.<br /> <br /> I'm probably feeling a bit more wary towards the idea than many of those posting as a result, but I will try to push past that initial &quot;I don't like change&quot; feeling. The concept isn't inherently bad. There's no need for there to be a difference between my Ogre character being an Ogre Gristlegrinder or a Gristlegrinder Ogre. We'll see how the execution goes. Like some of the others, I'm a bit wary of the message being sent by certain Contracts being locked out by Seeming choice, given what Changeling generally stands for.<br /> <br /> What I'm really hoping for is that Contracts actually feel like agreements, pacts, and, well, contracts. I never agreed that the 1-5 dot rating system didn't suit Contracts. I felt perfectly normal for a list of clauses to be unlocked for a participant in the Contract. So I'll be keeping an eye on how that unfolds with great interest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nezumi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232571#post232571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably way too early for this at this point in dev, but one of the things I want addressed is Cold Iron and what it is. Partway through the line, there was a retcon that it was iron that had never been heated by human agency, which kept it appropriately rare, I suppose, but was weird on way too many levels. Just for starters, how do you actually make anything but a crude club out of that?<br /> <br /> For another, it was weird internally in the line, too -- the corebook had a vignette where a (later enchanted) human managed to grab a bit of wrought-iron fence that, from its effects, was implied to, through a stroke of luck have been Cold Iron. It's weirdly lucky even if Cold Iron is something more sensible, but when you can only get it from meteorites (Because you have to heat ore to extract usable iron) and any way humans actually work iron makes it no longer &quot;Cold&quot;, it's... yeah.<br /> <br /> I'll give my books a (re)read and see if I can think of anything else, but separating Kith and Seeming seems good, and fits my long-planned C:tL character (a clockwork dancing doll who, shaped by her Durance but also trying to reject the role her Keeper put on her, has gone heavily into mechanical engineering, clockwork, and kinetic sculpture) a bit better, since in everything except that Doll = Elemental, Fairest (possibly transferring to something appropriate under Wizened if she can manage it) seemed more appropriate for her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... don't actually remember this problem. Iron did cause a lot of confusion among our group when we started, and the names of the two different kinds were the issue. The big problem is that pure iron is referred to as &quot;cold&quot; iron. It goes through faerie defences, and it doesn't matter how exposed it's been to heat or magic. Hand-forged iron is the one you're talking about, and confusingly it is the type that actually has to be left cold and untouched by flame. It is consequently far more rare, and does aggravated to the True Fae.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Cold Iron can be heated. Hand-forged needs to be kept cold. One of the worst and most confusing choices of terminology, but I don't feel it needs much work as a concept beyond a new set of names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T06:32:34-07:00","id":232786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dymphna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232657#post232657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, David -- you <i>must</i> let me talk Beasts with you sometime. They are my absolute favorite Seeming, and I think that they are quite distinct from Elementals (which are, in my mind, closer to the Wizened than the Beasts, but the Elementals have always been the hardest for me to grasp.)<br /> <br /> Find another author who loves Elementals (I know at least one of the authors does, I can't recall which one it is) and talk to them about it. If you can't wrap your head around them, find people who love them and figure out what they love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I don't see any overlap among both of them. They represent very distinct concepts. One of them represent Changelings with animal affinties, and the other one Changelings with forces of nature affinities. I see more overlap among Beasts and Ogres, for instance.<br /> <br /> Although usually I don't like to add new factions to inborn splats (new Clans, Auspices, Paths, etc...), I remember long ago, someone posted in old forums a homemade Seeming that had a lot of sense to me: Mechanicals. Changelings wrapped in a way that now their body is made of artificial and mechanical parts. What do you think about icluding that one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T07:05:40-07:00","id":232799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232551#post232551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would. But frankly, I know there'll be a ton of pushback.<br /> <br /> I actually like that idea. It's pretty much what I'm debating pitching to the group for consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>The primary problem with merging Beasts and Elementals is that they aren't really alike, except for the kith-heavy tendency. In my experience, Beast characters are more prone to overlap with Fairest, Ogres, and Darklings, while Elementals are more their own thing.<br /> <br /> So, while I'm not averse to removing the Beast Seeming and freeing up animalistic designs to all Seemings, the proposed &quot;Primal&quot; Seeming strikes me as an unsatisfying model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T07:06:30-07:00","id":232800,"title":"","content":"Uxas: bear in mind that in this setup, a Runnerswift or Hunterheart has an \u201canimal affinity\u201d, regardless of which Seeming you choose to focus on. A Fairest Hunterheart might be like a lion; a Darkling Hunterheart might be some sort of nocturnal predator; and so on. Likewise, a Fireheart or Waterborn has an affinity with a force of nature \u2014 again, regardless of which Seeming it has. Likewise, the Beast and/or Elemental Seeming should be applicable to Kiths that are neither animal nor element: what would an Elemental Muse look like, or a Bestial Smith? If Beast and Elemental are to survive as separate Seemings, they need to be distinguishable from each other in some manner other than \u201canimals\u201d vs. \u201celements\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:05:21-07:00","id":232878,"title":"","content":"To add to what dataweaver is saying, any changeling can be animalistic looking with the old Beast Kiths. A hunterheart Beast brings nothing but redundancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:15:05-07:00","id":232886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232878#post232878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add to what dataweaver is saying, any changeling can be animalistic looking with the old Beast Kiths. A hunterheart Beast brings nothing but redundancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what's being said, and I'm gonna have to think on it(fortunately, I have a walk coming up), but on the short hand a Hunterheart Beast isn't actually doesn't strike me as that redundant. It seems to emphasize theme and motif to potency rather than rounding it out like the others do.<br /> <br /> Now of course, whether that emphasis is particularly fae or not is a big part of the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2014, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T10:57:40-07:00","id":233038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232581#post232581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm leaning toward a more &quot;inferior arcanum&quot; route. Not sure. Honestly, the reason for the 'lockout' was that a lot of Contracts really don't seem intuitive to one Seeming.<br /> <br /> What I might do instead is only include five Seemings in a given Contract. But you can get like a one-point Merit that basically allows you to buy a Contract as if you were another Seeming. That'd prevent lockout, and act as a sort of 'cost increase' for non-affinity Contracts. It'd also let you just take another Seeming's effect for a given Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of using a cheap merit to allow a kind of &quot;buy in&quot; to access things that normally would not be available. I think it keeps with the theme of changelings being able to make themselves something else from what their keepers made them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:07:10-07:00","id":233044,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that under the hypothetical Primal kith (I prefer Wild myself) a Wild Hunterheart would be the exact same thing as a Hunterheart beast. But they you have Darkling Hunterhearts (spooky preditory spiders? Serial killers?). Fariest Hunterhearts (Lion is king of the beasts? A noble foxhunter? the possibilities...)<br /> <br /> I think it could work. The counter-argument would be demonstrating a clear difference between an Elemental and a Beast Hunterheart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:07:51-07:00","id":233046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232723#post232723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dymphna: at the risk of starting an argument, what is it that you love about the Beast Kith? In particular, what do you fear would be lost if it were to be merged alongside the Elemental Seeming into a Primal Seeming?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Dymphna, but to add my thoughts on this:<br /> <br /> The Elemental Seeming, as it stands, has a strong focus on having a disconnect from humanity. By becoming so twisted into something not-living, your ability to interact with humanity (and animals for that matter) has been reduced.<br /> <br /> Merging them into one Seeming either means saddling Beasts with that disconnect, or losing that disconnect with Elementals. For example, a Water Kith-Elemental can be used to play up a changeling that's become so fluid and mercurial that they have trouble dealing with the traditions and habits of humans, while a Water Kith-Beast could be used for a sea-lion who's skewed social point of view allows for apparently normal socialization while the changeling is really acting on more primal instincts as a social animal. I don't see how Water Kith-Primal allows the same differentiation of themes.<br /> <br /> And, what's the better argument for, say, combining Elementals and Beasts vs. Beasts and Ogres? In my mind, Beasts and Ogres actually overlap far more in thematic space even if less in mechanics space. Most Ogres could easily be painted as simply being some of the larger or more brutish animals.<br /> <br /> The proposed refocused on Inanimate vs. Animate concepts works for me as a way to redo these Seemings in a fashion that addresses this concern while making their thematic space a bit more clearly delineated, but the names could stay the same and keep that. It's just a conceptual space to design around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:08:39-07:00","id":233049,"title":"","content":"They may not be redundant; and I\u2019m not so much trying to shoot down any argument that Beast and Elemental should both be kept as I\u2019m trying to challenge the advocates to go a little deeper. To reiterate my final point from my last post in that light: if Beast and Elemental are to survive as distinct Seemings (as opposed to being rolled together into one \u201cPrimal\u201d Seeming, or something of the sort), the distinction between them needs to be something other than \u201canimals\u201d vs. \u201celements\u201d \u2014 because \u201canimals\u201d vs. \u201celements\u201d is already covered by your choice of Kith. <br /> <br /> So, taking that as a challenge: if the distinction between Beast and Elemental isn\u2019t animal vs. element, <i>what is it?</i> What do Beast and Elemental bring to the table that isn\u2019t covered by the bestial and elemental Kiths, that can apply to Kiths that <i>aren\u2019t</i> bestial or elemental, and that are distinct from each other (the last being an argument against a combined \u201cPrimal\u201d Seeming)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:10:19-07:00","id":233051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232786#post232786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although usually I don't like to add new factions to inborn splats (new Clans, Auspices, Paths, etc...), I remember long ago, someone posted in old forums a homemade Seeming that had a lot of sense to me: Mechanicals. Changelings wrapped in a way that now their body is made of artificial and mechanical parts. What do you think about icluding that one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uxas, what about the Manikin, Metalflesh, and Levinquick kiths? Failing that there's the Inventor Kith from Victorian Changeling. I've had players use these kiths to depict all kinds of transhuman cyborgs.<br /> <br /> I mean, I too like the idea, but I feel it steps on the Elemental's toes. I always thought of the seemings as being the intent for a particular changeling. Beasts became animals and livestock,, Darklings were everything creepy and malign, Elementals became objects and scenery, Fairest were entertainment and aesthetics, Ogres were muscle and brutality, and Wizened were the people that got shit done. I agree that Kith is played up more, but if Kith was what you did in Arcadia Seeming is what your keeper needed when you were transformed. So, if a Keeper needed a furnace, you were gonna be turned into an Elemental.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:20:29-07:00","id":233060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233046#post233046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not Dymphna, but to add my thoughts on this:<br /> <br /> The Elemental Seeming, as it stands, has a strong focus on having a disconnect from humanity. By becoming so twisted into something not-living, your ability to interact with humanity (and animals for that matter) has been reduced.<br /> <br /> Merging them into one Seeming either means saddling Beasts with that disconnect, or losing that disconnect with Elementals. For example, a Water Kith-Elemental can be used to play up a changeling that's become so fluid and mercurial that they have trouble dealing with the traditions and habits of humans, while a Water Kith-Beast could be used for a sea-lion who's skewed social point of view allows for apparently normal socialization while the changeling is really acting on more primal instincts as a social animal. I don't see how Water Kith-Primal allows the same differentiation of themes.<br /> <br /> And, what's the better argument for, say, combining Elementals and Beasts vs. Beasts and Ogres? In my mind, Beasts and Ogres actually overlap far more in thematic space even if less in mechanics space. Most Ogres could easily be painted as simply being some of the larger or more brutish animals.<br /> <br /> The proposed refocused on Inanimate vs. Animate concepts works for me as a way to redo these Seemings in a fashion that addresses this concern while making their thematic space a bit more clearly delineated, but the names could stay the same and keep that. It's just a conceptual space to design around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than Animate vs. Inanimate I suggest Creature vs. Object.<br /> <br /> Beasts were animals, all kinds of animals, (which is why I never really got why tunnelgrub was darkling, but anyway) the thing about being a beast is that you were literally dumbed down to be more like an animal, you're operating on a much more instinctive level, and you have a connection to an entire species/genus. You officially became a &quot;critter&quot; your status as top-omnivore human was stripped from you by something to emphasize that it was the top of a more important food chain. Beasts are unto keepers as animals are unto us: the living things that we kind-of ignore.<br /> <br /> Elementals were scenery and objects: The fire that kept keeper and &quot;faithful hound&quot; warm, the river that carried the river barge, the poor fucker that got tied to the roof to be a lightening rod? The curse of an elemental has to do with the fact that they don't fully think of themselves as &quot;people&quot;. If you were the centerpiece of a rock garden you probably can empathise with a sculpture being torn apart. Poets personify objects, keepers objectify persons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1838,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","user":"danparadox","date":". 08-18-2014, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:24:06-07:00","id":233064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233044#post233044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The counter-argument would be demonstrating a clear difference between an Elemental and a Beast Hunterheart.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Elemental Hunterheart would be thematically focused on damaging weather events or dangerous environments. They tear through areas leaving destruction and damage like major natural disasters, or are regular but devastating events. Boreas, the Winter courtier who's icy winds rend flesh from bone. An earth elemental born of razor sharp obsidian who's very touch lacerates flesh.<br /> <br /> These are very different from a Beast Seeming to refine Hunterheart down to its most essential: the animals that hunt their prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:29:02-07:00","id":233069,"title":"","content":"That sounds more like an Elemental Render; it's so impersoanl. A Hunterheart, no matter the seeming, &quot;hunts&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:44:49-07:00","id":233088,"title":"","content":"One thing worth remembering is that we probably aren't getting the Kiths straight-the Aquatics are heavily implied to be squished as does the entire &quot;We have weapons for hands, be htey claws or knives or whatever&quot; thing, so the Render/Hunterheart thing is a little less significant a punch.<br /> <br /> Still meditating on Data's question, which I think pins the entire conversation's concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:55:32-07:00","id":233100,"title":"","content":"Minor deviation: Is Wyrd Evolution going to be a thing for Seemings in Huntsmen? It's a minor thing to think about in regards to this discussion, but still it is a thing to add onto the table.(Yes, I know it's 2nd Edition, but Huntsmen is easier to say)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:01:29-07:00","id":233109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233088#post233088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing worth remembering is that we probably aren't getting the Kiths straight-the Aquatics are heavily implied to be squished as does the entire .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure they are actually. If &quot;be a shark&quot; is a kith, it's probably different from &quot;be a mermaid&quot; - just like &quot;be a hunter&quot; is probablly different from &quot;be a destroyer&quot;. Still; until we have a concrete example or two, we just have to speculate as best we can.<br /> <br /> edit: Though there's a very high chance we'll only get one water kith and have to use the custom kith rules for others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-18-2014, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:10:59-07:00","id":233123,"title":"","content":"Either way, it's benefits us to remember that the old kiths are now stand-ins. Functional for discussion, but not lasting icons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:14:49-07:00","id":233127,"title":"","content":"If that means I can still say Hunterhearts are about hunting and not just having natural weapons, I agree completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:22:02-07:00","id":233137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233127#post233127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that means I can still say Hunterhearts are about hunting and not just having natural weapons, I agree completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can say it all you want, so long as you remember they might not be in Huntsmen(least not as Hunterhearts), and thus the weight of that particular argument falls down. EDIT: I mean, I can easily compound Hunterheart(hunter), Razorhand(killer), Draconic(conqueror), and Render(Destroyer) into one Kith and let Seeming do the distinction.<br /> <br /> Things are in a state of flux, try for arguments with lasting consequences, I suppose is the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2014, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:43:01-07:00","id":233156,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s also possible that the Waterborn/Swimmerskin distinction will be kept, with the former being a Kith representing fae who have an affinity with the element of water while the latter is a Kith representing animal-like fae who are at home in the water. As ArcaneArts pointed out, things are still in a state of flux; while Kiths are almost certainly being generalized for broader support of multiple Seemings, the specifics of how they\u2019re being generalized are still being hammered out.<br /> <br /> Elaborating on this a bit: there are only two places where I see the possibility of bestial Kiths and elemental Kiths overlapping, and thus leaving us with the predicament of \u201cis it a beast or an elemental?\u201d becoming vague if those two Seemings get combined: avians in the air and swimmers in the sea. No other animal kiths have such direct elemental parallels: nobody is going to mistake a Runnerswift for an elemental or a afireheart for a beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2014, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:51:02-07:00","id":233161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233137#post233137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can say it all you want, so long as you remember they might not be in Huntsmen(least not as Hunterhearts), and thus the weight of that particular argument falls down.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hunterhearts might not be in Changeling 2.0; but the question I asked: What is the difference between a Beast hunter and an Elemental hunter - that has lasting significance.<br /> <br /> A clear difference that creates two neat playable concepts is an argument for keeping both Beasts and Elements, the lack of such a difference... isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233137#post233137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I mean, I can easily compound Hunterheart(hunter), Razorhand(killer), Draconic(conqueror), and Render(Destroyer) into one Kith and let Seeming do the distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see where you're going with this (you can easily throw in Soldier too). However the one sort-of-example kith we have (&quot;you're a shark&quot;) is specific. &quot;You're a hunter&quot; seems closer to that in spirit than your line up.<br /> <br /> (Razorhands can totally be seen as hunters)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-18-2014, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:58:56-07:00","id":233163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233161#post233161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Razorhands can totally be seen as hunters)</div> </div> </div> </div>(That would be a thematic mis-representation of the Razorhand archetype)<br /> <br /> But we're picking nits now. I think I have what I want to say, just need to find Data's post to pin all the information down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:29:22-07:00","id":233188,"title":"","content":"I'm going to add my request for the &quot;don't fully bar anyone from a contract list&quot; discussion - part of the draw of Changeling for me is that there's so much variety in what you can learn, powers-wise, which can help add flavor to characters. Give them a higher purchase cost, if you wish, but don't completely bar them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:34:08-07:00","id":233191,"title":"","content":"This all sounds neat. I am still deciding how I feel about all of it.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of treating Contracts like Ruling/Common/Inferior Arcana and requiring a teacher for them.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Seeming vs. Kith our LARP it was understood that basically you can tell someone's Seeming...kith not necessarily. In the case of my character he was an Ogre but what kind? He was some kind of gladiator, pit fighter type. He is very handsome but scary looking with the pointed ears, brutal features and pointed teeth. Then he turns his face and you see he has a ruined eye...claw marks and scar tissue over his left eye. In this case he was Cyclopean...but figuring that out might not be so easy. In any case he was all about Ogre unity and had would say stuff like &quot;Where are my Ogres at?&quot;<br /> <br /> I am okay with change...just want to matter and mean something. I guess I had a different experiance of Kith vs. Seeming.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>CP<br /> &quot;Be yourself; everyone else is already taken.&quot;\u2014 Oscar Wilde","edited":{"userid":1145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1145-ariesomega","user":"AriesOmega","date":".  Didn't finish my though. 08-18-2014, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1145-ariesomega","name":"AriesOmega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:02:10-07:00","id":233209,"title":"","content":"Why not just have varying Contract costs, rather than a lockout or a Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:05:56-07:00","id":233212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232800#post232800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uxas: bear in mind that in this setup, a Runnerswift or Hunterheart has an \u201canimal affinity\u201d, regardless of which Seeming you choose to focus on. A Fairest Hunterheart might be like a lion; a Darkling Hunterheart might be some sort of nocturnal predator; and so on. Likewise, a Fireheart or Waterborn has an affinity with a force of nature \u2014 again, regardless of which Seeming it has. Likewise, the Beast and/or Elemental Seeming should be applicable to Kiths that are neither animal nor element: what would an Elemental Muse look like, or a Bestial Smith? If Beast and Elemental are to survive as separate Seemings, they need to be distinguishable from each other in some manner other than \u201canimals\u201d vs. \u201celements\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so for the purpose of this conversation, I'm going to lay out the issue as flatly as I can before I dig into it. I should mention that, starting this, I don't have a conclusion. I might have one once I reach the end of this.<br /> <br /> Are the Beast and Elemental evocative enough on their own to merit a Seeming, or should the twain become Primal(for lack of a better word)?<br /> <br /> And I'll be honest, that's a tough question. I've been spinning around in circles on that one in my head, reading the books and doing thought experiments, and I still don't have a clear answer.<br /> <br /> I think I want to approach this from two angles-what I inherently think of on the words Elemental, Beast, and Primal, versus what the books had to say on Elementals and Beasts and what Primal would mean in response to that.<br /> <br /> I'm doing it that way because when I think about it without reference, the case for Primal starts off with a disturbing amount of sense. As has been pointed out, both Elemental and Beast are seemings that seem more or less defined by the fact that they're grab bags for specific kiths, which makes the concept fall apart a little when you no longer have to be an Elemental to be a water fae or a Beast to be a Coyote-wannabe. Going from the the kithless angle, People can see what an Ogre is and what a Fairest is easy enough, a Darkling with a little work and the Wizened with some explanation. But most people( I don't my own personal results, as I'm unusual) won't come up with chimerical beasts or clashing acts of creation when you say Beast or Elemental. For Beasts you either get Beast from <i>Beauty and the Beast</i>(Who actually could be squared as kithless, I suppose) or the Big Bad Wolf or Aslan(Yes, I know he's a Keeper,shut up) or stuff like that. For Elementals, people will quickly think of a particular element-a human-shaped flame will probably dance into their mind first, or something like that. But that's not a seeming thing, that's a <i>kith</i> thing.<br /> <br /> And on a casual think, what does it mean to be a Beast or a Elemental? You, more so than others, are now made one with the world, it's just a matter of a permanence(well, more than that). That's easily compoundable.<br /> <br /> But on the opposite hand, doesn't that just make it even more vague and bland?<br /> <br /> Say what you will about Kith specificness, at least I can tell someone I'm playing a Beast or an Elemental and nothing else(save maybe Court), and people will at least have something in mind of what I'm talking about. There's an image in their head-fuzzily painted, sure, but they can picture it.<br /> <br /> What the flying fuck does Primal mean to the average joe? How do they even know what I mean?<br /> <br /> Naturally, the Kiths being frontloaded solve this issue a bit, but let's go with the two example I mentioned in an earlier post-let's assume there's a kith that is&quot;You are fae that has to do with water&quot;(We'll call it Aquatic) or &quot;You are physiologically designed for ripping things apart&quot;(We'll call it Ripperhand). Okay, so you're an Aquatic Primal. So, are you a mermaid or a water sprite? What about a Ripperhand Primal? Are you a honey badger or a razor-sharp hailstorm?As casual short hand goes, how does a ST begin planning for that?(And I've had times where I needed to start planning based on nothing but a Seeming, a Kith, and a Court for a PC). That's sort of thing works for Awakening's Thyrsus, but Thyrsus don't have to luck errant hairs out of their tails or shave their beards with hedge clips. I don't know why I brought up that last point, it was relevant earlier in the day.<br /> <br /> Without going into the books and just thinking on it, the problem comes from taking two broad grab bags and turning it into one grab bag. The two aren't strong enough to stand on their own, but together they don't stand any better. Are they easier to improve combined or on their own? I don't know. At least there's some definition with Beast and Elemental, but I don't think that's grounds for leaving them as is.<br /> <br /> I think the casual thought doesn't serve us immensely well here. I'm gonna turn to the books. What do they say are the hallmarks of the seemings?<br /> <br /> Beasts are marked by sensation and sensuality, by compressed time in the form of the eternal moment we call now, by instinct, the inherent sense of just knowing what to do, and the struggle with reason and with civilization.<br /> <br /> Elementals are marked by alienation(aren't they all?), by stretched time in the form of the fleeting eternity we call always, by harmony, the inherent sense of just being one with the world, and the struggle of empathy and human relation.<br /> <br /> Groot, by the way, is probably not actually an Elemental-that guy was human as hell, within the purview of this discussion.<br /> <br /> Okay, so what does this mean? Well, on their own, they are actually way different from each other. Of course, that conversation doesn't last too long long when we start stripping them apart. What can Darklings, Ogres, Fairest, and Wizened do that they can do also, and what's left?<br /> <br /> Beasts have a lot in common with Fairest at a glance, but in a different way given that they're moved by ecstasy rather than simple sensation-the end results look kind of similar though. The idea of sense and sensation also carries over to the Darklings, in a sense that the Darklings tend to see and hear more than most-no on pays spiders or shadows much attention, after all. the savagery of some Beasts durances can't be told apart from the brutality of Ogres a lot of the time, even though there is a reason they each get a different word(yes, there's a deliberate word choice there). The fact that a lot of Beasts are used as hunting hounds or wall-pulling oxen does not escape the Wizened's notice. And it's worth mentioning that Winter Masques touches on this very fact.<br /> <br /> By and large, it seems like Beasts aren't just beasts-a lion can be used to kill(Ogre), to impress(Fairest), to stalk(Darkling, to a certain extent), or even for labor(Wizened, and yes some African cultures used lions for labor). The only thing beasts are left with is the Wild Beasts, and even then the archetypes work against it.<br /> <br /> What about Elementals?<br /> <br /> They're a little harder to split apart, and that's because a lot of what they did was simply <i>be</i>. Which, funnily enough, is a point you <i>can</i> tie to Beasts, with their sense of compressed time-there's nothing beyond their senses, including their sense of self and now. They are what they are, and they act accordingly.<br /> <br /> Which, unfortunately for us advocates, makes a very strong and compelling case for the Primal seeming. They are the ancient fae of the world, the fae who say &quot;Thus as it has been, so it shall always be, and today is just a reflection between&quot;. They are the voice of the forest and the ocean and the sky. It's a pretty powerful and compelling idea, with fae who might be wild and active each day, but perhaps repetitive and caught in their cycles.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I can actually warm up to that idea. I like my distinctive seemings of Beasts and Elementals, but the Primal idea, after some thought, does seem like a neat child of both.<br /> <br /> So, conclusion.....Yeah, compound them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: But come up with a better name than Primal, because seriously, what the fuck are you even talking about when you say that to people who don't know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2014, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:21:21-07:00","id":233220,"title":"","content":"Well I think I agree with all of that; especially coming up with a better name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:22:20-07:00","id":233221,"title":"","content":"&quot;be a shark (or a fish or an octopus or seal&quot; is only different from &quot;be a mermaid or a selkie&quot; in the seeming-related flavor. If you've decided to &quot;be a shark&quot;, but as a Fairest, that would be like a fierce warrior mermaid with a shark tail and sharp teeth, really.<br /> <br /> I'm going to slide in with the &quot;Don't push Beast and Elemental into the same role&quot;, because, like Heavy Arms said (which is actually a pretty good answer to Dataweaver's question? So it seems like it got missed by some people, I think), Beasts and Elemental are operating on a much different difference than just &quot;animal&quot; versus &quot;human&quot; -- Elementals are practically <i>defined</i> by how they can't relate to normal people, or even sentient things anymore, while Beasts are defined by how much more alive they are than the people around them.<br /> <br /> The real problem, mechanically speaking, to me is that Beasts get a <i>bonus</i> to interacting with living creatures -- they get 8 again and a free specialty to interacting with animals, and can spend glamour to increase dice pools based around Presence and Composure. The only people who are better than Beasts at dealing with people are Fairest, and this is actually stated in the Beast write-up for Winter Masques.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Elementals are actually worse at dealing with people than Wizened are. They don't get the ten again on rolls involving Manipulation, Empathy, Expression, Persuasion OR Socialize unless it's to with the elements. People are talking about how the proposal for Hunterheart Elementals are too impersonal, and not <i>hunting</i> enough, and that's the thing about Elementals. They ARE impersonal. A hunterheart would be the blizzard no one could run from, sneaker waves from the ocean, lightning that doesn't need to strike twice because the first strike left it's target dead. The scary thing about it is that when it's on your scent, you can't shake it and you can't beat it, you just have to hope it get what it wants and you manage to survive.<br /> <br /> Leave the &quot;personal&quot; to the beasts -- Elementals just get the job done.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Woops~ I knew I should have finished reading through the thread before posting. Got too excited, but I'll probably edit further once I finish reading AA's post! ^w^;;<br /> <br /> Double Edit: Even after reading that, I still don't think I like conflating Beast and Elemental, but it does make a lot of sense. . . . I might have more to say later, though~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","user":"Murder-chan","date":". 08-18-2014, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:31:30-07:00","id":233250,"title":"","content":"If a better name gets suggested, fine. But really, does Primal require more explanation than Wizened?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2014, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:35:27-07:00","id":233255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233221#post233221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are talking about how the proposal for Hunterheart Elementals are too impersonal, and not <i>hunting</i> enough, and that's the thing about Elementals. They ARE impersonal.</div> </div> </div> </div> And that, I think, is an argument in favour of primal.<br /> <br /> All those impersonal concepts you talked about, they're great. But they're not the same Kith as the hunting wolf. Or lets say you have a &quot;lover&quot; kith; or a &quot;friend&quot; kith the Truefriend kith from Winter Masques.<br /> <br /> These Kiths are defined by how personal they are, so how do you come up with an Elemental varient for them? What's the impersonal friend, what's the impersonal lover, and what's the impersonal hunter?<br /> <br /> <br /> Now if you have a Primal Seeming, then there's something for both personal and impersonal kiths. A primal hunter is a wolf, a primal destroyer is a whirlwind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:40:09-07:00","id":233257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233250#post233250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a better name gets suggested, fine. But really, does Primal require more explanation than Wizened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Data, did you see the amount of work it got me to admit to myself Primal was good idea in the first place?<br /> <br /> <i>Why do you do this to meeeeeeeeeeee?</i><br /> <br /> That aside......<span style=\"font-size:8px\">no, probably not.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:49:45-07:00","id":233284,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t throw in the towel on separate Beast and Elemental Seemings quite yet, ArcaneArts. Murder-chan makes some interesting points, too. Can these distinctions between instinct and utter alienation she makes be reframed in a more general way that doesn\u2019t involve the animals-vs-elements distinctions that either are or aren\u2019t covered by the Kiths? <br /> <br /> Try this thought experiment: pick a Kith that\u2019s neither animal nor element: say, Muse. What would a Muse with a \u201cBeast\u201d Seeming (for lack of a better name) be like? What would a Muse with an \u201cElemental\u201d Seeming be like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2014, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:52:31-07:00","id":233288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233255#post233255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These Kiths are defined by how personal they are, so how do you come up with an Elemental varient for them? What's the impersonal friend, what's the impersonal lover, and what's the impersonal hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>The clockwork companion, the <i>yuki-onna</i>, the lightning bolt.<br /> <br /> Not that &quot;impersonal&quot; is a suitable descriptor for Elementals. &quot;Dissociative&quot; would be more accurate; they're strange and apart, with a certain alien element in their psychology (more so than other changelings), but they're still mostly human, and can love and feel as much as other changelings can. Just... differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:53:35-07:00","id":233290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233250#post233250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try this thought experiment: pick a Kith that\u2019s neither animal nor element: say, Muse. What would a Muse with a \u201cBeast\u201d Seeming (for lack of a better name) be like? What would a Muse with an \u201cElemental\u201d Seeming be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>The natural follow-up is &quot;What would a Muse with a &quot;Primal&quot; Seeming be like?&quot;<br /> <br /> TO which I say &quot;Shut up and let me get the things in my head figured out first&quot;. I just got the groundwork for the Primals down in the idea of the struggle of natural cycle, jeez.<br /> <br /> As for personal and impersonal aspects of the mix, don't get me wrong, I agree-but Beast by itself doesn't have much to stand on that isn't handled as well by other seemings.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I feel like I could write out the &quot;Why Primals felt their journey back was the hardest&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2014, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:53:58-07:00","id":233299,"title":"","content":"I don't really care if Elemental and Beast get folded into a single Seeming. I can see the merits of both approaches but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233255#post233255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These Kiths are defined by how personal they are, so how do you come up with an Elemental varient for them? What's the impersonal friend, what's the impersonal lover, and what's the impersonal hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Elementals are people turned into objects, not always natural objects. An Elemental Trueheart is a Teddy Bear that was beloved by it's Keeper. An Elemental Hunter is a human riffle, a metaphorical and literal weapon, systematically and methodically eliminating it's Keeper's enemies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:55:54-07:00","id":233301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233290#post233290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The natural follow-up is &amp;quot;What would a Muse with a &amp;quot;Primal&amp;quot; Seeming be like?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> TO which I say &amp;quot;Shut up and let me get the things in my head figured out first&amp;quot;. I just got the groundwork for the Primals down in the idea of the struggle of natural cycle, jeez.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hey, I\u2019m grasping around in the dark, too. My main goal here isn\u2019t to push any given solution, but rather to make sure that all angles have been considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2014, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:59:22-07:00","id":233307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233299#post233299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elementals are people turned into objects, not always natural objects. An Elemental Trueheart is a Teddy Bear that was beloved by it's Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is that to consider. That is an obscenely good argument..<br /> <br /> ...that I could still tie into the entire Primal point if the word Primal wasn't in the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:02:33-07:00","id":233313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233284#post233284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn\u2019t throw in the towel on separate Beast and Elemental Seemings quite yet, ArcaneArts. Murder-chan makes some interesting points, too. Can these distinctions between instinct and utter alienation he makes be reframed in a more general way that doesn\u2019t involve the animals-vs-elements distinctions that either are or aren\u2019t covered by the Kiths?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just noticed the first half of this post. And that's room for thought.<br /> <br /> The big thing is that I don't think Beasts can stand on their own. Elementals, though, particularly when you mix in that point Ravraxas made, have something going on.<br /> <br /> Poking poking poking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:04:05-07:00","id":233316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233250#post233250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Murder-chan makes some interesting points, too. Can these distinctions between instinct and utter alienation he makes be reframed in a more general way that doesn\u2019t involve the animals-vs-elements distinctions that either are or aren\u2019t covered by the Kiths? <br /> <br /> Try this thought experiment: pick a Kith that\u2019s neither animal nor element: say, Muse. What would a Muse with a \u201cBeast\u201d Seeming (for lack of a better name) be like? What would a Muse with an \u201cElemental\u201d Seeming be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a lady, actually, haha ^-^;;; As for beast and elemental seemings where you're not working with a kith that's specifically tied to either beast or elemental, that's actually a lot easier, I think. (And fun. I really like having Kith be what you decide first, and then filtering it through Seeming) -- A muse beast would be like a songbird, or Lassie or a creature who is put through a story to illustrate a concept, like in a majority of Aesop's Fables. The goat who teaches us to look before we leap, the dog who teaches us to be content with what we have. Stories, at their heart, are lessons, and so in a way, a muse is a teacher, more than anything else. Meanwhile, an Elemental Muse would basically be what Flamesiren was basically trying to be, someone who is at their core the hypnotic beauty of fire, or the stars or the mysterious allure of the moon. You know those pictures people take of waterfalls and rainbows and beaches where everything looks like magic is around the corner? Those would be Elemental Muses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that, I think, is an argument in favour of primal.<br /> <br /> All those impersonal concepts you talked about, they're great. But they're not the same Kith as the hunting wolf. Or lets say you have a &quot;lover&quot; kith; or a &quot;friend&quot; kith the Truefriend kith from Winter Masques.<br /> <br /> These Kiths are defined by how personal they are, so how do you come up with an Elemental varient for them? What's the impersonal friend, what's the impersonal lover, and what's the impersonal hunter?<br /> <br /> <br /> Now if you have a Primal Seeming, then there's something for both personal and impersonal kiths. A primal hunter is a wolf, a primal destroyer is a whirlwind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see how a fox hunt is particularly personal. The Truefriend through an Elemental filter is a guiding star, always leading the way but never particularly close, while an Elemental lover is the ice maiden who is beautiful and inspiring, but who's heart is frozen. There are stories built on lovers who desperately seek to thaw the hearts of their beloved -- The Snow Queen's Gerda and Kai for a more platonic variant, or the Princess with a Stone Heart for a romantic one.<br /> <br /> I think the greatest argument (and the only one that's swayed my opinion, to be honest), is that Beast has a lot of things in common with Fairest and Wizened and Ogres and Darklings, but nothing which sets them in particular apart from anyone else. They're a jack of all trades, but have no particular specialization.<br /> <br /> (Also, I don't like the name Primal, and would be a lot easier to convince if it were something more poetic, I must admit.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On a final note -- someone mentioned finding a way to make an Elemental Brewer. Wouldn't that basically just be an elemental who was made of alcohol?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:05:18-07:00","id":233318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233313#post233313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just noticed the first half of this post. And that's room for thought.<br /> <br /> The big thing is that I don't think Beasts can stand on their own. Elementals, though, particularly when you mix in that point Ravraxas made, have something going on.<br /> <br /> Poking poking poking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Exactly this. I'd rather have Beasts and Elementals be bundled together than lose Beasts at this point &gt;:<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233299#post233299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elementals are people turned into objects, not always natural objects. An Elemental Trueheart is a Teddy Bear that was beloved by it's Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, at this point, I don't know how many quotes the forum thinks I need from one person in a single post. . . . I've got like ten here. But that is adorable oh my gosh ;;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","user":"Murder-chan","date":". 08-18-2014, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:14:59-07:00","id":233327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233313#post233313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just noticed the first half of this post. And that's room for thought.<br /> <br /> The big thing is that I don't think Beasts can stand on their own. Elementals, though, particularly when you mix in that point Ravraxas made, have something going on.<br /> <br /> Poking poking poking.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if Elementals can still stand on their own, but Beasts can\u2019t (as written), how could the Beast notion be tweaked to still be something worthy of the \u201cBeast\u201d moniker and able to stand on its own beside the likes of Darkling, Fairest, Ogre, and Wizened? As it stands, sneaky animals can be folded into Darkling, social animals can be folded into Fairest, vicious animals can be folded into Ogre, and industrious animals can be folded into Wizened. What\u2019s left?<br /> <br /> EDIT: and what would Elemental animals be like? E.g., an Elemental Runnerswift?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2014, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:20:32-07:00","id":233329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233316#post233316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a final note -- someone mentioned finding a way to make an Elemental Brewer. Wouldn't that basically just be an elemental who was made of alcohol?</div> </div> </div> </div>Annnnnnd there's my next character, thanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> So we have the idea of Primals as the idea of the natural fae who struggle against a sense of purpose and place in the world and it's cycles and fight to determine their own path, but that leaves things like Teddy Bears and fae with that strong personal touch...that doesn't cross over into Fairest territory.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna go sit away from the computer, vania some castles, chew on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:22:32-07:00","id":233331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233327#post233327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if Elementals can still stand on their own, but Beasts can\u2019t (as written), how could the Beast notion be tweaked to still be something worthy of the \u201cBeast\u201d moniker and able to stand on its own beside the likes of Darkling, Fairest, Ogre, and Wizened? As it stands, sneaky animals can be folded into Darkling, social animals can be folded into Fairest, vicious animals can be folded into Ogre, and industrious animals can be folded into Wizened. What\u2019s left?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the question that defeated me. i'll chew on that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:26:18-07:00","id":233332,"title":"","content":"An Elemental Runnerswift would be Ponyta.<br /> <br /> Or, more seriously, a kelpie or hippocampus would be good options too. Moooostly the kelpie, as it actually runs, but. . .<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:26:23-07:00","id":233333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233316#post233316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see how a fox hunt is particularly personal.</div> </div> </div> </div> Look at it from the fox's point of view <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> more seriously. Because fox hunters care about the fox, they objectify it as &quot;huntable animal&quot; but they still care. Storms don't care at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233316#post233316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Truefriend through an Elemental filter is a guiding star, always leading the way but never particularly close, while an Elemental lover is the ice maiden who is beautiful and inspiring, but who's heart is frozen. There are stories built on lovers who desperately seek to thaw the hearts of their beloved -- The Snow Queen's Gerda and Kai for a more platonic variant, or the Princess with a Stone Heart for a romantic one.</div> </div> </div> </div> And this, Arc, is why I asked that question. Because the answers are damn good.<br /> <br /> The theme I'm getting here, is that Elementals are acted upon.<br /> <br /> An Elemental lover is loved, but doesn't love back (at least, not unless you unfreeze her heart). An elemental friend doesn't talk to you, you talk to it but you hear guidence echoing back.<br /> <br /> That's a pretty cool theme - even if I can't quite make it fit hunters. (I don't like the rifle idea; as it doesn't have any relationship with the hunted. The ice queen does, it's just one sided)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-18-2014, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:38:25-07:00","id":233340,"title":"","content":"My one qualm with Elementals as \u201cthings being acted on\u201d is that while it\u2019s a neat Storyteller Character idea, I could never see myself playing someone who is defined by passivity. Perhaps I\u2019m just misunderstanding the concept, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:40:38-07:00","id":233344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233333#post233333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I don't like the rifle idea; as it doesn't have any relationship with the hunted. The ice queen does, it's just one sided)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, like it or not hunting is mostly a one sided affair. Stalk prey, kill prey, eat/stuff prey, rise and repeat. Specially from the decadent and sophisticated point of view of the Lords of Faery.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, part of the point is that Elementals are <i>Tools </i>rather than simple natural objects. They are made how they are to fulfill a purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:44:13-07:00","id":233349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233340#post233340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one qualm with Elementals as \u201cthings being acted on\u201d is that while it\u2019s a neat Storyteller Character idea, I could never see myself playing someone who is defined by passivity. Perhaps I\u2019m just misunderstanding the concept, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>A very good point.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:44:19-07:00","id":233350,"title":"","content":"Beings that were passive in Arcadia are not necessarily passive in the mortal world. The player characters are those who rediscovered their activity and used it to escape. Now they embrace doing and acting upon other objects and beings, all while struggling against their innate, Fae-given passivity, and trying to balance their action on others so they don't fall into the trap of their True Fae masters and see everyone else as objects that must conform to their whims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:44:38-07:00","id":233351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233333#post233333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Look at it from the fox's point of view <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> more seriously. Because fox hunters care about the fox, they objectify it as &quot;huntable animal&quot; but they still care. Storms don't care at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the fox, they are the same: implacable, noisy, fearsome, deadly. The hunt &quot;cares&quot; only in that it is specifically out to get the fox, and that is hardly something <i>it</i> can relate to, or even understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:51:38-07:00","id":233358,"title":"","content":"The fox doesn't care if it's this hunt or the last or the next, or which huntsman is pursuing him. He just wants to go home. Likewise, a hunter doesn't care what fox she's chasing. She just wants to get together with her friends and have a merry time. Hunting parties aren't really about the hunt so much as they are another way for humans to socialize. Well, then again, I don't hunt.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I still like the prideful lightning bolt assassin who defines himself by one-shotting targets that physically more powerful comrades would need a proper brawl to lay down. He's great at work, but when he comes home, he doesn't know how to relate to the rest of his motley, or other courtiers, because he doesn't exist outside of that job. Maybe he was one of Zeus's lightning bolts in his durance.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;things being acted on&quot;, that would be the default state of an Elemental; that's what they were in Faerie. Now that they're back in the human world, they're going to figure out how to become more proactive. If you're playing a Truefriend or Romancer, you're probably going to have more social goals for your character anyway -- and heart wrenching arcs of people trying to figure out how to love and be loved are, again, a staple of stories everywhere.<br /> <br /> The icy maiden keeps seeking out fiery companions, hoping for some warmth, but can never really bring herself to get close enough to melt -- and if she did, would it destroy everything she ever was? The teddy bear is overshadowed by his closest friend -- but when his friend disappears, what is he supposed to do alone? And how is he supposed to find them again? How does the guiding star feel about her friend constantly straying from her advice?<br /> <br /> It's a slow journey to go from completely impersonal object to seeing oneself as human again, and getting back from one's durance is only the first step.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:53:18-07:00","id":233359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233340#post233340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one qualm with Elementals as \u201cthings being acted on\u201d is that while it\u2019s a neat Storyteller Character idea, I could never see myself playing someone who is defined by passivity. Perhaps I\u2019m just misunderstanding the concept, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that Elementals are Tools rather than merely objects. This one is the flame of a furnace, other a toy to give comfort, another is a weapon of war or for sport. In a way they are like Demons. They used to be things, impotent and not allowed an agency, but they are now escaped and can make their own decisions for the first time in ages. Will they strive to scape the purpose that was imposed upon them? Will they embrace it?<br /> <br /> To give an example: Will Mr.Pawns, the Teddy Bear, keep comforting children and people even after he has escaped from Arcadia or will he use that sense of harmlessness he gives away to exploit people becoming a ruthless criminal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:55:23-07:00","id":233364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dymphna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232657#post232657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, David -- you <i>must</i> let me talk Beasts with you sometime. They are my absolute favorite Seeming, and I think that they are quite distinct from Elementals (which are, in my mind, closer to the Wizened than the Beasts, but the Elementals have always been the hardest for me to grasp.)<br /> <br /> Find another author who loves Elementals (I know at least one of the authors does, I can't recall which one it is) and talk to them about it. If you can't wrap your head around them, find people who love them and figure out what they love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the differences, but I could also see enough overlap to want to merge them, too. For example, one of my favorite changeling concepts and one I hope to be able to do with 2E is a Spring phoenix: that is, a Windwing/Fireheart focused on healing and renewal. I never could quite decide whether to make her an Elemental foremost or a Beast, and usually ended up deciding on Elemental, I think.<br /> <br /> Other things, like a merfolk-esque changeling, might well be an Elemental <i>or </i>a Beast. Heck, it could be a Fairest, too. Which is where I think the idea of &quot;Kith refined by Seeming&quot; really shines like the scales on a fishy tail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:00:37-07:00","id":233366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233209#post233209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just have varying Contract costs, rather than a lockout or a Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because increased costs only ever matter once, and never in a one-shot game. They don't actually do anything to the story. Straight-up XP taxes are boring unless they do something else.<br /> <br /> With the Merit idea, you're getting a cross-Seeming Contract. So if you're (hypothetically) not able to get Strength as a Wizened, buying it as an Ogre means something interesting for your story. <br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:14:11-07:00","id":233375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233340#post233340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one qualm with Elementals as \u201cthings being acted on\u201d is that while it\u2019s a neat Storyteller Character idea, I could never see myself playing someone who is defined by passivity. Perhaps I\u2019m just misunderstanding the concept, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe passivity is the wrong way to go about it. It's not that they're passive, they're just not active toward the same things, and the effect they have on others just flows out from who and what they are. Take the Elemental Muse as shooting star example from earlier (because I love that one). That Elemental inspires other characters, but not from actively trying to inspire them, just from going about whatever she goes about in a manner that is very natural to her. It's just what she does. Perhaps an Elemental Seeming would tend to give a spin on a Kith related to just observing or being near the Changeling, without needing direct action on her part...? I dunno. May not be wise to generalize to that degree.<br /> <br /> For the record, I want to keep the Beast / Elemental split at present -- well, if I'm honest, I mostly want to keep some representation particular to Beasts. I'm still rolling things around, though, and I can see some persuasive bits to it. I'm hopeful I'll find a justification or rationale that satisfies me, whichever way that is. For now, they just feel too distinct to me to be happy about one category for both, even if I find trouble articulating the why of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:17:15-07:00","id":233377,"title":"","content":"So, a thing to consider. <br /> <br /> We're discussing Seemings as coming out of your escape. The method of escape stains what you were, what role you played in your Durance. That's mostly just to add a little more flavor on the splat intersection, since we're going to front-load the Durance a little bit. <br /> <br /> Also, regarding the two Kiths, here's a weird thing that comes up in a lot of games. &quot;Naturalist&quot; character archetypes don't occur much in my games, because we tend toward heavily urban games. They certainly exist, but they're not a large percentage of the character base. When I'm in a Vampire game, I see few Gangrel, and even then, heavily urban concepts. Ventrue almost never take Animalism. When I play Werewolf, I see a disproportionate number of Iron Masters. Not that Elementals or Beasts are either anti-urban, per se. But their Kiths trend heavily toward character types who are. With both Elementals and Beasts, when I see them, their concepts both swing heavily toward rejection of the highly civilized. <br /> <br /> Again, my personal experiences here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:38:09-07:00","id":233414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233377#post233377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a thing to consider.<br /> <br /> We're discussing Seemings as coming out of your escape. The method of escape stains what you were, what role you played in your Durance. That's mostly just to add a little more flavor on the splat intersection, since we're going to front-load the Durance a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry of this comes off as thick, but could you clarify what you mean by &quot;front-load the Durance?&quot; For whatever reason, something just isn't clicking with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, regarding the two Kiths, here's a weird thing that comes up in a lot of games. &quot;Naturalist&quot; character archetypes don't occur much in my games, because we tend toward heavily urban games. They certainly exist, but they're not a large percentage of the character base. When I'm in a Vampire game, I see few Gangrel, and even then, heavily urban concepts. Ventrue almost never take Animalism. When I play Werewolf, I see a disproportionate number of Iron Masters. Not that Elementals or Beasts are either anti-urban, per se. But their Kiths trend heavily toward character types who are. With both Elementals and Beasts, when I see them, their concepts both swing heavily toward rejection of the highly civilized.<br /> <br /> Again, my personal experiences here. </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting take to hear. I don't know. When I think of Elementals and Beasts, I usually think more of how inanimate things or natural forces and animals have been made useful to the Gentry. Sometimes that's just turning someone into predator or prey, natural disaster or set piece and letting them go because that suits the Fey's sensibilities. But, and perhaps this is just me, I usually think more about a lady with her beasts of burden for hauling, hounds for hunting, fires for her forges, or waterfall for her inspiration, sculpted to turn something of the natural world toward some end of civilization, even if it's a fantastic and/or pointless parody. Not... altogether sure where I'm going with this, but &quot;rejection of civilization&quot; doesn't quite hit it for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:48:11-07:00","id":233430,"title":"","content":"This is a fair point: in Arcadia, where everything is subject to the Gentry\u2019s whims, is <i>anything</i> truly a rejection of \u201ccivilization\u201d (at least as conceived by the Gentry)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:49:06-07:00","id":233432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233377#post233377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a thing to consider.<br /> <br /> We're discussing Seemings as coming out of your escape. The method of escape stains what you were, what role you played in your Durance. That's mostly just to add a little more flavor on the splat intersection, since we're going to front-load the Durance a little bit.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding the two Kiths, here's a weird thing that comes up in a lot of games. &quot;Naturalist&quot; character archetypes don't occur much in my games, because we tend toward heavily urban games. They certainly exist, but they're not a large percentage of the character base. When I'm in a Vampire game, I see few Gangrel, and even then, heavily urban concepts. Ventrue almost never take Animalism. When I play Werewolf, I see a disproportionate number of Iron Masters. Not that Elementals or Beasts are either anti-urban, per se. But their Kiths trend heavily toward character types who are. With both Elementals and Beasts, when I see them, their concepts both swing heavily toward rejection of the highly civilized.<br /> <br /> Again, my personal experiences here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like Gaius above I've never got the impression of rejection of civilization, at least with Elementals. After all if it's about turning people into things then it's more about what is that thing going to be used for than what that thing is. For me it never was about having a person who was a wildfire, but a person who was turned into the flame of a lamp, it was never about someone turned into a lightning-bolt, but about someone who was used as a source of power for strange and alien machinery. It was less about what he had been turned into and more about why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:55:05-07:00","id":233441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233340#post233340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one qualm with Elementals as \u201cthings being acted on\u201d is that while it\u2019s a neat Storyteller Character idea, I could never see myself playing someone who is defined by passivity. Perhaps I\u2019m just misunderstanding the concept, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, perhaps the conflict there is essentially getting people to view you as more than that. After all, isn't some of recovering from your Durance trying to find an identity outside out of your Kith/Seeming? Well, that could be a huge thing here.<br /> <br /> And actually, if building a mythology around your Durance is a thing, as I think the OP said, then this conflict would matter a lot more. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":".  Tiny expansion. 08-18-2014, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:59:09-07:00","id":233446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233414#post233414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry of this comes off as thick, but could you clarify what you mean by &quot;front-load the Durance?&quot; For whatever reason, something just isn't clicking with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm sorry. In the second edition material, we're adding some angles to character creation that key character elements to aspects of the story. So like in Werewolf, pack creation is right there in the character creation section. In Vampire, you have to come up with Touchstones. <br /> <br /> As part of character creation, we're going to hit on a few things that occurred within the Durance, and key them to character traits. You could just sit down and punch out a character sheet. But we want to offer a functional way to tell a short story of the Durance, and come out with most of your character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:01:29-07:00","id":233469,"title":"","content":"So Kith is what they did to you, and Seeming is how you escaped?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:06:59-07:00","id":233481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233430#post233430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a fair point: in Arcadia, where everything is subject to the Gentry\u2019s whims, is <i>anything</i> truly a rejection of \u201ccivilization\u201d (at least as conceived by the Gentry)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The play's the thing. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking about how things are reflected in the immediacy of play. The Gentry's whims only go so far with that. Day-to-day, they barely matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:09:06-07:00","id":233486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233469#post233469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Kith is what they did to you, and Seeming is how you escaped?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically, yeah. Kith is the role you played in their myth. Seeming is how you broke it. Kith is your Arcadian side. Your flesh is your Earthly side. Seeming is the bridge between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:09:29-07:00","id":233487,"title":"","content":"But, to comment on the whole Beast thing, I think a key difference between Beasts and Fairest may be one of how personal each is. <br /> <br /> To put it another way, Fairest are defined by being perfect, sort of, but in a sense, unreachable. Their beauty is unnatural, and they're also separated from humanity by other stuff(consider in the original they're the ones that have a Clarity penalty for a reason.) <br /> <br /> By contrast, Beasts are approachable, and can be connected with. Sure, they were reduced to being instinctual, and have connections to animals most people wouldn't get. However, they aren't unnatural. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <br /> For Beasts and Ogres, there are more issues. Ogres do have the origin dealing with violence shaping them, however that's a hair splitty thing when compared to beasts. One way to differ this though, using the example of Hunterheart(which may not appear), is this.<br /> <br /> A beast hunter heart represents the animal that kills you because it needs food, not because it hates you, or wants to kill you for sport. By comparison, the Ogre Hunterheart hunts you because its fun, and or they want to make a point out of hunting you down. One represents the uncaring aspect of nature, (yes, that brings them to elementals, but there's ways around that), while the other is, depending, either representing the abuses of society, or a bully who pretends to have an honor code. <br /> <br /> To differ the Beast here from how Elements have lost connection with humanity, again, Elementals are more representations of objects. By contrast, Beasts are representations of natural creatures, and how they act. Well, does a wolf care, other than how you threaten it, or whether its hungry? In this case, its primal needs versus being an object. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:12:54-07:00","id":233488,"title":"","content":"One of the things I like the most from Changeling: The Lost 1st edition was it Seeming/Kith system, it works so well. I don't understand why change it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But well, after saying this, if your Seeming depends in how you scape from Arcadia and Kith in what you suffered during your Durance, the Changeling system is changing a lot. This way I suppose all Seemings will change because with this new perspective the old Seemings have no sense at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/n6g3njp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/kpa5GS5Mp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/93820aaad7.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/584-eliseo-ap-liam","name":"Eliseo ap Liam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:17:35-07:00","id":233492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233486#post233486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Basically, yeah. Kith is the role you played in their myth. Seeming is how you broke it. Kith is your Arcadian side. Your flesh is your Earthly side. Seeming is the bridge between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh... <br /> <br /> That changes my thoughts quite a bit with Beasts, as there's quite a few more ways to define them here as their own Seeming, same goes for Elementals and Ogres, in this new setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:19:26-07:00","id":233494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233486#post233486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Basically, yeah. Kith is the role you played in their myth. Seeming is how you broke it. Kith is your Arcadian side. Your flesh is your Earthly side. Seeming is the bridge between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>This completely changes the entire angle of attack for the Seeming discussion.<br /> <br /> Today's a day for long, hard thinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:23:28-07:00","id":233495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233494#post233494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This completely changes the entire angle of attack for the Seeming discussion.<br /> <br /> Today's a day for long, hard thinks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, although I think the aspects of Elemental discussion may work here. <br /> <br /> Also, for Beasts, perhaps it represents you breaking free, by in a sense becoming a wild animal? Abandoning yourself to nature, if you will, as a theme could certainly help differ Beasts from other Seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:29:19-07:00","id":233500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233494#post233494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This completely changes the entire angle of attack for the Seeming discussion.<br /> <br /> Today's a day for long, hard thinks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is going to happen more than a few times, I suspect. As we build context, parts are going to hit a little dissonance here and there. Perspectives might shift. <br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of other bigger shifts we're considering. I don't think there are a lot of them. I know we're approaching Courts differently (more that we're presenting no Court system as an inherent default, so we can give more attention to cool examples like the way we did cities in Vampire 2.0 and we can add nifty tools for crafting your own to fit your chronicle).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:39:35-07:00","id":233506,"title":"","content":"Okay, having thought a little, let me analyze a kith from the original, Earthbones, and see what you guys think of how i try to interpret it here. Now, this may not even make it again, so I'm just using the Kith to demonstrate a point. Obviously, tell me if I'm grossly wrong from how development has changed things here.<br /> <br /> To begin, lets take a Elemental Earthbones here. Well, that you could mean in Arcadia... you were literally rock that made up a larger structure. Part of coming back, to show Elemental as a linking element, was that you embraced part of that, i.e. accepting that you come from a building essentially, but also sought an identity greater than that. The impersonal aspect of this, assuming this stays part of being an Elemental, is that much of how you define yourself is still tied to being an object, however an object of great importance. You would never look at see, monuments the same way again, because you know what it is like to literally be a part of one. Notice I'm not putting a nature theme here, because I'd argue Elemental, which perhaps may change to something else like Inanimates perhaps, are going to be more represented by being objects than being natural, if they were to stay an independent Seeming. Maybe. Speculation of course.<br /> <br /> If you're a Beast Earthbones, this could mean you were essentially the equivalent of some burrowing animal, trained to do the equivalent of digging up treasure or similar for your Keeper. When you broke free, part of that meant essentially becoming a wild animal, linking yourself back to the human world by being someone outside of your Keeper's, or anyone for that matter to some extent, control. <br /> <br /> Those are the two I got. Thoughts? Does this meet with how Durance is going? Hope this helps somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:40:32-07:00","id":233508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233500#post233500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is going to happen more than a few times, I suspect. As we build context, parts are going to hit a little dissonance here and there. Perspectives might shift.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of other bigger shifts we're considering. I don't think there are a lot of them. I know we're approaching Courts differently (more that we're presenting no Court system as an inherent default, so we can give more attention to cool examples like the way we did cities in Vampire 2.0 and we can add nifty tools for crafting your own to fit your chronicle).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Court thing should be interesting, but doesn't sound quite as major. I mean, the Durance thing completely changes how basic character creation works, where as here... the Court change doesn't do it quite as much. I think. Feel free to correct me guys, but I'm just judging by appearance here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:44:14-07:00","id":233513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233500#post233500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is going to happen more than a few times, I suspect. As we build context, parts are going to hit a little dissonance here and there. Perspectives might shift.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of other bigger shifts we're considering. I don't think there are a lot of them. I know we're approaching Courts differently (more that we're presenting no Court system as an inherent default, so we can give more attention to cool examples like the way we did cities in Vampire 2.0 and we can add nifty tools for crafting your own to fit your chronicle).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no, I realize. I had forgotten the discussions from the days I was working with people designing a Sonic RPG site, and this has brought it all back.<br /> <br /> That said, The role of Seeming deals with one big issue I've had with the Changeing's X-splat-the wibbliness of Seeming and Kith origins. Before it was that the True Fae had to work with what they got but were pretty creative, so trying to figure out if a seeming or a kith came from you or them was this entire indistinct affair. Now it's clear-Kith's the Stranger's contribution, Seeming is yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2014, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:53:53-07:00","id":233522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233508#post233508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Court thing should be interesting, but doesn't sound quite as major. I mean, the Durance thing completely changes how basic character creation works, where as here... the Court change doesn't do it quite as much. I think. Feel free to correct me guys, but I'm just judging by appearance here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It means there's no default assumption of mantles and courts. Which may or may not be a big deal in your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:56:09-07:00","id":233525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233522#post233522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It means there's no default assumption of mantles and courts. Which may or may not be a big deal in your games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. That does indeed change things just... not as much as the whole re-defining Seemings and Kiths does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:57:53-07:00","id":233526,"title":"","content":"Question: Original kiths were pretty archetypal, of course, but does this mean that the Fatebound Merits and the idea of fate...I forget Dancer's word for it, but Roles now concepts baked into Kiths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:00:21-07:00","id":233529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233526#post233526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Original kiths were pretty archetypal, of course, but does this mean that the Fatebound Merits and the idea of fate...I forget Dancer's word for it, but Roles now concepts baked into Kiths?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can kind of see the distinction, but I don't think it's as concrete as it could be. One of my writers said she has some ideas about Fatebound stuff. It's not something we've discussed yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:01:49-07:00","id":233532,"title":"","content":"Oh, and let me put it this way. <br /> <br /> Kith is what happened to you. Seeming is your agency. It represents the moment you took control away from your victimizer. <br /> <br /> Lost is a game about survivors. Seeming is one of a few ways we really emphasize the characters' agency and human spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:04:17-07:00","id":233537,"title":"","content":"OH! Okay, that just eradicated, aspects at least, of the discussion on Elementals and Beasts, along with whether they should be combined or anything. <br /> <br /> Heck, how any of the Seemings work has just completely changed here, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:06:36-07:00","id":233543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233537#post233537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OH! Okay, that just eradicated, aspects at least, of the discussion on Elementals and Beasts, along with whether they should be combined or anything.<br /> <br /> Heck, how any of the Seemings work has just completely changed here, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why I said it was going to need a long hard think-because now I need to understand how each of the Seemings reflects agency, which is a subject not really tackled before by Changeling.<br /> <br /> It's fucking genius, actually, but not discussed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:07:40-07:00","id":233546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233525#post233525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, okay. That does indeed change things just... not as much as the whole re-defining Seemings and Kiths does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah. I'm just trying to think of any other sweeping stuff to bring it up right away. <br /> <br /> There's a conceptual change to what Courts mean. But that'll require a post and thread of its own to really explain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:08:25-07:00","id":233547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233526#post233526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">fate...I forget Dancer's word for it, but Roles</div> </div> </div> </div>Personas, if I'm not mistaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:11:41-07:00","id":233551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233547#post233547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personas, if I'm not mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>PERSONAS! That's it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:17:16-07:00","id":233553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233543#post233543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's why I said it was going to need a long hard think-because now I need to understand how each of the Seemings reflects agency, which is a subject not really tackled before by Changeling.<br /> <br /> It's fucking genius, actually, but not discussed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, especially as I'm not sure certain Seemings would even survive with the same name here. <br /> <br /> But hmm. Well, my idea with Beast sort of works, I think(essentially, you become a wild animal to break free of being someone's pet, if you will), but I have NO idea how Elemental could be Agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:19:10-07:00","id":233557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233553#post233553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, especially as I'm not sure certain Seemings would even survive with the same name here.<br /> <br /> But hmm. Well, my idea with Beast sort of works, I think(essentially, you become a wild animal to break free of being someone's pet, if you will), but I have NO idea how Elemental could be Agency.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Appeal to the outside world. Appeal to the environment. Did you burn your Keeper's mansion? Did you trap his hounds in a rockslide during your escape? Did you set a trap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:26:55-07:00","id":233565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233553#post233553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have NO idea how Elemental could be Agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first instinct was that you faded into the background so that your Keeper didn't notice when you were gone.<br /> <br /> The more interesting question to me is how the Fairest works with Agency, since those are almost antithetical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:37:30-07:00","id":233571,"title":"","content":"For Fairest as Agency, I think the most obvious answer is emotional manipulation. Did you convince a drudge to let you out the back for a kiss? Turn your Keeper's allies against them? Trade a lock of hair for the key to your shackles? Sally from Nightmare Before Christmas escaped repeatedly by drugging her &quot;creator&quot;, and convincing him to trust her cooking the next time she did something suspicious. That could be very Fairest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:37:55-07:00","id":233573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233546#post233546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh yeah. I'm just trying to think of any other sweeping stuff to bring it up right away. <br /> <br /> There's a conceptual change to what Courts mean. But that'll require a post and thread of its own to really explain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that any major change you make will require its own brainspew to really explain. I also expect that several of the game\u2019s numerous magic systems (Contracts, Pledges, Oneiromancy, Talecraft?, etc.) will undergo substantial revision; but as noted above, they\u2019re probably best addressed in their own topics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:38:16-07:00","id":233575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233557#post233557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Appeal to the outside world. Appeal to the environment. Did you burn your Keeper's mansion? Did you trap his hounds in a rockslide during your escape? Did you set a trap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Good points.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Beast ties to the animal while Element ties to the more physical environment, which is returning to the older distinction, but it now works better...<br /> <br /> I'm happy.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:40:45-07:00","id":233578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233565#post233565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more interesting question to me is how the Fairest works with Agency, since those are almost antithetical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially as Fairest represented also the Changelings at the most risk of becoming like their Keepers, or at least, that was how the book presented it. <br /> <br /> Perhaps here you become like your Keeper to escape said Keeper? Could also involve some sort of social dueling, if you will, with said Keeper, by using their customs against them. <br /> <br /> Just speculating, but honestly, the clarification really makes Seemings new all over again(in a good way), because of needing to think about them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:42:36-07:00","id":233579,"title":"","content":"Seeming as Agency also means that Seeming is less likely to impact your character\u2019s appearance. It\u2019s not impossible, mind you \u2014 your means of gaining agency may have involved seizing control over the physical transformations you were undergoing \u2014 but more likely than not, your physical appearance is determined almost entirely by your Kith, and your Seeming is almost entirely mental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:48:08-07:00","id":233591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233565#post233565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first instinct was that you faded into the background so that your Keeper didn't notice when you were gone.<br /> <br /> The more interesting question to me is how the Fairest works with Agency, since those are almost antithetical.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a great quote from Fate/Zero delivered by Tohsaka that basically embodies how the Fairest would embody Agency, at least on the positive front. I'll find it later.<br /> <br /> Given that the person saying this also gave his second daughter to a psychopath so she could continue the magic line instead of being left out and felt proud at the idea of his two daughters fighting for the root of magic, it might also be a commentary on the negative front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:51:06-07:00","id":233594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233579#post233579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeming as Agency also means that Seeming is less likely to impact your character\u2019s appearance. It\u2019s not impossible, mind you \u2014 your means of gaining agency may have involved seizing control over the physical transformations you were undergoing \u2014 but more likely than not, your physical appearance is determined almost entirely by your Kith, and your Seeming is almost entirely mental.</div> </div> </div> </div>A thought to add to this. <br /> Okay, if Seeming is the bridge, if you will, between the Faire and Human sides of a Changeling, this to me means that Seeming could be how you shaped yourself both physically and mentally to escape Arcadia. <br /> <br /> So, to give an example, say you were once literally made to be part of a building by your Keeper. In escaping, you couldn't just become a human again, but obviously, you can't just stay as part of a building to escape. So, you came up with a middle solution, becoming a moving mixture of rock and flesh(which I think some Earthbones look like).<br /> <br /> Maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:53:34-07:00","id":233597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233591#post233591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a great quote from Fate/Zero delivered by Tohsaka that basically embodies how the Fairest would embody Agency, at least on the positive front. I'll find it later.<br /> <br /> Given that the person saying this also gave his second daughter to a psychopath so she could continue the magic line instead of being left out and felt proud at the idea of his two daughters fighting for the root of magic, it might also be a commentary on the negative front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this sounds VERY interesting, and do hope you grab the quote. <br /> <br /> <br /> But, going back to Ogres, their embodiment of Agency, to tie to the original use of Ogres, could be using Brutality somehow. Their origins are essentially constant brutality directed against them, and encouraged to use it, in the original, so perhaps their escape is turning that on their Keepers somehow? <br /> <br /> Regardless, the new Kith and Seeming definitions certainly has me excited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:56:39-07:00","id":233599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233594#post233594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A thought to add to this. <br /> Okay, if Seeming is the bridge, if you will, between the Faire and Human sides of a Changeling, this to me means that Seeming could be how you shaped yourself both physically and mentally to escape Arcadia. <br /> <br /> So, to give an example, say you were once literally made to be part of a building by your Keeper. In escaping, you couldn't just become a human again, but obviously, you can't just stay as part of a building to escape. So, you came up with a middle solution, becoming a moving mixture of rock and flesh(which I think some Earthbones look like).<br /> <br /> Maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. It would allow changelings the option to have spent their Durances in wildly inhuman forms before reclaiming a basically human formon their way out the door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:01:15-07:00","id":233600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233599#post233599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe. It would allow changelings the option to have spent their Durances in wildly inhuman forms before reclaiming a basically human formon their way out the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would certainly be a cool concept, especially for Elementals, as it'd fit their alienation theme from the prior edition of the game, but giving it a new twist, as you had to use part of that nature to escape. <br /> <br /> Also fits into that, as a Changeling, one can't just deny their Faire side, but rather have to balance it with being human. Also, shaping yourself to escape would seem to be the height of Agency, to say the least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:05:44-07:00","id":233601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233571#post233571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Fairest as Agency, I think the most obvious answer is emotional manipulation. Did you convince a drudge to let you out the back for a kiss? Turn your Keeper's allies against them? Trade a lock of hair for the key to your shackles? Sally from Nightmare Before Christmas escaped repeatedly by drugging her &quot;creator&quot;, and convincing him to trust her cooking the next time she did something suspicious. That could be very Fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! Good ideas here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:14:08-07:00","id":233605,"title":"","content":"&quot;Maintain a calm mind. In order to control magic, you must first control your mind. Lose control,and the [magic] will suddenly rebound back to your body. Too much power, or power in the wrong form, will endanger not only yourself, but those around you. Strive to consistently maintain the proper flow. That is the Tohsaka family motto. <b><i>It means always remaining reserved and <u>elegant</u>.</i></b>&quot;-Tokiomi Tohsaka, Fate/Zero<br /> <br /> So two things: Creepy part, with everything I mentioned, I would still describe this guy as a loving father, and while he is strict, he is not cruel...until you account for how he bought his second daughter's 'happiness'. He's a human mage, but he quite embodies some of the most confusing and therefore terrifying Keepers there are.<br /> <br /> Second, the reason I think of the Fairest with this is because it occurs to me that they often win <i>by playing the Stranger's game</i>. They don't escape by the power of sensation, brutality, or arson, they don't sneak out or trick their way out-no, they take control in the midst of all their ecstasy, and act above and beyond pleasure and pain, <i>and they play the game well</i>. They act with elegance and poise, and become the Fair Folk(The Fairest, if you will) long enough to play the game and win enough to get out.<br /> <br /> Agency through poise, power from elegance. It strikes me as very Fairest.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And of course, that sort of attitude, that sort of distance, sets the stage for the Fairest to continue. THe lovely little girl the Strangers entertained will, by the final act, either come back to the game, or become immensely dull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2014, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:17:57-07:00","id":233609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233377#post233377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With both Elementals and Beasts, when I see them, their concepts both swing heavily toward rejection of the highly civilized.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is somewhat amusing to me, because my only Elemental character was a statue of glass, which is definitely more urban.<br /> <br /> And it was, by the way, a bit of a pain in chargen, because none of the friggin' Elemental kiths represent something fragile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:22:55-07:00","id":233614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233605#post233605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Maintain a calm mind. In order to control magic, you must first control your mind. Lose control,and the [magic] will suddenly rebound back to your body. Too much power, or power in the wrong form, will endanger not only yourself, but those around you. Strive to consistently maintain the proper flow. That is the Tohsaka family motto. <b><i>It means always remaining reserved and <u>elegant</u>.</i></b>&quot;-Tokiomi Tohsaka, Fate/Zero<br /> <br /> So two things: Creepy part, with everything I mentioned, I would still describe this guy as a loving father, and while he is strict, he is not cruel...until you account for how he bought his second daughter's 'happiness'. He's a human mage, but he quite embodies some of the most confusing and therefore terrifying Keepers there are.<br /> <br /> Second, the reason I think of the Fairest with this is because it occurs to me that they often win <i>by playing the Stranger's game</i>. They don't escape by the power of sensation, brutality, or arson, they don't sneak out or trick their way out-no, they take control in the midst of all their ecstasy, and act above and beyond pleasure and pain, <i>and they play the game well</i>. They act with elegance and poise, and become the Fair Folk(The Fairest, if you will) long enough to play the game and win enough to get out.<br /> <br /> Agency through poise, power from elegance. It strikes me as very Fairest.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And of course, that sort of attitude, that sort of distance, sets the stage for the Fairest to continue. THe lovely little girl the Strangers entertained will, by the final act, either come back to the game, or become immensely dull.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that is indeed quite a good quote. <br /> <br /> Now also quite interesting to think how this impacts the myriad number of Kiths, to put things mildly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:25:30-07:00","id":233616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233609#post233609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is somewhat amusing to me, because my only Elemental character was a statue of glass, which is definitely more urban.<br /> <br /> And it was, by the way, a bit of a pain in chargen, because none of the friggin' Elemental kiths represent something fragile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, Elementals to me are better represented by being raw materials than something dealing with, &quot;nature.&quot; <br /> <br /> Now, Mankin messed with this(to the point where someone made a separate Seeming based around machines), and stuff like Water and Air are messed with here, but honestly, I think the interpretation of them as material objects may still hold quite a bit. <br /> <br /> Also, that last bit might be less of an issue in the new version. That, and you forget things like shatterproof glass.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:31:37-07:00","id":233623,"title":"","content":"In all of this, Darklings and Wizened have an interesting time. Now, the former are relatively easy here, they snuck or scared their way out of captivity, and embraced that as part of their new Agency. <br /> <br /> Wizened though? In the original... their form is pure punishment, and they're the Seeming that seemed to represent the absolute worst possible fate for someone taken to Faire. What does that change to here to represent Agency? Yes, they're kind of the mental splat, if you will, but its worth noting elsewhere I think it was said that had more to do with a sort of process of natural selection being at work than anything inherent to their new natures. <br /> <br /> So, what do they represent here? They had to become useful to their Keepers somehow, so... hmm. Maybe their Agency is somehow related to Handiness? <br /> <br /> More thoughts here would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:32:01-07:00","id":233624,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting reveal! I'm still digesting it, but first impressions are positive! Also, since it seems I hadn't before, I wanted to compliment the idea of elevating the Kith to be more than just a subset of the Seeming. I see some people found the Seeming to be more important to them than the Kith,* but I had always found Kiths a more distinctive way to define my characters. I'm very pleased to hear they're becoming more prominent and robust.<br /> <br /> * Though <i>both</i> being very significant to a character in their own ways seems to go a long way in satisfying everyone.<br /> <br /> Hm, a question I haven't heard. In the current setup, the Seeming offers a blessing and a curse, while the Kith is all blessing. Given the change-up, are you considering reversing that? Or perhaps giving a blessing and a curse from each?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:40:02-07:00","id":233631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233623#post233623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all of this, Darklings and Wizened have an interesting time. Now, the former are relatively easy here, they snuck or scared their way out of captivity, and embraced that as part of their new Agency. <br /> <br /> Wizened though? In the original... their form is pure punishment, and they're the Seeming that seemed to represent the absolute worst possible fate for someone taken to Faire. What does that change to here to represent Agency? Yes, they're kind of the mental splat, if you will, but its worth noting elsewhere I think it was said that had more to do with a sort of process of natural selection being at work than anything inherent to their new natures. <br /> <br /> So, what do they represent here? They had to become useful to their Keepers somehow, so... hmm. Maybe their Agency is somehow related to Handiness? <br /> <br /> More thoughts here would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wizened? They gain agency through hard work and expertise. Shawshank Redemption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:52:10-07:00","id":233635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233631#post233631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wizened? They gain agency through hard work and expertise. Shawshank Redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. The latter I see, the former I would presume applies to all Seemings to some extent. <br /> <br /> But Expertise definitely makes sense here, considering their Kiths were previously defined by different job roles(Kiths like Soldier may now work far better). <br /> <br /> So... yeah, Shawshank Redemption would be a good comparison, all things considered. The expertise angle will create some oddities at points, but still, works. <br /> <br /> <br /> And... well, to return to Beasts, there's now more to work with. Specifically, their nature focus can be unique(assuming Elements stay with more of a raw material focus and local environment(not the same as natural because their environments could easily be urban). Now, as for how it causes Agency, it could be embracing, again, the chaotic, out of control side of being an animal. Whether that's being a feral dog to force your out, or being willing to squirm your way through sewage as a rat, you're doing what it takes as a beast would, and no longer being anyone's pet. <br /> <br /> Ogres meanwhile turning brutality against their masters has a myriad number of interpretations. An example could be getting all the brute strength you ever harnessed... and turning it on not only their Keepers, but anyone who dare gets in their way getting out. Others could be... well, being willing to inflict great pain somehow to get out. Just speculation for now. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:58:11-07:00","id":233656,"title":"","content":"Ogres could be something as simple as forcing one\u2019s way through the gate and plowing through any obstacles in your way.<br /> <br /> BTW, what I meant by \u201chard work\u201d was the twenty(?) years spent with a rock hammer to carve an escape tunnel; the expertise was the knowledge of geology that let him know it could work, and his bookkeeping skills that kept him alive and let him set up the rest of his escape plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2014, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:01:00-07:00","id":233660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233656#post233656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ogres could be something as simple as forcing one\u2019s way through the gate and plowing through any obstacles in your way.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. I admit I'm trying to extrapolate it from things like the little short stories that accompanied the original Seemings in the first core book.<br /> <br /> Darklings are interesting here in that it could mean becoming the monster, if you will, to escape, ala utilizing fear to force their way. Something to mull over. Stealth may play a part, but to be honest, that's more something a Kith that can now be any Seeming would embody more. <br /> <br /> Its fun to think over the new possibilities regardless.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-18-2014, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:06:15-07:00","id":233663,"title":"","content":"I started my first and only Changeling character by asking how many kiths I could buy with my merit points, and then completely forgetting about Seeming while I mixed and matched them to a common theme. While this is a single choice rather than a whole mix-match-ery, I do think my experience illustrates how people tend to like the Kiths more than the Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:15:33-07:00","id":233674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233631#post233631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wizened? They gain agency through hard work and expertise. Shawshank Redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought is &quot;Agency through (systematic) understanding, power from expertise.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Wizened are associated with craft-work, even the Oracles, Drudges, and Fatemakers. And, as everyone knows, how a thing is made has a lot of layers to it. But understanding the process and the systems of a thing, be it a book or a human body or Fate itself, you learn how to subvert those crafts. A Wizened is someone who probably comes to understand the game the Strangers are playing, and takes advantage of the flaws in the system. If <i>anyone</i> is going to deliberately use a Stranger's frailty to escape, it's going to be a Wizened, because he knows the rules of their game, <i>and he can break them or twist them to his advantage.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2014, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:25:28-07:00","id":233687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233674#post233674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thought is &quot;Agency through (systematic) understanding, power through expertise.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Wizened are associated with craft-work, even the Oracles, Drudges, and Fatemakers. And, as everyone knows, how a thing is made has a lot of layers to it. But understanding the process and the systems of a thing, be it a book or a human body or Fate itself, you learn how to subvert those crafts. A Wizened is someone who probably comes to understand the game the Strangers are playing, and takes advantage of the flaws in the system. If <i>anyone</i> is going to deliberately use a Stranger's frailty to escape, it's going to be a Wizened, because he knows the rules of their game, <i>and he can break them or twist them to his advantage.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, interesting.<br /> <br /> A lot of manipulation style origins here, which is hardly a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on Darklings here? I've got fear, but am trying to think how to tie that into their Agency here.<br /> <br /> To give Ogres more than just being brute force types for Agency, perhaps a look at Oathbreaker could have interesting results? That could perhaps represent them beating up the True Fae by bending their rules to force a fair fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-18-2014, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:37:18-07:00","id":233702,"title":"","content":"Ogre's easy enough, so I'll do them too.<br /> <br /> Agency through violence, power from might.<br /> <br /> The Ogres are the ones who flip the game board. They might start it up with &quot;I got a 23, what does that mean&quot; and then punch the Stranger while he's looking up the result, but either way, someone's getting hit with a fist the size of a stump. Of course, might's not really the point alone-it's <i>violence</i>. An Ogre doesn't have to be strong to be violent, and <i>violence</i> is the great decider. If you can <i>violate Them </i>like they violated you, then how can they stop you? To threaten their lives and livelihood, to put the fear of death or maiming in them, that's Ogres. It's the abuse victim who goes nuts and stabs the guy 50 times and yells at them to leave them the fuck alone before storming out(and that abuse need not even ave been physical in response, it could have been social or emotional-Fiona is a princess who becomes an Ogre doesn't correlate, but that image does). They never needed to be deep stabs individually, so long as they can choose their own will by creating a dire consequence for any other answer.<br /> <br /> Of course, Might just makes it easy. And when you have it easy, why bother with the social niceties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:40:28-07:00","id":233705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233687#post233687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, interesting.<br /> <br /> A lot of manipulation style origins here, which is hardly a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on Darklings here? I've got fear, but am trying to think how to tie that into their Agency here.<br /> <br /> To give Ogres more than just being brute force types for Agency, perhaps a look at Oathbreaker could have interesting results? That could perhaps represent them beating up the True Fae by bending their rules to force a fair fight?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Our initial thought was Darklings = Betrayal. You betrayed someone else. You tripped your proverbial friend during the escape. You resorted to darkness in order to save yourself. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:42:49-07:00","id":233708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233705#post233705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Our initial thought was Darklings = Betrayal. You betrayed someone else. You tripped your proverbial friend during the escape. You resorted to darkness in order to save yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been poking at Darklings, trying to get them down pat.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is it(it somewhat negatively stereotypes them <i>way more</i> than the others), but it does feel in the neighborhood.<br /> <br /> 'Course, I don't make those calls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:43:12-07:00","id":233709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233702#post233702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ogre's easy enough, so I'll do them too.<br /> <br /> Agency through violence, power from might.<br /> <br /> The Ogres are the ones who flip the game board. They might start it up with &quot;I got a 23, what does that mean&quot; and then punch the Stranger while he's looking up the result, but either way, someone's getting hit with a fist the size of a stump. Of course, might's not really the point alone-it's <i>violence</i>. An Ogre doesn't have to be strong to be violent, and <i>violence</i> is the great decider. If you can <i>violate Them </i>like they violated you, then how can they stop you? To threaten their lives and livelihood, to put the fear of death or maiming in them, that's Ogres. It's the abuse victim who goes nuts and stabs the guy 50 times and yells at them to leave them the fuck alone before storming out(and that abuse need not even ave been physical in response, it could have been social or emotional-Fiona is a princess who becomes an Ogre doesn't correlate, but that image does). They never needed to be deep stabs individually, so long as they can choose their own will by creating a dire consequence for any other answer.<br /> <br /> Of course, Might just makes it easy. And when you have it easy, why bother with the social niceties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Great! Fits the themes of the original Changeling the Lost book, while giving a way for their Seeming to be liberating. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, so far we have someone bending social rules to their advantage, Fairest, using raw material selves to escape somehow, Elementals, turning to the wild side of Nature, Beasts, (I admit the last two may need more development), using violence to escape, not necessarily physical, as Ogres, and using expertise, along with advantages of such, to manipulate the rules to escape, Wizened. <br /> <br /> Darklings... hmm. We have themes of becoming something to Fear, along with losing the part of humanity that allows one to say, tolerate the sun, in the original. Evolving this to Agency suggests using fear, and perhaps a sort of monstrous cunning to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:45:28-07:00","id":233718,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's one answer to take from how a Seeming represents agency. I agree with Arcane's bit on the Wizened (which is great!) being the most likely to use the rules of the game to turn a frailty against their Good Folk -- it fits especially well with the idea that the Wizened are lessened; of course they know deficiencies! Still, I'd argue the Fairest stand a good chance of the tactic as well. While beating the Gentry at their own game has an excellent feel, I can also see a Fairest seizing on a frailty. They are the ones playing a game most like the Stranger's, after all, and are most likely brutalized for not playing perfectly. The Fairest are the closest of the Lost to being their Keepers, <i>but</i> <i>they're not there</i>. Even if they know they're close. That's important to them. And they may just use this tremendous insight into their own weaknesses with their human viewpoint to make their Stranger crumple for the lessons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:47:12-07:00","id":233723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233718#post233718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's one answer to take from how a Seeming represents agency. I agree with Arcane's bit on the Wizened (which is great!) being the most likely to use the rules of the game to turn a frailty against their Good Folk -- it fits especially well with the idea that the Wizened are lessened; of course they know deficiencies! Still, I'd argue the Fairest stand a good chance of the tactic as well. While beating the Gentry at their own game has an excellent feel, I can also see a Fairest seizing on a frailty. They are the ones playing a game most like the Stranger's, after all, and are most likely brutalized for not playing perfectly. The Fairest are the closest of the Lost to being their Keepers, <i>but</i> <i>they're not there</i>. Even if they know they're close. That's important to them. And they may just use this tremendous insight into their own weaknesses with their human viewpoint to make their Stranger crumple for the lessons.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true, my approach, so far, has been to try to use what I know of the Seemings in the original core book to identify how they reflect Agency. Still, good point. <br /> <br /> But hmm. Darklings are indeed tricky here. We have the usage of Violence, Ogres, Social rules, in a way, with Fairest, and Wizened turning the rules of the game against the True Fae. <br /> <br /> So... well, how's the game with fear? The True Fae can't really be scared, but their servants can. Additionally, the over all element of Darkness with them(disliking the Sun, along with their Kiths mostly emphasizing the theme), could allow them to literally sneak away from their Keepers, with numerous implications from that alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-18-2014, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:56:43-07:00","id":233730,"title":"","content":"I was thinking the Darklings\u2019 agency came from deception\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:58:48-07:00","id":233732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233730#post233730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking the Darklings\u2019 agency came from deception\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting... although not sure how that ties into their fear theme, and additionally... wouldn't that apply to all Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:05:08-07:00","id":233736,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest True Fae can be scared (or at least act the part). Some Darklings sneak away from their Keepers, but others frighten their Keepers into releasing them. What do the Fae fear? Loss of power, loss of titles, becoming lesser beings, having others gain dominion over them. The truly cunning Darklings spread whispers of the discovery of their Keeper's bane, weaving these whispers into the story of the Keeper's play until the True Fae cannot help but believe them. Desperate and afraid, these Keepers expel the Darkling from their domains before the wicked changeling can use the bane to destroy or limit the True Fae.<br /> <br /> Simultaneously, the True Fae gorges on the passions and thrill generated by the whispers, gorging on the unrepeatable meal as the Darkling escapes. With its nemesis gone, the fear quickly fades, leaving the Keeper empty, listless and less alive than ever before. It casts its net out to find another victim to bring to its domain in the hope of experiencing such thrills again. But the Darkling doesn't care about any of that - she tricked a True Fae with shadow and misdirection, and if she can flee back through the thorns into the real world she may have a second chance at life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:11:43-07:00","id":233740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233732#post233732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting... although not sure how that ties into their fear theme, and additionally... wouldn't that apply to all Changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Deception can apply to any changeling; exploitng loopholes in the rules can apply to any changeling, as can hard work. That\u2019s not a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:17:26-07:00","id":233748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233740#post233740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deception can apply to any changeling; exploitng loopholes in the rules can apply to any changeling, as can hard work. That\u2019s not a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true, but we are trying to introduce the spin each Seeming brings to the table here. Still, good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:20:37-07:00","id":233751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233736#post233736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest True Fae can be scared (or at least act the part). Some Darklings sneak away from their Keepers, but others frighten their Keepers into releasing them. What do the Fae fear? Loss of power, loss of titles, becoming lesser beings, having others gain dominion over them. The truly cunning Darklings spread whispers of the discovery of their Keeper's bane, weaving these whispers into the story of the Keeper's play until the True Fae cannot help but believe them. Desperate and afraid, these Keepers expel the Darkling from their domains before the wicked changeling can use the bane to destroy or limit the True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>That. Is. Awesome. It gives Darklings a new spin on manipulation, also gives them experience at doing something that gives them fearsome tools to use in the mortal world too. <br /> <br /> I mean, can you imagine what a Changeling that preys on paranoia could be capable of? Especially if they have say, the resources of a Freehold Court behind them, or even an entire freehold in some instances? (Aspects of this may change, yes, but still, worth noting for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simultaneously, the True Fae gorges on the passions and thrill generated by the whispers, gorging on the unrepeatable meal as the Darkling escapes. With its nemesis gone, the fear quickly fades, leaving the Keeper empty, listless and less alive than ever before. It casts its net out to find another victim to bring to its domain in the hope of experiencing such thrills again. But the Darkling doesn't care about any of that - she tricked a True Fae with shadow and misdirection, and if she can flee back through the thorns into the real world she may have a second chance at life. </div> </div> </div>Finished well too. That you found something the True Fae fear, and in a way, allowed the Darklings to rob them of power in the process? Is awesome creativity. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:24:01-07:00","id":233775,"title":"","content":"All changelings use deception.<br /> <br /> But Darklings do it behind your back. Everyone else has a certain &quot;cards in the open&quot; attitude about themselves, risking being caught in their tricks, where the Darklings go the extra step to hide it from you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:24:38-07:00","id":233776,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm going to ramble a bit here, and it's largely unrelated to the ideas people have been having.<br /> Kith is defined by what you *gained* from your durance. So an mermaid's gills, an antiquarian's trivia, or a singer's musical voice. It's the superficial what you 'are': a fish-person or a sage or a performer. It's what people will see on the outside. Mechanically, a kith gives you a blessing (like ability to breath water, or bonuses to research and knowledge rolls, or bonuses to performance and charm).<br /> Seeming always seemed to be more defined by how your durance messed you up. A beast lost their sense of civilisation and became feral and wild. A darkling gave up something important, and now has a void where it used to be that they need to fill. An elemental forgot that they were ever a person, and now struggles to relate to people rather than things. A fairest gave up on their mortal life, and became more like their keeper. An ogre became brutalised and calloused by the horrible things inflicted on them. A wizened was forced to work and sacrifice, and now can't feel joy or satisfaction in anything else. Seeming's give you a curse (and only a curse), such as a darkling's cravings (making them more susceptible to virtue/vice) a fairest's madness (making them more likely to degenerate) or a wizened's obsession (giving them penalties to 'idle' tasks).<br /> <br /> So, for your concept, you pick your Kith, and your seeming, and combine them to determine how you ended up.<br /> So you might combine the antiquarian kith and the fairest's seeming, getting the regal intellectual who considers herself above 'petty mortal concerns' since she knows the truth now! An antiquarian Wizened, however, is our joyless scribe who can't ever take a day off- everybody will be dead soon, but his records will live on, so why eat, drink and be merry?<br /> A darkling, meanwile, could be a singer who was so deprived of attention that she forced herself to whisper in her master's ear whilst he slept, honing her voice as she did so. Now free, she uses her singing to gain the adoration she desperately craves. A darkling flamekin, meanwhile, was deprived of warmth and light, until he literally set himself alight rather than shivering, and craves home and comfort after being exposed to the elements.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3726-xtan","name":"Xtan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:32:08-07:00","id":233779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233775#post233775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All changelings use deception.<br /> <br /> But Darklings do it behind your back. Everyone else has a certain &quot;cards in the open&quot; attitude about themselves, risking being caught in their tricks, where the Darklings go the extra step to hide it from you.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and this oddly shows a unique element for each other, how they hide their tricks. Fairest use social ability and customs to hide their tricks, Ogres use violence to, perhaps not hide, but at least enforce their tricks? Meanwhile, Wizened use their expertise to hide their various tricks.<br /> <br /> Now, for a more full take on Elementals.<br /> <br /> Elementals are defined by alienation, which means turning that to Agency oddly means... well, turning lack of understanding to advantage. The True Fae lack empathy, and while experienced with plotting, this weakness can strike, the Elementals being a good example. How do you know the thoughts or plans of a pile of rocks? The wind? The ocean? And when the time comes to escape, they have built the strength to smash their way out like a natural disaster, smashing away even the True Fae on their way out.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Did have to go back to nature elements, but still tied to them being inanimate objects. Trying to match excellent suggestions so far with the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:34:42-07:00","id":233782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233736#post233736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest True Fae can be scared (or at least act the part). Some Darklings sneak away from their Keepers, but others frighten their Keepers into releasing them. What do the Fae fear? Loss of power, loss of titles, becoming lesser beings, having others gain dominion over them. The truly cunning Darklings spread whispers of the discovery of their Keeper's bane, weaving these whispers into the story of the Keeper's play until the True Fae cannot help but believe them. Desperate and afraid, these Keepers expel the Darkling from their domains before the wicked changeling can use the bane to destroy or limit the True Fae.<br /> <br /> Simultaneously, the True Fae gorges on the passions and thrill generated by the whispers, gorging on the unrepeatable meal as the Darkling escapes. With its nemesis gone, the fear quickly fades, leaving the Keeper empty, listless and less alive than ever before. It casts its net out to find another victim to bring to its domain in the hope of experiencing such thrills again. But the Darkling doesn't care about any of that - she tricked a True Fae with shadow and misdirection, and if she can flee back through the thorns into the real world she may have a second chance at life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: doesn't this cross over onto the Autumn Court's toes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:45:57-07:00","id":233809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233782#post233782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: doesn't this cross over onto the Autumn Court's toes?</div> </div> </div> </div>True, however isn't the Autumn also magic? That, and there are fears besides paranoia, which was the main theme there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:50:08-07:00","id":233817,"title":"","content":"No more than Changelings who use violence to escape tread on the Summer Court's toes, or those who hide and sneak away tread on Winter's.<br /> <br /> IMO, and building on what David has given us so far, the means of escape gives the Seeming, but what you choose to do *next* defines the character's outlook on her returned life, which may in turn lead to her Court.<br /> <br /> Put another way - just because a Changeling saw stealth and deception as her only way to escape the Durance doesn't mean she can't t emerge from the Hedge burning with rage, that leads her to sign up with the Summer Court to finally be able to get physical with those True Fae bastards!<br /> <br /> Edit: Characters can be easy or strange fits for their Court of choice. The Changeling who started the Autumn Court, and the initial quorum of that group, came from somewhere. They had the idea of finding the True Fae's weaknesses and using fear to protect themselves and fight back. Maybe they came up with the idea after they returned, maybe they remembered it from snippets of nightmares, maybe they had clear memories of their durances? These Changelings are an easy fit for the Autumn Court's theme, but they aren't the only members, and Autumn doesn't have a monopoly on fear, they just thrive best in it.<br /> <br /> 2nd Edit: The first edit was cross-posted with Dataweaver's post below. We must have been on the same frequency <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 08-19-2014, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:51:03-07:00","id":233818,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s worth noting that the original Courts were defined by how the changeling responds to his Durance \u2014 which is quite similar to this new take on Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:51:20-07:00","id":233819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233817#post233817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No more than Changelings who use violence to escape tread on the Summer Court's toes, or those who hide and sneak away tread on Winter's.<br /> <br /> IMO, and building on what David has given us so far, the means of escape gives the Seeming, but what you choose to do *next* defines the character's outlook on her returned life, which may in turn lead to her Court.<br /> <br /> Put another way - just because a Changeling saw stealth and deception as her only way to escape the Durance doesn't mean she can't t emerge from the Hedge burning with rage, that leads her to sign up with the Summer Court to finally be able to get physical with those True Fae bastards!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Part of me wonder how much of this is going to be used.<br /> <br /> Also, holy shit, 12 pages?<br /> <br /> Changeling, you still one popular babe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:53:31-07:00","id":233825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233818#post233818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s worth noting that the original Courts were defined by how the changeling responds to his Durance \u2014 which is quite similar to this new take on Seemings.</div> </div> </div> </div>And seeing as we know courts are changing too, this suggests they have a new role as well, although I imagine it being something to help unite Changelings, and perhaps avoid their former Keepers through tricks, could stick around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:15:19-07:00","id":233896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233529#post233529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can kind of see the distinction, but I don't think it's as concrete as it could be. One of my writers said she has some ideas about Fatebound stuff. It's not something we've discussed yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm going to mention it now, since I just thought of it, but... reading over this, Fatebound seems like it could be a... this is a bit complex but the idea in my head is almost like a &quot;Court of One&quot; baked into your Seeming? It's a role you choose to help protect you, part of how you escape and stay free, if that makes sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:22:33-07:00","id":233906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233705#post233705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Our initial thought was Darklings = Betrayal. You betrayed someone else. You tripped your proverbial friend during the escape. You resorted to darkness in order to save yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My thoughts are not necessarily Betrayal, but Loss (which can be included)... or maybe a better word is Sacrifice... did you give up something of yourself to escape? A friend? What is worth losing but not too costly for the chance to return home?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:40:46-07:00","id":234066,"title":"","content":"Ok, let's see. If your Seeming is the way you escaped this could be:<br /> <br /> Beasts: You return to your most primal self, to your animal parts. That's not just wild, it's pure instict. Only impulses not reasoning.<br /> Darklings: You embrace the darkest parts of yourself. You flee harming others, or hurting yourself, physically or mentally. It can be betrayal, sacrifice, some kind of fae-death or much darker things.<br /> Elementals: You forget to be human, you become something else because you can't escape Feerie if you don't understand it. And to understand Feerie you have to be a part of it.<br /> Fairest: You lie, seduce, intimidate, manipulate... You're the Beauty, the Grace. And (like the old tales tell) Beauty means you can do, you can get anything you want, by any mean you need.<br /> Ogres: Violence. The ogres has always been creatures of violence, not just brute force, but abuse and torture, both mental and physical.<br /> Wizened: You keep withering, until you where nothing but your work. And your work, and through your slavery you free yourself.<br /> <br /> I think the most important thing is to get something that can makes that any kind of flight work for every Seeming. For example, if you betray your Keeper: a Beast could embrace his primal being until become the best dog of his Keeper until one day he bites him and eat him; a Darkling could sell his own shadow to get a poison that will kill everyone with a shadow in the realm where he is captive; an Elemental could be a lover made of fire from the hearth of the house who keeps warm hier Keeper everynight, until one night she burns him, and all his palace; a Fairest could seduce him, make all kind of promises to him, until he begins to make promises to her, and she can use them to tie him and free herself; and Ogre could cook for his Keeper and add a poison to his food to make him sleep, and then suffocate him ith her bare hands; a Wizened could be the best smith in the realm, there are no armours like te ones he creates, until the time is right and he creates an armour that reveals agains his own wielder.<br /> <br /> I think that every Seeming should reflect something wide enough so any kind of escape can work will every Seeming. Just saying &quot;Darklings is betrayal&quot; sounds too easy. Perhaps, sometimes some escape could work for two Seeming, but that's better than made it too narrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/n6g3njp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/kpa5GS5Mp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/93820aaad7.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/584-eliseo-ap-liam","name":"Eliseo ap Liam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:09:30-07:00","id":234100,"title":"","content":"I like it conceptually. It really jives with how players <i>actually</i> go about making their characters and shows you are really paying attention to things like that, which I appreciate. It does highlight a few challenges that would have to be discussed anyways, but this direction makes us have to look at them a smidge earlier. This is just brainspew continuing along the lines of thinking about the implications of what you've posted. I'm sure you know some/all of this already.<br /> <br /> <b>1) Kiths are going to have to serve a fundamentally different role in the narrative and characterization of Changeling.</b><br /> Before, Kiths were glorified merits and pallet swaps of their Seemings. Its really a case where players took something relatively minor but evocative and latched on to it for dear life (which is awesome!). That said, their current design is inappropriate to let them occupy the space your giving them. They will need to be bigger, more general, and be able to represent a variety of concepts. This is pretty easy to do, but its important to keep in mind that this is happening going forward. As an aside, a perhaps overlooked area to mine for ideas on how to handle this might be Talecrafting. What if Kiths were more Fairytale Archetypes or the type of story (Fae) you were caught up in? Then Seemings take it from general archetypes to specific, flavorful examples.<br /> <br /> <b>2) You have a crisis of depth vs breadth of concept on your hands.</b><br /> art of the original appeal of kiths is their specificity. A person who wants to play something specific looks through a list of Kiths and the game tells them, &quot;Oh yeah. You want Fire Elements? We -totally- got Fire Elements. Pick this. Now you're a Fire Elemental. Isn't that cool? Did I say cool? I meant Hot. You are totally HOT STUFF.&quot; For someone who isn't sure what they are playing yet, a list of Kiths was an easy list of instant concepts. It also hedged itself against paralysis of choice by presenting itself as primarily a fluff choice, with Seemings being the big, but manageable important choice. Note that this dynamic changes for older players, but its important to keep in mind for newer players. This means your Kith/Seeming system really has three central goals it needs to fulfill.<br /> a) You need to address specific concepts in order to enable your creative players.<br /> b) You need to tease and sell the gameline to invite and entice your hesitant players into the game.<br /> c) Do something about Choice Paralysis.<br /> <br /> <b>3) Formatting is going to be key, it needs to be decided early, and its going to be difficult.</b><br /> This is one of those &quot;how you present the information is more important than the information itself&quot; situations. Although from a design perspective it might be &quot;Choose Kith, Flavor it With Seeming&quot; the presentation might want to go against the grain for that on the outset. You're going to want specific examples in Kiths anyways, which requires the reader to understand Seemings, so you may actually want to present Seemings in the book before you present Kiths. Seemings are also probably where you want your vignettes and very narrative-heavy material, that's because Kiths have a very particular need.<br /> <br /> <b>4) People need to be able to decide whether they want to play a certain Kith without actually reading the material.</b><br /> Being able to do this is the difference between &quot;ugh, this is a slog&quot; and &quot;holy shit that's awesome! That's even MORE awesome!&quot; Obviously some skimming of the material will be necessary, but they should be able to ascertain everything they need to know to determine if they want to play a certain character by reading the name, the section headings, maybe a one-liner presented at the bottom and no more than two sentences. The amount of space each Kith takes up also needs to not be more than a page (with fancy formatting and/or art) or half a page (without that). This is so that each Kith requires a minimal amount of emotional investment in order to reach the cool stuff.<br /> <br /> If players are here, they want to be sold. Their brains will naturally filter out information that isn't important to them and will zero in on whatever they think is awesome. If we make it very easy for the brain to find the parts it thinks is cool, players will walk away from most Kiths thinking they are great, and that some Kiths are -really- amazing. If you make someone have to read an entire page or even half a page before deciding whether a Kith is for them and they decide it isn't, then you add a bit of emotional baggage as the reader will feel their effort was &quot;wasted.&quot; This will carry on to the next entry. The formatting needs to facilitate the brain's natural screening process in every possible way. I would also consider, but not am not sold on, presenting choosing your Kith and Seeming as being a part of the same &quot;step.&quot; It should prevent cognitive dissonance and let people who decide to picks Seeming first (for whatever reason) to do that.<br /> <br /> <b>5) Art is going to be important, and can lift some of the burden off your writers.</b><br /> Changeling and Art are conceptually married on a fundemental level. While it is almost certainly too early to worry about the specifics of art, I think that writing Kiths/Seemings in particular would benefit from deciding what and how much weight your artwork is going to pull. There is a rather large contingent of people (particularly LARPers) who are &quot;sold&quot; on Changeling by the costuming opportunities and the variety of exotic semi-human characters that are possible. A picture can drive that point home and get the creative juices flowing better than any block of text.<br /> <br /> If your writers understand what the pictures are going to, in general, do it'll help them not waste wordcount. If each Kith is going to have a picture accompanying it showing an example from that Kith (which would be great but may not be in budget) then you don't have to spend too much time describing what it looks like. I would also have as many art pieces as is reasonable feature a different type of changeling. I'm debating whether actually labeling them would be of benefit or if it'd actually stifle creativity. The point of the art throughout the book should be &quot;See that? You can TOTALLY play that&quot; and to otherwise empower the players. Not every entry, for sure, but a lion's share of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-19-2014, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:49:12-07:00","id":234146,"title":"","content":"Off the top for Seemings as Agency. Will probably circle back and expand on these later.<br /> <br /> Beasts<br /> The Ones Who Bought Freedom<br /> - Billy Goats Gruff style &quot;Oh you don't want me.&quot;<br /> - Ten years a captain for a hundred years of service. Your Keeper's come due for payment but you'll be damned if that's going to happen.<br /> - He just wanted your heart, so you left it with him. Sometimes you can still feel cold fingers grip your chest.<br /> - Beasts are flat out more desperate and willing to give up more than other Changelings. They know more than anyone else the price of freedom.<br /> <br /> Darklings<br /> The Ones Who Slipped Away<br /> - Run. Other people played the Fae's games. Most of them didn't make it. You have your bag of tricks but you use them to do the smart thing: <i>run</i>.<br /> - Darklings are more cunning than other Changelings. They observed and learned their keeper's habits, and then worked in the places their keeper didn't see. While all Changelings &quot;escaped&quot; in some fashion, Darklings <b>escaped</b>.<br /> <br /> Elementals<br /> The Ones Who Played Along<br /> - Shawshank Redemption style playing along with the system and then using it as leverage to escape.<br /> - Some elementals are just let go. They don't know why. Maybe their Keeper got bored. Maybe they didn't. Not sure which is more terrifying.<br /> - Above all, Elementals <i>endure</i> the torments other Changelings shy away from. They look their keeper in the eyes as she carves poetry into their lungs.<br /> <br /> Fairest<br /> The Ones Enticed The Guard<br /> - Not &quot;No.&quot; Instead &quot;Yes, but...&quot; Fairest engaged in a delicate dance with their Keeper by holding what they wanted just out of reach until the opportune moment.<br /> - Maybe you still have the thing the Keeper wanted (assuming it wasn't you), maybe you put it forever out of their reach, or maybe you gave it to them. All good angles for story.<br /> - Pick a princess or historical figure that made the hero do really stupid and dangerous stuff in exchange for um... Love. Lets call it Love. Napolean's Wife is actually pretty hilarious as inspiration for this. If you haven't read her letters I highly recommend it.<br /> - Pitting one Keeper against another or enticing someone else to fight for you should probably fall under here as well. Fairest and Ogre/Wizened/Darkling pairs should be a thing.<br /> - Fairest know what everyone else wants and knows just how to not give it to them. They are more willing to play the &quot;game&quot; and far more prone to winning. More than any other Changelings, Fairest will do anything to win.<br /> <br /> Ogres<br /> The Ones Who Broke their Chains<br /> - They pried their freedom from their Keeper's cold, dead hands. If only Keepers stayed dead.<br /> - Pick a prison break scene where like three people escape at the end.<br /> - Pick any action horror movie ever.<br /> - More than any other Changelings, Ogres understand they have to fight. While other Changelings plan or coerce Ogres <i>act</i>. They don't win by knowing the rules, they win by just being good enough.<br /> <br /> Wizened<br /> The Ones Who Found the Key<br /> - Caroline with the snowglobe scene.<br /> - Sphnx's riddles.<br /> - You figured out the rules to the game and with lateral thinking figured a way out.<br /> - Wizened understand Magic and the Wyrd more than any other Changeling. Others look and see a malestrom of chaos where the Wizened observes a sea of opportunity. They tricked the Fae at their own game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-19-2014, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:18:24-07:00","id":234159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eliseo ap Liam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234066#post234066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, let's see. If your Seeming is the way you escaped this could be:<br /> <br /> Beasts: You return to your most primal self, to your animal parts. That's not just wild, it's pure instict. Only impulses not reasoning.<br /> Darklings: You embrace the darkest parts of yourself. You flee harming others, or hurting yourself, physically or mentally. It can be betrayal, sacrifice, some kind of fae-death or much darker things.<br /> Elementals: You forget to be human, you become something else because you can't escape Feerie if you don't understand it. And to understand Feerie you have to be a part of it.<br /> Fairest: You lie, seduce, intimidate, manipulate... You're the Beauty, the Grace. And (like the old tales tell) Beauty means you can do, you can get anything you want, by any mean you need.<br /> Ogres: Violence. The ogres has always been creatures of violence, not just brute force, but abuse and torture, both mental and physical.<br /> Wizened: You keep withering, until you where nothing but your work. And your work, and through your slavery you free yourself.<br /> <br /> I think the most important thing is to get something that can makes that any kind of flight work for every Seeming. For example, if you betray your Keeper: a Beast could embrace his primal being until become the best dog of his Keeper until one day he bites him and eat him; a Darkling could sell his own shadow to get a poison that will kill everyone with a shadow in the realm where he is captive; an Elemental could be a lover made of fire from the hearth of the house who keeps warm hier Keeper everynight, until one night she burns him, and all his palace; a Fairest could seduce him, make all kind of promises to him, until he begins to make promises to her, and she can use them to tie him and free herself; and Ogre could cook for his Keeper and add a poison to his food to make him sleep, and then suffocate him ith her bare hands; a Wizened could be the best smith in the realm, there are no armours like te ones he creates, until the time is right and he creates an armour that reveals agains his own wielder.<br /> <br /> I think that every Seeming should reflect something wide enough so any kind of escape can work will every Seeming. Just saying &quot;Darklings is betrayal&quot; sounds too easy. Perhaps, sometimes some escape could work for two Seeming, but that's better than made it too narrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with some of these is they don't quite embrace the Agency part enough, which to me means the Seeming as being Empowering. Hence, the focus on the more positive parts of each Seeming earlier in the thread. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:31:27-07:00","id":234164,"title":"","content":"(Note, I'm playing Devil's advocate here as much as I can, sorry if that comes off badly at any point.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234146#post234146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the top for Seemings as Agency. Will probably circle back and expand on these later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts<br /> The Ones Who Bought Freedom<br /> - Billy Goats Gruff style &quot;Oh you don't want me.&quot;<br /> - Ten years a captain for a hundred years of service. Your Keeper's come due for payment but you'll be damned if that's going to happen.<br /> - He just wanted your heart, so you left it with him. Sometimes you can still feel cold fingers grip your chest.<br /> - Beasts are flat out more desperate and willing to give up more than other Changelings. They know more than anyone else the price of freedom. </div> </div> </div>This... doesn't really match Beasts in 1.0. I mean, for one thing, &quot;bought,&quot; doesn't really seem like something Beasts would do. Does an animal buy anything? And that's the main thing that has defined Beasts before this, being primal. <br /> <br /> Now, yes, Beasts will change, but why in this direction? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Darklings<br /> The Ones Who Slipped Away<br /> - Run. Other people played the Fae's games. Most of them didn't make it. You have your bag of tricks but you use them to do the smart thing: <i>run</i>.<br /> - Darklings are more cunning than other Changelings. They observed and learned their keeper's habits, and then worked in the places their keeper didn't see. While all Changelings &quot;escaped&quot; in some fashion, Darklings <b>escaped</b>. </div> </div> </div>These both seem like traits almost every Changeling would have to use at some point anyway. I will grant you cunning may fit Darklings more but running? At some point, that's what every Changeling had to do, even those who played the game, why should Darklings get to be especially good at it, especially when part of their theme was being scary themselves?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Elementals<br /> The Ones Who Played Along<br /> - Shawshank Redemption style playing along with the system and then using it as leverage to escape.<br /> - Some elementals are just let go. They don't know why. Maybe their Keeper got bored. Maybe they didn't. Not sure which is more terrifying.<br /> - Above all, Elementals <i>endure</i> the torments other Changelings shy away from. They look their keeper in the eyes as she carves poetry into their lungs. </div> </div> </div>With the 2nd, wouldn't their Keeper just forget they exist, and therefore, not let them go? The leverage idea also seems odd given that implies a social ability most Elementals aren't really supposed to possess, considering their alienation themes. <br /> <br /> Now, I actually like the idea of enduring torments others can't, because that could fit taking being a material to your own advantage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fairest<br /> The Ones Enticed The Guard<br /> - Not &quot;No.&quot; Instead &quot;Yes, but...&quot; Fairest engaged in a delicate dance with their Keeper by holding what they wanted just out of reach until the opportune moment.<br /> - Maybe you still have the thing the Keeper wanted (assuming it wasn't you), maybe you put it forever out of their reach, or maybe you gave it to them. All good angles for story.<br /> - Pick a princess or historical figure that made the hero do really stupid and dangerous stuff in exchange for um... Love. Lets call it Love. Napolean's Wife is actually pretty hilarious as inspiration for this. If you haven't read her letters I highly recommend it.<br /> - Pitting one Keeper against another or enticing someone else to fight for you should probably fall under here as well. Fairest and Ogre/Wizened/Darkling pairs should be a thing.<br /> - Fairest know what everyone else wants and knows just how to not give it to them. They are more willing to play the &quot;game&quot; and far more prone to winning. More than any other Changelings, Fairest will do anything to win. </div> </div> </div>No issues here, all emphasizes the social aspects of being a Fairest that we all know and love, along with their darker bits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ogres<br /> The Ones Who Broke their Chains<br /> - They pried their freedom from their Keeper's cold, dead hands. If only Keepers stayed dead.<br /> - Pick a prison break scene where like three people escape at the end.<br /> - Pick any action horror movie ever.<br /> - More than any other Changelings, Ogres understand they have to fight. While other Changelings plan or coerce Ogres <i>act</i>. They don't win by knowing the rules, they win by just being good enough. </div> </div> </div>Again, no issues, seeing as Ogres are the ones said to be crafted from violence in the original, and that theme still feels strong here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wizened<br /> The Ones Who Found the Key<br /> - Caroline with the snowglobe scene.<br /> - Sphnx's riddles.<br /> - You figured out the rules to the game and with lateral thinking figured a way out.<br /> - Wizened understand Magic and the Wyrd more than any other Changeling. Others look and see a malestrom of chaos where the Wizened observes a sea of opportunity. They tricked the Fae at their own game. </div> </div> </div>On one hand, I do agree mental would be important to them, but on the other hand, what about their expertise? To be fair, yes, that's taking a Kith centric approach where it doesn't work anymore, but its worth noting Wizened were defined a lot by their profession, and by extension, a particular expertise they had. Shouldn't that be the case here as well?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:44:02-07:00","id":234174,"title":"","content":"This is a -tiny- bit off topic from how Kiths relate to Seemings and going into how Seemings relate to powers.<br /> <br /> Just want to take a moment to comment on the powers, contracts, and how that relates to Seemings. I'm not certain if &quot;Contracts will be flavored by your Seeming&quot; is something that is set in stone but I hope to God it isn't. <i>That design decision will cause massive headaches for all future supplements and all fan creators.</i> I think what you are trying to do is have Seemings create an undercurrent to how the players solve conflict within the story. The Ogre who beat the worst thing to ever happen in her life by punching it in the face is likely to punch all of her problems in the face until she runs into someone without a face. Or that can't be punched. Whatever. The Fairest who was entrusted with the Fae's True Heart (a giant ruby) and collected the things he needed for his escape by claiming he just <i>needed</i> them to tend to or enhance the greatness of the heart is likely to solve all of his problems like that until he just can't get the upper hand.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of ways to accomplish that without creating a ton of strenuous work for your team. I like bucket-of-powers ala Mummy and Demon. You can seperate those into categories and give an EXP reduction for your Seeming's category like Demon does with Embeds. You can also have Seeming-Specific Merits like B&amp;S does that adds special bonuses. You can even have Mantle (Seeming) if you want to copy that style wholecloth. Now you have some unique but minor bennies that say &quot;This Seeming is just -better- at this sort of thing&quot; and a set of powers it favors.<br /> <br /> Not enough? Have merits that modify Contracts. This lets you do exactly the same thing you are thinking of doing, but makes sure that you only have to do it when it makes sense instead of doing 5 options for each Contract.<br /> <br /> Not enough? Well, the powers are <i>Contracts</i> and you have Catches, which jive well with players. You can make it so that to learn an Out of Seeming contract, you <i>must</i> fulfill the Catch. Contracts in your Seeming are things you inherit or can just do. Contracts out of your Seeming are things you have to earn. If you go through the trouble of fulfilling an In-Seeming Contract's catch then you can use the power for free or get a + to it or something. As an aside, this makes Goblin Contracts easy--just make them Out of Seeming for everyone.<br /> <br /> You guys are great, and I'm sure you can think of options I haven't. Please don't take this as confrontational, but I think you should really explore your options and compare workload to benefit before committing yourself to that model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-19-2014, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:08:06-07:00","id":234346,"title":"","content":"Counter argument: Keys and Manifestations.<br /> <br /> I just woke up, that's why it's short.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:21:12-07:00","id":234366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233818#post233818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s worth noting that the original Courts were defined by how the changeling responds to his Durance \u2014 which is quite similar to this new take on Seemings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Courts were always &quot;what do you do next&quot;. So that fits perfectly:<br /> <br /> Kiths were what your Keeper did.<br /> Seeming was how you escaped.<br /> Court is what you do next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:48:46-07:00","id":234401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234174#post234174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>They also mentioned they might have 1 seeming per contract who &quot;favour&quot; that contract. Who says the contract doesn't only work different for the ones favouring it, but then similar for all the others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:50:08-07:00","id":234402,"title":"","content":"So, I got a spin on the Darklings.<br /> <br /> Agency through exploitation, power from hiding.<br /> <br /> Darklings have a bad rep. Of course they do. the Darklings are the ones who got, well, dark with their escape methods. All changelings are opportunists by necessity, but the Darklings are definitely opportunists by choice. Whether they tripped their companion while running or talked another changeling into doing something that would upset the Strangers before running away, whether they spread whispers of the Stranger's banes being known, or, hell, even threatening them with nothing but an empty bag and some dark words, the Darklings would lie, cheat, extort, threaten, and take advantage of anything-or anyone-to get out. It requires killing the soul a little bit, snuffing out some of the humanity in their soul, and that light never really comes back. More so than anyone else, the Darklings are the ones who <i>cheat the game</i>-or perhaps, more accurately, they cheat the<i> players</i> of the game, both willing and unwilling.<br /> <br /> How's that?<br /> <br /> I have two variations for the Elementals on the entire game line, I'm still pondering them as a whole. &quot;Those who become the game/Those who change the game&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:15:48-07:00","id":234425,"title":"","content":"Do you want to consign an entire seeming and the stealth/subterfuge playstyle to being uncomfortably like the Keepers?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what I think of that... though I still think sacrificed something to escape was my favorite of the proposed Darkling spins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:23:18-07:00","id":234431,"title":"","content":"Did you miss the part where the devs opening thought was &quot;Betrayal&quot;?<br /> <br /> Did you miss the part how Ogres Get agency through bloody, gorey, scary as shit violence?<br /> <br /> Did you miss the part how the Fairest escape <i>by playing the same game as the Strangers</i>?<br /> <br /> There's kind of an uncomfortable thing going on here, but it's been consistent.<br /> <br /> Anyways, this is where the idea of power comes in-once they've exercised agency, they can lay off the hardcore stuff. It's a part of them, but an Ogre who escapes doesn't have to be continually violent, but now knows the value of might, of having that as an option. They become the bigguy, andcan become the lovable guy as well,because he's not as paranoid now-he feels safe having gained might. A Fairest can let loose a little, and the Darkling's don't need to exploit, they just need to hide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-19-2014, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:38:03-07:00","id":234439,"title":"","content":"I really adore the ideas being presented in this thread, and I really think that the second edition of Changeling will be just as awesome as the first. But, I do have just one question about how your Seeming is how you escaped.<br /> <br /> It's rare, but mentioned a few times in Changeling, that some people don't as much escape, as are let go. If they made an oath with their Keeper unwittingly before they were taken, such as to only stay for a single night (a night that lasts for eternity in Arcadia) but the Changeling messes with some symbolism and tricks the Changeling hung in the sky as the moon to come down, effectively ending night, that seems like it would be a Fairest or a Darkling, escaping through social allure and treachery. But, what if a Keeper just lets someone go?<br /> <br /> In our game, we have someone who's Keeper grew bored of him, and playing in a 'relationship' mimicking courtly love, and sent him out to the world to do as he wished. To try to find a favor to gift to her, to win her back. Would that be an example of someone without a Seeming? Since they have not taken agency of their own escape and it is more of something that just... happened one day?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:45:09-07:00","id":234451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234439#post234439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really adore the ideas being presented in this thread, and I really think that the second edition of Changeling will be just as awesome as the first. But, I do have just one question about how your Seeming is how you escaped.<br /> <br /> It's rare, but mentioned a few times in Changeling, that some people don't as much escape, as are let go. If they made an oath with their Keeper unwittingly before they were taken, such as to only stay for a single night (a night that lasts for eternity in Arcadia) but the Changeling messes with some symbolism and tricks the Changeling hung in the sky as the moon to come down, effectively ending night, that seems like it would be a Fairest or a Darkling, escaping through social allure and treachery. But, what if a Keeper just lets someone go?<br /> <br /> In our game, we have someone who's Keeper grew bored of him, and playing in a 'relationship' mimicking courtly love, and sent him out to the world to do as he wished. To try to find a favor to gift to her, to win her back. Would that be an example of someone without a Seeming? Since they have not taken agency of their own escape and it is more of something that just... happened one day?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to give thoughts to this one, wouldn't a Keeper growing bored of you possibly be something the Changeling causes? <br /> <br /> Also, its worth noting frequently letting a Changeling go may very well to hunt them later. Heck, maybe the True Fae chases them to begin the hunt, all things considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:49:53-07:00","id":234459,"title":"","content":"You know, I realize that it's a real possibility and it plays into the paranoia aspect and that changelings would think it anyways?<br /> <br /> But <i>goddamn</i> do I hate the entire &quot;They could have been let go&quot; argument. It's like, in a single line, you castrate the entire character type and instantly diminish their achievements-which for a game about survivors is a big freaking deal!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:52:36-07:00","id":234463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234402#post234402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I got a spin on the Darklings.<br /> <br /> Agency through exploitation, power from hiding.<br /> <br /> Darklings have a bad rep. Of course they do. the Darklings are the ones who got, well, dark with their escape methods. All changelings are opportunists by necessity, but the Darklings are definitely opportunists by choice. Whether they tripped their companion while running or talked another changeling into doing something that would upset the Strangers before running away, whether they spread whispers of the Stranger's banes being known, or, hell, even threatening them with nothing but an empty bag and some dark words, the Darklings would lie, cheat, extort, threaten, and take advantage of anything-or anyone-to get out. It requires killing the soul a little bit, snuffing out some of the humanity in their soul, and that light never really comes back. More so than anyone else, the Darklings are the ones who <i>cheat the game</i>-or perhaps, more accurately, they cheat the<i> players</i> of the game, both willing and unwilling.<br /> <br /> How's that?<br /> <br /> I have two variations for the Elementals on the entire game line, I'm still pondering them as a whole. &quot;Those who become the game/Those who change the game&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far my favorite Darkling is them causing mistrust, like paranoia, and hence, using Fear as their get out of Arcadia card. Exploitation feels like something every Seeming should be equally capable of, and even equally suspected of. I say the latter because it'd be interesting if the Changelings have a reputation as con artists for justifiable reasons. <br /> <br /> Elementals I can't wait to hear about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:57:25-07:00","id":234469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234431#post234431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, this is where the idea of power comes in-once they've exercised agency, they can lay off the hardcore stuff. It's a part of them, but an Ogre who escapes doesn't have to be continually violent, but now knows the value of might, of having that as an option. They become the bigguy, andcan become the lovable guy as well,because he's not as paranoid now-he feels safe having gained might. A Fairest can let loose a little, and the Darkling's don't need to exploit, they just need to hide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, judging by some themes from 1.0, and the Betrayal thing, they may have to continue being hardcore, depending. I mean, Changelings were frequently depicted as being paranoid wrecks, part of that could be using extreme methods when they aren't eve necessary. <br /> <br /> Hey, a Seeming isn't all roses, to say the least, part of that could be learning a behavior that worked in Arcadia, but can get rather extreme in the real world. Especially if they think Arcadia is trying to get them back, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:01:48-07:00","id":234495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234469#post234469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, judging by some themes from 1.0, and the Betrayal thing, they may have to continue being hardcore, depending. I mean, Changelings were frequently depicted as being paranoid wrecks, part of that could be using extreme methods when they aren't eve necessary.<br /> <br /> Hey, a Seeming isn't all roses, to say the least, part of that could be learning a behavior that worked in Arcadia, but can get rather extreme in the real world. Especially if they think Arcadia is trying to get them back, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you never forget the reason you escaped. It's the sort of thing that haunts you, and once you've found out freedom lies behind a certain style of action, it's tempting to rely on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:14:34-07:00","id":234520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234431#post234431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you miss the part where the devs opening thought was &quot;Betrayal&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly using this as a jumping off point:<br /> <br /> I think that is -- and some of the derivatives are -- still what people are focused on. As you said, it's kind of uncomfortable. It may feel to many like taking options away. Before, one could have a character with all the aesthetics that Darklings have, without seeing it as the game insisting they have a moral judgment in their backstory. I think getting people not to read it that way may be a hard sell. It's not to say there isn't a fascinating wealth of story and character options to explore there.* But I can understand people feeling like they're losing more than they're gaining on this. Certainly, of all I've heard -- while I still need to digest some of it -- this is the first thing that gives me pause.<br /> <br /> * A character may hate himself for making that call, and resolve to be as morally upright and outstanding as he knows how to make up for it, even if he's sure he never can.<br /> <br /> I mean, if it's now a certainty that the Darkling betrayed someone, that changes the social context around them tremendously. Changelings are already rather paranoid sorts. Many are likely to see past behavior as a predictor of future behavior, and that creates <i>huge</i> barriers to trust a Darkling character. Again, it's got interesting possibilities -- makes it all the more meaningful when a Darkling wins that trust -- but it lays out a particular area of stories that I'm not sure everyone who likes the Darkling aesthetics wants to explore in that way.<br /> <br /> That's part of why I'm not sure laying down one overriding means of escape that a particular Seeming represents is the way to go. Doing something dark, dirty, and underhanded to get out feels like it fits Darklings to a tee and gives a broad swatch of possibilities. But definitively making it &quot;betrayal&quot; feels like it's too narrow, in a way that will turn off too many people. If there are concerns that giving Seemings broad possibilities will overlap in places, I don't see that as a bad thing. Players and Storytellers can pick whichever of the Seemings makes the best fit for the character's story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor tweaking. 08-19-2014, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:22:36-07:00","id":234530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234520#post234520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mainly using this as a jumping off point:<br /> <br /> I think that is -- and some of the derivatives are -- still what people are focused on. As you said, it's kind of uncomfortable. It may feel to many like taking options away. Before, one could have a character with all the aesthetics that Darklings have, without seeing it as the game insisting they have a moral judgment in their backstory. I think getting people not to read it that way may be a hard sell. It's not to say there isn't a fascinating wealth of story and character options to explore there.* But I can understand people feeling like they're losing more than they're gaining on this. Certainly, of all I've heard -- while I still need to digest some of it -- this is the first thing that gives me pause.<br /> <br /> * A character may hate himself for making that call, and resolve to be as morally upright and outstanding as he knows how to make up for it, even if he's sure he never can.<br /> <br /> I mean, if it's now a certainty that the Darkling betrayed someone, that changes the social context around them tremendously. Changelings are already rather paranoid sorts. Many are likely to see past behavior as a predictor of future behavior, and that creates <i>huge</i> barriers to trust a Darkling character. Again, it's got interesting possibilities -- makes it all the more meaningful when a Darkling wins that trust -- but it lays out a particular area of stories that I'm not sure everyone who likes the Darkling aesthetics wants to explore in that way.<br /> <br /> That's part of why I'm not sure laying down one overriding means of escape that a particular Seeming represents is the way to go. Doing something dark, dirty, and underhanded to get out feels like it fits Darklings to a tee and gives a broad swatch of possibilities. But definitively making it &quot;betrayal&quot; feels like it's too narrow, in a way that will turn off too many people. If there are concerns that giving Seemings broad possibilities will overlap in places, I don't see that as a bad thing. Players and Storytellers can pick whichever of the Seemings makes the best fit for the character's story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its worth noting, in 1.0... well, Changelings are supposed to paranoid. Really paranoid. Giving more reasons to fuel that isn't necessarily a bad thing. <br /> <br /> But really, I don't quite see Darklings being unique in betrayal, rather in using fear to get out(in this case, propagating fear of others.) I see ALL of the Seemings having had to do some... dark things to get out of Arcadia, many of which are things they may feel guilty over later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:29:17-07:00","id":234535,"title":"","content":"THis is part of the reason I went with exploitation, the idea that they cheat the game. It could mean other changelings, but it could mean that they did the equivalent of hiding cards or lying about rules. It could mean they exploited the True Fae, making them afraid or misled or confused. It could mean taking cheating the domain. Could mean blackmailing hobgoblins. Could mean tripping changelings.<br /> <br /> I felt like exploitation had a range, from the DnD &quot;Oh, they do what rogues do&quot; to &quot;OMG, these people are all con men and traitors&quot;. There's room for heroic exploitation and horrific exploitation. I also felt like that idea neatly encompassed many of the ideas put forth here.<br /> <br /> Of course, one thing about Darklings is that they've never been considered the most trustworthy. It's really bad in the Victorian Era, but even in Winter Masques they make a point of noting how people assume a Darkling is available to do the more morally ambiguous stuff. Hence another reason for exploitation as a uniting factor-if people know you took advantage of others before, why not do it again?<br /> <br /> On a different front, exploitation is a thingthey all do, but again, it's who or what's exploited. Wizened certainly exploit the system, but that's simply taking advantage of the Fae's rules and domains. A Darkling exploits aren't as informed, and what's more they are more inflicting than others. An Ogre beats, a Darkling steals, as it were.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I'm running with what makes sense to me until something better comes along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-19-2014, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:46:47-07:00","id":234546,"title":"","content":"See, here's the big thing: if Seemings are when you grab the reins, that the actions that tie into them need a certain drastic-ness to them. Victims often feel like they need to go to extremes, and in the case of Changelings, they really do. THey have to do something that jerks control out from Them long enough to escape, and that often requires the heights and depths of what a changeling can convince themselves to do. It's part of the reason why they debate if they were let go or not-if they had to go <i>that far </i>just to get out, how do they even know if it's enough? It's also part of the reason they end up falling into the cycle, too-when you learn the extremes solve your problems,you tend to use them a lot.<br /> <br /> The feeling of drasticality or whatever the correct word is goes to different places, of course.Lots of changelings play the long game. The important thing to remember is that long games are often desperate, thread-thin shots that can easily fall apart. They are fraught with failure,and therefore drastic in their execution. They're tension ridden things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:36:05-07:00","id":234798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234459#post234459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I realize that it's a real possibility and it plays into the paranoia aspect and that changelings would think it anyways?<br /> <br /> But <i>goddamn</i> do I hate the entire &quot;They could have been let go&quot; argument. It's like, in a single line, you castrate the entire character type and instantly diminish their achievements-which for a game about survivors is a big freaking deal!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In counterpoint though, I'm okay with &quot;You thought you were let go. And that's why you have no Seeming&quot;. <br /> <br /> Without getting into a huge, extended post, I think that's a tragic but reasonable response from a survivor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:10:24-07:00","id":234818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233522#post233522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It means there's no default assumption of mantles and courts. Which may or may not be a big deal in your games.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, this is actually important to me because I've had some less than constructive experiences with people who stubbornly insist that the seasonal courts are the only true courts, even if they would otherwise not make sense in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:25:40-07:00","id":234825,"title":"","content":"This is just a very simple look here, but in the end, to me... Kith is <b>WHAT</b> you are while Seeming is <b>WHO</b> you are. Kith is a slice of you that you really had no (or at least very little) choice in. But Seeming is a VERY PERSONAL thing... it says something about you. What you feel your strengths are, what your strengths really are, where you try to go mentally to solve problems... (even if it's just to think &quot;Hey, if I punch this guy... right... <b>NOW!</b> I can escape!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:32:05-07:00","id":234828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234798#post234798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In counterpoint though, I'm okay with &quot;You thought you were let go. And that's why you have no Seeming&quot;.<br /> <br /> Without getting into a huge, extended post, I think that's a tragic but reasonable response from a survivor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't get me wrong-it's never an aspect I would remove, and as an explanation for the No Seeming merit it's great.<br /> <br /> It's just -gah, I can know something has a good place and purpose in the discussion, and still not like it personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:34:55-07:00","id":234830,"title":"","content":"If everyone agreed on everything always ArcaneArts, the world would be a pretty boring place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:41:19-07:00","id":234833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234830#post234830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If everyone agreed on everything always ArcaneArts, the world would be a pretty boring place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't I know it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:20:41-07:00","id":234863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234818#post234818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an aside, this is actually important to me because I've had some less than constructive experiences with people who stubbornly insist that the seasonal courts are the only true courts, even if they would otherwise not make sense in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Me too. And most of my team. And I've heard a lot of people grumble and refuse to play games with other Courts, because there just wasn't enough to make them work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:26:45-07:00","id":234873,"title":"","content":"Being &quot;let go&quot; as a thing for No Seeming could be cool.<br /> <br /> <b>@Killer </b><br /> <br /> Re: Beast.<br /> Been trying to find a niche for Beast that isn't &quot;I am an animal,&quot; which would now be handled more by Kiths. Circling back to fables and fairytales for inspiration, being turned into an animal was rarely a good thing. It usually denoted a curse, a loss of humanity, or something similar. So a theme of degredation or losing something boiled to the surface. But Seemings can't be about losing something, they are about agency and empowerment! So how can you lose something but it represent agency? If you give/trade it away.<br /> <br /> Re: Darkling<br /> There is a difference between &quot;contains running&quot; and running defining the escape from the durance. Darklings didn't play the Fae's games or try to conquer them or figure out the rules. They took the first opportunity they had to get the hell out of dodge.<br /> <br /> Re: Elementals<br /> I don't feel being socially inept is an important or evocative enough concept to be worth preserving.<br /> <br /> Re: Wizened<br /> Technically in that writeup expertise would fall under Ogre, not Wizened.<br /> <br /> <b>@ArcaneArts:</b><br /> Counter-Counter point. Keys and Manifestations. Single(-ish) book Splat vs Splat designed to sell more than one book.<br /> <br /> That said, its a tangential conversation, so I don't want to waste too much discussion on the topic in this particular thread.<br /> <br /> <b>AN IDEA</b><br /> <br /> So. I have a smidge of a game I think may really help with this. Why don't people post example Durances (like a paragraph, two at most) that lend themselves strongly to a Kith. Lets say one of the current Kiths because we don't know the new ones, just for the sake of example. Then post how you feel each Seeming would escape from that exact same durance. Then we can start looking for emerging trends.<br /> <br /> Note: If you want to just put a Durance without how each Seeming solves it, that's actually better because...<br /> Bonus Points: Post how each Seeming escapes from someone else's Durance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:42:30-07:00","id":234888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234346#post234346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counter argument: Keys and Manifestations.<br /> <br /> I just woke up, that's why it's short.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a good counter point. Geist has the worst, most non-intuitive system in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:45:26-07:00","id":234892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233532#post233532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and let me put it this way.<br /> <br /> Kith is what happened to you. Seeming is your agency. It represents the moment you took control away from your victimizer.<br /> <br /> Lost is a game about survivors. Seeming is one of a few ways we really emphasize the characters' agency and human spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I'm still catching up as I post this (Like page 10), but I've got an argument for Primal being the aspect of agency.<br /> <br /> The other seemings involved changing, challenging or carving a way out, a Primal (Sorry about the name, it was the best I could think of) embraces the Keeper's story, owning your Durance and becoming so divorced from humanity that you willingly became part of the Keeper's story. You reveled in your role, becoming the best rock thing, the best bird, the perfect Big Bad Wolf; you did so well in fact that as time went on you twisted yourself without the Keeper even having to do anything. The story would be better if the lion attacked the hunting party at the beginning, and stalked them across the savannah instead of hiding from them the whole time. You chose to burn the orphanage, because it created more drama. You lost your humanity, gave it up, became a Primal aspect of the story. Maybe your keeper grew bored with a willing toy, or maybe you were just waiting, learning the story before making your escape. Whatever it is, by willingly giving up your own human nature you were able to find a way out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:51:09-07:00","id":234900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234828#post234828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, don't get me wrong-it's never an aspect I would remove, and as an explanation for the No Seeming merit it's great.<br /> <br /> It's just -gah, I can know something has a good place and purpose in the discussion, and still not like it personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, it depends on the situation. The character I have that has No Seeming has because he was out hunting with a few of his friends before his Wedding night and ended up getting finding a prey which was driving him to hunt it. He spent months hunting it, in a fugue state. He failed over and over again. One day he realized he had to go home and did so not really knowing what had happened but it was rather quick and abrupt. It was neither a positive or negative experience just a rather jarring one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:53:45-07:00","id":234903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234892#post234892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, I'm still catching up as I post this (Like page 10), but I've got an argument for Primal being the aspect of agency.<br /> <br /> The other seemings involved changing, challenging or carving a way out, a Primal (Sorry about the name, it was the best I could think of) embraces the Keeper's story, owning your Durance and becoming so divorced from humanity that you willingly became part of the Keeper's story. You reveled in your role, becoming the best rock thing, the best bird, the perfect Big Bad Wolf; you did so well in fact that as time went on you twisted yourself without the Keeper even having to do anything. The story would be better if the lion attacked the hunting party at the beginning, and stalked them across the savannah instead of hiding from them the whole time. You chose to burn the orphanage, because it created more drama. You lost your humanity, gave it up, became a Primal aspect of the story. Maybe your keeper grew bored with a willing toy, or maybe you were just waiting, learning the story before making your escape. Whatever it is, by willingly giving up your own human nature you were able to find a way out</div> </div> </div> </div>That's...not a PC character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:57:50-07:00","id":234905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234888#post234888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a good counter point. Geist has the worst, most non-intuitive system in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a point we'll disagree on later. I semi-agree with Gambit, in that I don't think now's the time. Suffice it to say I have a different opinion and (pointed at Gambit)that I don't think saying a gameline that only had one book is a convincing argument destroyer-particularly when said gameline was designed to only have one book anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T19:02:46-07:00","id":234908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234905#post234905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a point we'll disagree on later. I semi-agree with Gambit, in that I don't think now's the time. Suffice it to say I have a different opinion and (pointed at Gambit)that I don't think saying a gameline that only had one book is a convincing argument destroyer-particularly when said gameline was designed to only have one book anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And technically ended with TWO books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T19:15:47-07:00","id":234918,"title":"","content":"To clarify: My point was not that Manifestations and Keys somehow &quot;ruined Geist.&quot; My point is that a gameline designed to have multiple books has a different set of needs from a gameline intended to run one or two books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T19:30:08-07:00","id":234926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234903#post234903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's...not a PC character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that it iss a great point to start a character. You had to sacrifice your very core for the even chance at freedom; had to give in and hope that it would pay off in the end. You lost yourself to escape, but now that you're free where do you start rebuilding? You became something primal, something ruled by instinct because you had to but now that you're free you have to live with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T19:48:05-07:00","id":234935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234926#post234926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that it iss a great point to start a character. You had to sacrifice your very core for the even chance at freedom; had to give in and hope that it would pay off in the end. You lost yourself to escape, but now that you're free where do you start rebuilding? You became something primal, something ruled by instinct because you had to but now that you're free you have to live with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean it's not what PC's are.<br /> <br /> Whether marked by their own success or the play of Others, PC Changelings are marked <i>by the desire to escape</i>. Even if they don't really have the ability, really, to do it, <i>player characters are the ones who said &quot;Enough of this shit&quot;.</i> The ones who embrace what's been given them are the ones who become loyalists, privateers at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-19-2014, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T20:43:39-07:00","id":234982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234798#post234798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In counterpoint though, I'm okay with &quot;You thought you were let go. And that's why you have no Seeming&quot;.<br /> <br /> Without getting into a huge, extended post, I think that's a tragic but reasonable response from a survivor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I misread this earlier, so some clarification:<br /> <br /> I am okay with changelings <i>thinking</i> they were let go. That's a big part of the game, the hit to self-esteem, the doubt, the fear, and the struggle to deal with that. And I can see how that could definitely become so overriding that it becomes the No Seeming Merit.<br /> <br /> Where the castration comes in is when Keepers <i>actually</i> let them go-but really, it's more the way some people use these cases, deliberately or not, as something to inform <i>all</i> changelings.EDIT: This has happened enough that I have a kneejerk reaction against people saying &quot;But sometimes they're let go&quot;. Yes, sometimes they are let go, but clearly not all the time.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that having Keepers letting changelings go without any impetus on the Changeling's part doesn't have a place in this game-because it really does, and I'd never keep it out of the game. But I don't like it, and I don't like the way it gets used in conversations sometimes. And that might be being dumb and oversensitive on it, but still-blegh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-19-2014, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T22:27:27-07:00","id":235059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233069#post233069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds more like an Elemental Render; it's so impersoanl. A Hunterheart, no matter the seeming, &quot;hunts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wildfire that chases you through the woods, cracking twigs and splitting trees manic and cruel laughter. The tornado that descends like the feet of an angry god and rampages across your homes like a toddler. The sandstorm running slipshod across your encampment, trampling like a herd of horses. The thun'drous stalker who follows silent and invisible, detectable only as a charge of static and scent of ozone before you are struck and electrocuted as if by a descending hawk.<br /> <br /> Where there is humanity, there are stories. Where there are stories, nature has been anthropomorphised. Where nature has been made manlike, it can be made animal-like. Neptune's frothing white chargers, say.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I believe, until a writer comes up with gold, it's best to work with them as separate. The key difference between the two is that a Beast and an Elemental have different narratives. Identical construction of kith, seeming and build will still fundamentally point to different perspectives.<br /> <br /> A hunter heart elemental is a predatory force of nature. A hunter heart beast is a reflection of human nature. It's the difference between &quot;the mountains don't care. If you're out after dark, you will freeze and die&quot; and &quot;the wolf must hunt&quot;. An elemental hunter heart could be lightning which strikes the tallest, cutting all things down. A beast hunter heart could have spent it's durance thinking it was a thunderbird. Identical build and thematics, very different stories.<br /> <br /> E: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233221#post233221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;be a shark (or a fish or an octopus or seal&amp;quot; is only different from &amp;quot;be a mermaid or a selkie&amp;quot; in the seeming-related flavor. If you've decided to &amp;quot;be a shark&amp;quot;, but as a Fairest, that would be like a fierce warrior mermaid with a shark tail and sharp teeth, really.<br /> <br /> I'm going to slide in with the &amp;quot;Don't push Beast and Elemental into the same role&amp;quot;, because, like Heavy Arms said (which is actually a pretty good answer to Dataweaver's question? So it seems like it got missed by some people, I think), Beasts and Elemental are operating on a much different difference than just &amp;quot;animal&amp;quot; versus &amp;quot;human&amp;quot; -- Elementals are practically <i>defined</i> by how they can't relate to normal people, or even sentient things anymore, while Beasts are defined by how much more alive they are than the people around them.<br /> <br /> The real problem, mechanically speaking, to me is that Beasts get a <i>bonus</i> to interacting with living creatures -- they get 8 again and a free specialty to interacting with animals, and can spend glamour to increase dice pools based around Presence and Composure. The only people who are better than Beasts at dealing with people are Fairest, and this is actually stated in the Beast write-up for Winter Masques.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Elementals are actually worse at dealing with people than Wizened are. They don't get the ten again on rolls involving Manipulation, Empathy, Expression, Persuasion OR Socialize unless it's to with the elements. People are talking about how the proposal for Hunterheart Elementals are too impersonal, and not <i>hunting</i> enough, and that's the thing about Elementals. They ARE impersonal. A hunterheart would be the blizzard no one could run from, sneaker waves from the ocean, lightning that doesn't need to strike twice because the first strike left it's target dead. The scary thing about it is that when it's on your scent, you can't shake it and you can't beat it, you just have to hope it get what it wants and you manage to survive.<br /> <br /> Leave the &amp;quot;personal&amp;quot; to the beasts -- Elementals just get the job done.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Woops~ I knew I should have finished reading through the thread before posting. Got too excited, but I'll probably edit further once I finish reading AA's post! ^w^;;<br /> <br /> Double Edit: Even after reading that, I still don't think I like conflating Beast and Elemental, but it does make a lot of sense. . . . I might have more to say later, though~</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. The difference is between a Wolf as a sexual predator metaphor with his animal magnetism, say, or the utter implacability of an elemental with the same seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3652,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3652-siuis","user":"SiuiS","date":". 08-20-2014, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3652-siuis","name":"SiuiS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T01:12:42-07:00","id":235162,"title":"","content":"After reading all the 15 pages I somehow still can't see merging Elemental and Beast into Primal as a good option. Seems to have more cons than pros tbh.<br /> <br /> I would probably integrate Beasts into Ogres, and maybe even the other way, as the &quot;Beasts&quot; is a more generic name. They're both focused on physical attributes, both have animal/monster characteristics. It's like the only difference is that the beasts are &quot;sexy monsters&quot; and the ogres are &quot;violent monsters&quot; and that the former are focused on real animals and latter on fantasy creatures. With the main focus kept on kiths anyway I see no harm in putting them into larger category containing all wild, dangerous, physical and animalistic things, both fantasy and mundane.<br /> <br /> Then for more clarity I would split Elementals into Nature Forces and Inanimate constructs. Former are primal forces, elements, flora, weather, energy. Latter are objects, constructs, machines and items. They're too different to work together.<br /> <br /> I can't make any more clear thematic distinction between those three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1969-alexander","name":"Alexander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1969_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T03:09:55-07:00","id":235250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234982#post234982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I misread this earlier, so some clarification:<br /> <br /> I am okay with changelings <i>thinking</i> they were let go. That's a big part of the game, the hit to self-esteem, the doubt, the fear, and the struggle to deal with that. And I can see how that could definitely become so overriding that it becomes the No Seeming Merit.<br /> <br /> Where the castration comes in is when Keepers <i>actually</i> let them go-but really, it's more the way some people use these cases, deliberately or not, as something to inform <i>all</i> changelings.EDIT: This has happened enough that I have a kneejerk reaction against people saying &quot;But sometimes they're let go&quot;. Yes, sometimes they are let go, but clearly not all the time.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that having Keepers letting changelings go without any impetus on the Changeling's part doesn't have a place in this game-because it really does, and I'd never keep it out of the game. But I don't like it, and I don't like the way it gets used in conversations sometimes. And that might be being dumb and oversensitive on it, but still-blegh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I totally agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T03:19:41-07:00","id":235252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &gt; Kith is what happened to you. Seeming is your agency. It represents the moment you took control away from your victimizer. <br /> &gt; Lost is a game about survivors. Seeming is one of a few ways we really emphasize the characters' agency and human spirit. </div> </div> </div>so, first we define what kind of abuse our abuse victim went through, and then how he/she copes with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T03:24:12-07:00","id":235254,"title":"","content":"So, I'm wondering, under this new definition of Seemings, wouldn't most Loyalists lack one? Not that this is a bad thing, really, and doesn't account for Privateers, but logically this would place those Changelings without Seemings under extreme suspicion. Again, not a bad thing, but it would seem to have some pretty concrete effects on the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T05:06:28-07:00","id":235314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=235252#post235252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so, first we define what kind of abuse our abuse victim went through, and then how he/she copes with it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a little more complicated than that. But we're talking in pretty simplified terms here. So more or less? <br /> <br /> It's not always abuse though. The Lost are Survivors. It's not just abuse. There's a spectrum. Kith is where your identity was challenged and compromised. Your Seeming is how you took it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T05:08:06-07:00","id":235315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=235254#post235254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm wondering, under this new definition of Seemings, wouldn't most Loyalists lack one? Not that this is a bad thing, really, and doesn't account for Privateers, but logically this would place those Changelings without Seemings under extreme suspicion. Again, not a bad thing, but it would seem to have some pretty concrete effects on the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=235254#post235254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm wondering, under this new definition of Seemings, wouldn't most Loyalists lack one? Not that this is a bad thing, really, and doesn't account for Privateers, but logically this would place those Changelings without Seemings under extreme suspicion. Again, not a bad thing, but it would seem to have some pretty concrete effects on the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm working with the assumption that Seeming isn't always something you wear on your sleeve. Because it's a shift on your Kith, it's not always immediately evident. I could certainly see some people looking for it. But, too much scrutiny puts the scrutinizer under scrutiny. If you're investigating people and poking too deep into their affairs, who's to say you're not a Loyalist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T05:16:32-07:00","id":235319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a little more complicated than that. But we're talking in pretty simplified terms here. So more or less? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a simple metaphor, nothing more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T08:59:04-07:00","id":235444,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I work well with examples. I understand it might be too early for you to be ready or comfortable with giving some (might skew discussion, and there's already so much we know about in flux)*, but I'm curious. On the &quot;different Seemings access/use Contracts differently, through some undetermined way,&quot; could you give an example of a couple of Contracts/Clauses you're reasonably sure will be similar, and how you're thinking the relevant Seeming might get less out of it or be barred from it?<br /> <br /> * How contracts work, how Seemings and Kiths work and what they mean, etc.<br /> <br /> As a somewhat broader question, I think you've mentioned the Kith will be more potent than it's been. I remember hearing some talk over the years that Changeling as a splat was intended to be set at a lower &quot;power level&quot; relative to others, in strict terms. That's sort of the crux of the rest of this post, so please disregard this entire spiel here if I'm off-base on this point. I just remember hearing it as an explanation for why Changelings don't get, say, any sort of &quot;turn someone into a frog&quot; or similar powers. There's also been observation in this thread about how some of the Seeming/Kith blessings have been, well... a little unimpressive (that water-breathing example). I come from an Exalted background, where an excessive level of strictness has been a source of frustration. I've been encouraged by the new line from the devs for 3rd edition: some splats will still be broadly stronger than others, which is fine, but they're not generally going to be denied something if it's appropriate for them to have it, even if that particular thing is stronger than a &quot;more powerful&quot; splat gets. Basically, I'm wondering if you have a similar holistic plan for Changeling, that the first consideration for what Changelings can do and should be is what's appropriate for their themes and nature, and what will be fun and cool for them as a gameline. Concern about where they stand relative to other WoD splats isn't unimportant, but I feel it should be secondary.<br /> <br /> Again, going off of hearsay that may well be nothing, but figured it couldn't hurt to raise the point. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T16:36:20-07:00","id":235882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=235444#post235444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a somewhat broader question, I think you've mentioned the Kith will be more potent than it's been. I remember hearing some talk over the years that Changeling as a splat was intended to be set at a lower &quot;power level&quot; relative to others, in strict terms. That's sort of the crux of the rest of this post, so please disregard this entire spiel here if I'm off-base on this point. I just remember hearing it as an explanation for why Changelings don't get, say, any sort of &quot;turn someone into a frog&quot; or similar powers. There's also been observation in this thread about how some of the Seeming/Kith blessings have been, well... a little unimpressive (that water-breathing example). I come from an Exalted background, where an excessive level of strictness has been a source of frustration. I've been encouraged by the new line from the devs for 3rd edition: some splats will still be broadly stronger than others, which is fine, but they're not generally going to be denied something if it's appropriate for them to have it, even if that particular thing is stronger than a &quot;more powerful&quot; splat gets. Basically, I'm wondering if you have a similar holistic plan for Changeling, that the first consideration for what Changelings can do and should be is what's appropriate for their themes and nature, and what will be fun and cool for them as a gameline. Concern about where they stand relative to other WoD splats isn't unimportant, but I feel it should be secondary.<br /> <br /> Again, going off of hearsay that may well be nothing, but figured it couldn't hurt to raise the point. &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really complicated question. I could probably write a book answering it. Everything's dials. My team is discussing 100 dials right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:05:00-07:00","id":236001,"title":"","content":"It's frustrating to keep running into the same walls with Beasts and Elementals.<br /> <br /> On a different score, Dave, any of this thread been useful?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:49:00-07:00","id":236037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=236001#post236001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's frustrating to keep running into the same walls with Beasts and Elementals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you. I <i>like</i> them as separate, and feel there are two distinct concepts between them that would differ from the other Seemings. But it's hard to tell if my fondness for them as separate is blinding me, or if I'm just not coming up with a good way to articulate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a different score, Dave, any of this thread been useful? </div> </div> </div>Aye, I'm curious, too. Additionally, are there any ideas or notions it's given you? Any particular angles you'd like to see munched over in the Seeming/Kith arena?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T19:17:16-07:00","id":236063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=236001#post236001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's frustrating to keep running into the same walls with Beasts and Elementals.<br /> <br /> On a different score, Dave, any of this thread been useful?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's been immensely helpful. I don't think I'm merging Beasts and Elementals, because I'm afraid Dymphna might kill me. While I can't say what changes and ideas I might or might not be implementing, I've read everything here, and I'm going to be direct linking this thread in my outline for whomever ends up writing the basic Kith/Seeming stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T19:30:57-07:00","id":236069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=236001#post236001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's frustrating to keep running into the same walls with Beasts and Elementals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main issue with Beasts and Elementals is that back in 1.0, the other seemings were defined by what you <i>did</i>, while Beasts and Elementals were defined by what you <i>were</i>. So its easier to draw a line from the other seemings to a method of escape/expression of agency. IE - Darklings sneak, Fairest manipulate, Ogres smash, Wizened plan. It's harder to nail down a single unifying concept as to how Beasts or Elementals would escape or assert their agency because those seeming are more about passive identity. Also, I feel like the big reason nobody wants to delete or change these seemings up <i>too</i> much is because now that seemings color your character, adding Beast or Elemental stuff to a player's character is going to be in pretty high demand (Why have a regular dragonwoman when you can have a dragon woman made of VOLCANOES?!) specifically because those two seemings would have the most broad/drastic choice of physical alterations. Which, thinking on it, may be an issue of its own.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think just up and mashing the two into a singular <i>~*NATURE JUNK*~</i> seeming just sounds kind of silly and a little <i>too</i> broad a concept.<br /> <br /> On another note, my other concern with turning seemings into an expression of your humanity/agency is that a major theme (at least of 1.0) was that all your changes were <i>forced</i> on you, with the <i>courts</i> acting as the expressions of humanity/agency. So I'm hoping the writers find a way to reconcile that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T19:40:48-07:00","id":236090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=236063#post236063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's been immensely helpful. I don't think I'm merging Beasts and Elementals, because I'm afraid Dymphna might kill me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm amused at your reasoning here.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I'm glad. I'm not done ramming some of the questions about Beasts and Elementals in with my head yet, but it's nice to know that so far it hasn't all been sound and fury.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> *takes that thread and adds it to the loom*<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T19:42:13-07:00","id":236092,"title":"","content":"Nice summary, Illuminated Minutia. And yes, of all of the Seemings, Beast and Elemental are indeed the most likely to incorporate some sort of physical change into your escape. However they get differentiated from each other, they <i>do</i> have that in common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T20:07:05-07:00","id":236115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=236069#post236069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, my other concern with turning seemings into an expression of your humanity/agency is that a major theme (at least of 1.0) was that all your changes were <i>forced</i> on you, with the <i>courts</i> acting as the expressions of humanity/agency. So I'm hoping the writers find a way to reconcile that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Seeming is a result of your escape, but not a conscious choice necessarily. You didn't go in it knowing how it'd affect you. Perhaps coming out of it and realizing your quite possibly spur-of-the-moment choices have changed you forever could be very horrifying indeed, even if these changes are an expression of your agency, the way you took control back. I don't think you need to be too concerned.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T20:16:42-07:00","id":236126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=236069#post236069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main issue with Beasts and Elementals is that back in 1.0, the other seemings were defined by what you <i>did</i>, while Beasts and Elementals were defined by what you <i>were</i>. So its easier to draw a line from the other seemings to a method of escape/expression of agency. IE - Darklings sneak, Fairest manipulate, Ogres smash, Wizened plan. It's harder to nail down a single unifying concept as to how Beasts or Elementals would escape or assert their agency because those seeming are more about passive identity. Also, I feel like the big reason nobody wants to delete or change these seemings up <i>too</i> much is because now that seemings color your character, adding Beast or Elemental stuff to a player's character is going to be in pretty high demand (Why have a regular dragonwoman when you can have a dragon woman made of VOLCANOES?!) specifically because those two seemings would have the most broad/drastic choice of physical alterations. Which, thinking on it, may be an issue of its own.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think just up and mashing the two into a singular <i>~*NATURE JUNK*~</i> seeming just sounds kind of silly and a little <i>too</i> broad a concept.<br /> <br /> On another note, my other concern with turning seemings into an expression of your humanity/agency is that a major theme (at least of 1.0) was that all your changes were <i>forced</i> on you, with the <i>courts</i> acting as the expressions of humanity/agency. So I'm hoping the writers find a way to reconcile that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last gives me an idea that, might, help with the first. <br /> <br /> Namely, Changeling was always a game about dealing with trauma, well, part of that is adapting to it, which can be quite painful. Hence, my thought is Seemings would have a physical aspect, because you literally changed yourself to get out Arcadia, which could be a very painful process, even if it is an expression of your Agency. The ability or lack of to do this may even shape who can reasonably escape Arcadia. <br /> <br /> The last matters, as I remember with Fairest in 1.0, a theme at times was the confusing mix of pleasure and pain made it hard for them to even will themselves to leave Arcadia. Imagine if every Changeling has to go through an aspect of that, who has a Seeming mind you, from needing to accept the need to change yourself in a way that still won't make you human, just a compromise between your human and faire sides. <br /> <br /> Also? I don't really view Elementals as inherently tied to nature, but rather their surrounding Environment, even in the original(consider we later on got a freaking Pollution Elemental). To go to an example that isn't a building material, as I've used that before, consider someone turned into the water that fills a pipe. The water may technically be natural, but the environment it resides in is distinctly not, which is something I think that'd make the biggest impact on an Elemental. Point is, if they're connected to nature, it means the environment they were reborn in, if you will, was natural, but they can urban or unnatural in some other manner from coming from an environment encompassing such. <br /> Now, turning that into a form of Agency would be tricky, but I just want to remove nature as a necessity being an impediment, if that was the case with Elementals. <br /> <br /> Beasts, meanwhile, while being Nature, to me is also being Wild, which while certainly an aspect of Nature, isn't the only theme to explore there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T20:22:00-07:00","id":236130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=236115#post236115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your Seeming is a result of your escape, but not a conscious choice necessarily. You didn't go in it knowing how it'd affect you. Perhaps coming out of it and realizing your quite possibly spur-of-the-moment choices have changed you forever could be very horrifying indeed, even if these changes are an expression of your agency, the way you took control back. I don't think you need to be too concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. <br /> <br /> Also, consider that becoming a Seeming, in many ways is still forcing you, because you have to choose between accepting you can't be human anymore, or continuing under the never ending torment of your Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T21:01:53-07:00","id":236153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=234935#post234935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I mean it's not what PC's are.<br /> <br /> Whether marked by their own success or the play of Others, PC Changelings are marked <i>by the desire to escape</i>. Even if they don't really have the ability, really, to do it, <i>player characters are the ones who said &quot;Enough of this shit&quot;.</i> The ones who embrace what's been given them are the ones who become loyalists, privateers at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again. It really depends on the changeling. There's a focus on one type of Keeper; the very abusive/overly carrying keeper that tries to do everything to keep Changelings in arcadia. However, there's more than just one type of narrative. Having just one type of Fae with essentially the same personality doesn't make sense. Not all Fae should go for the same type of narrative. Not every Changeling is going to have the same or even a relatable position. You don't have to hate your time with the Fae in order to want to leave them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T09:16:24-07:00","id":236560,"title":"","content":"1. Darklings: Someone on page 12 hit on Darklings being defined by what they sacrificed to escape, and that resonated really well for me. I like that word. That is a good word. It brings the right image to the forefront--and your liar and sneaks could be those who gave up honor and integrity, willfully becoming \u2018the bad guys\u2019.<br /> <br /> 2. Wizened: Agency through expertise, and the line of thought following it, led me to the mental image of a group of changelings planning an escape with their individual skills given by their keeper\u2014the result in my head was similar to Ocean\u2019s Eleven. You\u2019ve got great actors, you\u2019ve got codemonkeys, you\u2019ve got a demolitions expert, you\u2019ve got a contortionist\u2026and all of them combine their skills to achieve their objective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T09:40:11-07:00","id":236581,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I thought on it a bit. I'm going to throw these out there. I tried to pick ideas that would put them in a similar place conceptually as in 1.0, with them being somewhat separated from the directness of the other seemings. (Elementals especially.)<br /> <br /> <b>Beasts</b> didn't escape alone. Whether its silently stalking after another escapee, following along with fellow slave out of a sense of loyalty, or protecting the ragged youngster as they make their way out, beasts are drawn to others in some way. Few animals are truly solitary, even predators seek out other creatures if only to feed. Beasts are social above all else, but they lack the manipulative aloofness of Fairest. They don't <i>use</i> others in the way a Fairest or Darkling might, though they may be used themselves. Their agency is defined by choosing to follow the escaping changeling and trusting that said changeling knows where they're going.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Elementals</b> escaped by realizing that they were never truly bound. All they had to do was let go of whatever was holding them back. They let go of their complicated &quot;self,&quot; becoming something more basic (more elemental, even), and simply leave. The escape itself can be violent or stealthy or what have you, but they are all defined by their relinquishing of their superfluous &quot;humanity&quot; and holding on to only the parts of themselves that really matter (What those parts are depend on the individual).<br /> To quote The Buddha: <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even so, monks, whatever isn't yours: Let go of it. Your letting go of it will be for your long-term welfare &amp; happiness. And what isn't yours? Form isn't yours... Feeling isn't yours... Perception... Thought fabrications... Consciousness isn't yours: Let go of it. Your letting go of it will be for your long-term welfare &amp; happiness. </div> </div> </div> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:22:14-07:00","id":236981,"title":"","content":"Hmm\u2026 I like the Elemental idea; but I think Beasts need their agency to be something more along the lines of \u201ctrust your instincts\u201d than \u201cfollow someone else out\u201d. Acid test: how well would these work if applied to a non-bestial, non-elemental Kith, such as the aforementioned Muse? <br /> <br /> Also, how well do the Blessing and Curse(?) of a Beast or an Elemental work when the Kith isn\u2019t bestial or elemental? I don\u2019t have my book handy, so I can\u2019t check on them myself. Do they work fine as is? Do they need some reinterpretation? Or do they need an overhaul? <br /> <br /> Finally: given this new setup where Seemings and Kiths can be mixed and matched: could we get an \u201cadjective form\u201d for every Seeming\u2019s name? \u201cFairest Muse\u201d rolls off the tongue, as does \u201cElemental Muse\u201d and \u201cWizened Muse\u201d; \u201cDarkling Muse\u201d strikesme as appropriate, too, though it\u2019s a bit more questionable; maybe they should also be called something like, I don\u2019t know, \u201cthe shadowed\u201d? \u201cBeast Muse\u201d is just awkward; but \u201cBestial Muse\u201d works fine<sup>*</sup>. \u201cOgre Muse\u201d just doesn\u2019t work at all, and \u201cOgrish\u201d just feels wrong.<hr />* For future reference, I intend to be very careful with my capitalization: \u201cBestial\u201d is the adjective form for the Beast Seeming; \u201cbestial\u201d is an adjective used to sungle out Kiths that have animal features.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-21-2014, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T13:35:32-07:00","id":237282,"title":"","content":"Seemings as Agency.<br /> <br /> Beasts<br /> The Ones Who Forgot Learning and Discovered the Freedom of Now<br /> <br /> <br /> Darklings<br /> The Ones Who Hid Their Hearts and Bent the Rules<br /> <br /> <br /> Elementals<br /> The Ones Who Shed Humanity and Breathe the Wyrd<br /> <br /> <br /> Fairest<br /> The Ones Who Believed and Lived as Fae<br /> <br /> <br /> Ogres<br /> The Ones Who Broke their Chains and Savaged the Rules<br /> <br /> <br /> Wizened<br /> The Ones Who Became Twisted and Married Magic<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T13:59:23-07:00","id":237293,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Blugh, quotes don't seem to be working for me at the moment. &gt;_&lt; Improvising! I'm trying to respond to Dataweaver's second paragraph in the most recent post.<br /> EDIT2: Or maybe not...? Let's try again...<br /> EDIT3: Nnnnnope, that just does not want to appear in there.<br /> <br /> @Dataweaver: I think the Seeming blessings/curses should probably change, just because of how they're approaching this topic. It sounds like each Kith is becoming more robust and has one variant per Seeming. I don't know if it would be too much, but I could see the Seeming's mechanical impact being tailored to the Kith. By which I mean that a Fairest Hunterheart and a Fairest Muse might each receive a different Blessing/Curse, dependent on the themes of the Kith. It almost sounded like each Seeming may modify whatever base power(s) the Kith provides in some way (or offers something complementary) that mostly makes it better, but could attach some constraint to its use or to the character. No Seeming characters might then just get a Kith power in its unmodified form.<br /> <br /> Of course, it could just be that Seeming doesn't affect anything other than Contracts. I just really like the idea of a blessing and curse tailored to each Kith-Seeming combination, even if I could easily see word count and effort required making it prohibitive.<br /> <br /> EDIT: @Arref: Those are interesting. I... have nothing more coherent on them at the moment, but nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 08-22-2014, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T09:27:02-07:00","id":238277,"title":"","content":"Beast: Those that where saved by someone else. Be it a motley raiding party, a group of other escapes who pulled him along for the ride, or even another fay lord looking to piss off a rival, someone saved him from Arcadia and when he came back he was like a wounded animal, growling and clawing at everyone, not knowing who was friend of foe and even when he regained his senses that feral spark stayed inside him.<br /> <br /> Still working on elemental. I'm thinking something along the lines of memories of who you were and where you've been acting as a bridge between Arcadia and the mortal world. The childhood memories of camping with your dad allow you to walk between the volcanoes flames and the flames of the campfire pit, but you had to let the flames inside of you and become one with them in order to do it. *Edit* The major theme being that you are now mired in the past, always looking back at how it was before everything went wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/182-sciurrus","user":"sciurrus","date":". 08-23-2014, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/182-sciurrus","name":"sciurrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:06:12-07:00","id":238355,"title":"","content":"@Dataweaver: Instinct works way better actually, I like that.<br /> <br /> Also, to everyone else, keep in mind that Seemings don't seem to be as... literal as they were before. Every kith can potentially fit into most (if not all) Seemings. (Re)Looking over what David's said, they aren't going to be something that's completely obvious, so it'll probably a bit more subtle than &quot;You're a Beast have some ears.&quot;<br /> <br /> So to take the Muse idea and run with it a bit:<br /> <br /> The <b>Wizened</b> Muse plays beautifully complex and intricate melodies. You can listen to the same song repeatedly and always hear something new.<br /> <br /> The <b>Fairest</b> Muse plays what you want to hear, when you didn't even realize you wanted to hear it. You can listen to the same song repeatedly and always find yourself loving it.<br /> <br /> The <b>Elemental</b> Muse plays simple things, and yet in those basic notes you find infinite depth. You can listen to the same song repeatedly and never truly understand it.<br /> <br /> The <b>Beast</b>(ial?) Muse plays songs that seem alive, like a reflection of the soul of the artist. You can listen for years and never hear the same song twice.<br /> <br /> The <b>Darkling</b> Muse plays in the background, subtle tunes that set moods and guide emotions. You can listen to the same song repeatedly and never know what you heard.<br /> <br /> The <b>Ogre</b> Muse punches you to &quot;Shave and a Haircut.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T22:21:01-07:00","id":238863,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Interesting. Let me see what I can up with using Earthbones, and what that interpretation could bring. <br /> <br /> The <b>Wizened</b> Earthbones always seems to know just how to repair a building, even when the flaw that causes so many problems confounds everyone else. <br /> <br /> The <b>Fairest</b> Earthbones smells of polish, and their voice is as rich as fertile soil. Their body is chiseled like a marble statue, and even smoother. Their presence always gets attention, regardless of occasion. <br /> <br /> The <b>Elemental</b> Earthbones is like a gate that will only budge for those worthy. They are the staunchest of allies, and the most stubborn of enemies, refusing to back down, or break. <br /> <br /> The <b>Beast </b>Earthbones always seems to be ready to hide, always ready to curl into the nearest crack in the wall or hole in the ground. If a suitable hiding spot is lacking, they can just easily create one through digging and effort. <br /> <br /> The <b>Darkling </b>Earthbones is like a warped mirror, reflecting the sins of yourself and others, while they sit back, silent as a rock. When building themselves seem to reveal the lies of their owners, they may have played a part. <br /> <br /> The <b>Ogre </b>Earthbones is a giant of brutal might, ready to overwhelm an opponent like a rockslide, and smash through anyone who dares to help their enemies the same way. <br /> <br /> Thoughts? Darkling is kind of weak, but I had a much harder time connecting rocks or buildings with their paranoia theme(which I've latched onto, that and fear. Perhaps connections to haunted houses are in order?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T22:42:49-07:00","id":238872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=237282#post237282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seemings as Agency.<br /> <br /> Beasts<br /> The Ones Who Forgot Learning and Discovered the Freedom of Now<br /> <br /> <br /> Darklings<br /> The Ones Who Hid Their Hearts and Bent the Rules<br /> <br /> <br /> Elementals<br /> The Ones Who Shed Humanity and Breathe the Wyrd<br /> <br /> <br /> Fairest<br /> The Ones Who Believed and Lived as Fae<br /> <br /> <br /> Ogres<br /> The Ones Who Broke their Chains and Savaged the Rules<br /> <br /> <br /> Wizened<br /> The Ones Who Became Twisted and Married Magic<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, I like both the Beasts and Elementals as interpreted here. Darklings... hmm. Latter to me could apply to a fair amount, but the former part of it, hiding their hearts, certainly works. Wizened I feel like needs to keep with the expertise focus, and specifically marrying magic doesn't quite work to me in relation to them. Ogres are great, the Fairest's first part is... odd. Believed Fae? Meaning they took themselves to be Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T23:07:03-07:00","id":238900,"title":"","content":"Having re-read the Beast's section, it really looks like sensory overload is a core theme in 1.0, along with being stuck in the present, and things like sensuality. Expanding that theme to one of agency suggests perhaps rejecting the rules of the Fae, and by extension, the tyranny of things like, &quot;tradition,&quot; in favor of some baser, instinctual part of anyone, the wild rebel if you will. Now, the latter has been suggested already, but could perhaps be expanded upon, and would certainly help build off themes from 1.0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T23:09:27-07:00","id":238902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=236063#post236063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I'm merging Beasts and Elementals, because I'm afraid Dymphna might kill me.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Thank</b> you. I'm not too big into Changeling but I'm passively interested in all the 2e updates, but I was worried when I read this in my thread-lurking. I don't have a very convincing or articulate argument for not combining them, though.<br /> <br /> But for me Seemings were far more inspirational than Kiths. I really think the game nailed down every fucking archetype there is between those six and I was hating to see it go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T23:53:25-07:00","id":238909,"title":"","content":"I don't think I ever said it, because I assume I made it clear, but thats a bad assumption, so let me say: <i>Thank God </i>Beasts and Elementals are staying I know I said I had a case for Primals, but I loved the idea of both as Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T00:09:08-07:00","id":238914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=238872#post238872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to say, I like both the Beasts and Elementals as interpreted here. Darklings... hmm. Latter to me could apply to a fair amount, but the former part of it, hiding their hearts, certainly works. Wizened I feel like needs to keep with the expertise focus, and specifically marrying magic doesn't quite work to me in relation to them. Ogres are great, the Fairest's first part is... odd. Believed Fae? Meaning they took themselves to be Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>To orient the Seemings to the idea of Agency, I wanted some poetic 'price' and 'advantage' in each description (not unlike a Contract, as it were). And yet we want to retain flexibility to access a whole lot of Kiths. So again, flexibility being interpretation of the 'price vs advantage'. Each player can explain the approach within a framework of the Seeming.<br /> <br /> So with the <b>Fairest</b>, imagine they are sucked into the Glory of the Fairytale Story. They warp close to Fae themselves, beautiful, uncanny, manipulative, and they carry away this veneer with them when they escape. The Fairest have to pull themselves back from becoming collaborators and believing it all. They fooled the Keepers, but they now resemble moreso the thing they were fighting. &quot;My Manipulation will set me free.&quot;<br /> <br /> So with the <b>Wizened</b>, imagine they obsessed on the expertise that was giving them power, gained frightening skills, but became twisted in pursuit of that. They lost parts of themselves as they chased the secrets. They learned more than the Keepers could guess, pushing themselves into a love of arcane skills and craft that change them but allow fantastic ability. &quot;My Craft will set me free.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T00:23:19-07:00","id":238926,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;My X will set me free&quot; works as a tag line much better than just &quot;agency&quot;.<br /> <br /> It also works more generally, since it marries the metaphor of Seeming as Bridge with the lack of Clarity between Earth and Arcadia: your Seeming <i>continues</i> to set you free, rather than just being the moment of freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T05:21:13-07:00","id":239028,"title":"","content":"Agreed on the setting free tag line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T05:35:30-07:00","id":239047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=238926#post238926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;My X will set me free&quot; works as a tag line much better than just &quot;agency&quot;.<br /> <br /> It also works more generally, since it marries the metaphor of Seeming as Bridge with the lack of Clarity between Earth and Arcadia: your Seeming <i>continues</i> to set you free, rather than just being the moment of freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh. It's a nitpick. But that sounds like it takes the power out of the character's hand. It gives the credit to the Seeming, not to the character. The character took control; the Seeming reflects that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T05:46:55-07:00","id":239049,"title":"","content":"I'm a little more fond of &quot;Here's where you twisted the story&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T08:28:36-07:00","id":239164,"title":"","content":"How about &quot;Freedom through X&quot;? &quot;Freedom through Craft&quot;, &quot;Freedom through Manipulation&quot;, &quot;Freedom through Instinct&quot;, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T09:39:58-07:00","id":239265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=238914#post238914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To orient the Seemings to the idea of Agency, I wanted some poetic 'price' and 'advantage' in each description (not unlike a Contract, as it were). And yet we want to retain flexibility to access a whole lot of Kiths. So again, flexibility being interpretation of the 'price vs advantage'. Each player can explain the approach within a framework of the Seeming.<br /> <br /> So with the <b>Fairest</b>, imagine they are sucked into the Glory of the Fairytale Story. They warp close to Fae themselves, beautiful, uncanny, manipulative, and they carry away this veneer with them when they escape. The Fairest have to pull themselves back from becoming collaborators and believing it all. They fooled the Keepers, but they now resemble moreso the thing they were fighting. &quot;My Manipulation will set me free.&quot;<br /> <br /> So with the <b>Wizened</b>, imagine they obsessed on the expertise that was giving them power, gained frightening skills, but became twisted in pursuit of that. They lost parts of themselves as they chased the secrets. They learned more than the Keepers could guess, pushing themselves into a love of arcane skills and craft that change them but allow fantastic ability. &quot;My Craft will set me free.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, interesting. Your explanation for Fairest certainly works. Wizened... I do admit that, yes, their talent would probably be magical, so I'm guessing I'm thinking of their expertise still in a much more mundane sense. Hmm. <br /> <br /> But also, isn't the Price part, somewhat, now covered by a Kith? To be fair, a Seeming probably shouldn't be all roses, so there's that. (That, and I subscribe to the viewpoint that becoming a Seeming meant you had to change yourself physically, not just mentally or magically.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T09:45:01-07:00","id":239269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=239049#post239049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little more fond of &quot;Here's where you twisted the story&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! Especially if the True Fae are possibly living embodiments of stories, it really shows how the Changeling changes things, because you wrote the story to favor your side of the tale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:16:25-07:00","id":239305,"title":"","content":"And now, my attempt to get Gristlegrinder for every Seeming. While, of course, this is all rather mutable, and will probably be completely changed with time, I think this is an interesting thought exercise to go along with how we now think of the Seemings. <br /> <br /> The <b>Beast </b>Gristlegrinder is like the Big Bad Wolf, always entrancing more to their beds to be devoured. Their smile holds wicked sharp teeth, and their bodies have the irresistible sensuality of a beast. <br /> <br /> The <b>Darkling </b>Gristlegrinder is the monster under the bed or in the closet, waiting to swallow up children the minute their parents leave. Their form is like the shadows that dance around one's bed at night, hard to define, and seeming to warp with need. <br /> <br /> The <b>Elemental </b>Gristlegrinder is like quicksand, swallowing up those foolish enough to step in its grasp. They almost seem a little sandy whenever they're around, or appear. <br /> <br /> The <b>Fairest </b>Gristlegrinder is the caring one, waiting to offer treats to those who'll have a stay in her home for the night. Once her victims are asleep, she prepares to dump them into a pot to boil and gorge on. <br /> <br /> The <b>Ogre </b>Gristlegrinder is ferocious, willing to savage opponents with teeth and fists, before devouring their remains. Their teeth are immense, all the better to rip and tear with. <br /> <br /> The <b>Wizened </b>Gristlegrinder is an amazing chef, always knowing what their guests need for sustenance. However, don't ever ask them where the best ingredients come from...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T19:44:30-07:00","id":239812,"title":"","content":"For the fun of it, how about a Kith that's usually never thought of with anything BUT darklings; Gravewights?<br /> <br /> A Beast would be those who take the superstitions about animals to the extreme; a black cat is a harbringer of death, the crows and ravens act as a messenger between worlds, and an owl is able to see the lingering souls in the world, and perhaps sense when new ones are to form. Acting as psychopomps and instinctive guides, these companions do their best to move the dead on. Some may then attempt to keep the living from interacting with the dead, while others might take their duty as harbringer of death seriously, choosing who among the living should be moved on with little more than a whim as guidance.<br /> <br /> A Darkling has severed their proper ties to the living in their mind, instead taking a grim comfort in consorting with the dead. Slowly losing touch with the living, the comfortably predictable patterns of earthly spectres seems to comfort them in a way, a reminder of how they've managed to escape the world of the ever-changing Fae. This separation, of course, has a cost, making it difficult for them amongst humankind, and they all too often find themselves mirroring the haunting games of spectres and shades in order to keep their solitude.<br /> <br /> An Elemental is as much flesh as ephemera, a being half formed of the ectoplasmic essence that makes up the lingering dead. While a Darkling consorts with the dead, an elemental becomes them, not purposely withdrawing so much as simply finding their minds forming an entirely different sort of thought process than any human would. They find it difficult to do more than follow and watch their loved ones at a distance, unsure how to connect firsthand.<br /> <br /> A Fairest commands an otherworldly allure, pale skin and blackened hair somehow enhancing them instead of detracting. The shades flock to them like moths to the swamp light, and their reach extends beyond the realm of the living to networks of undead informants and allies, working to spread word of their beauty and worth. That's not to say that the deceased are their only followers; their eerie grace and exotic form of beauty seems to captivate the living just as easily, putting a shiver down mortal spines while they long for the courage to get closer.<br /> <br /> An Ogre finds themselves as brutal protectors of the sanctity of death, stalking graveyards to punish those that might vandalize graves or uproot bodies. The spectres act as their eyes and ears, guiding the fury of one who knows all too well what it's like to have one's body taken and mutilated with no care for proper respect. No small number of tales of creatures guarding graveyards are actually about the Ogre guarding them, rather than the dead themselves.<br /> <br /> A Wizened is a necromancer and wisdom keeper, performing small favors for the deceased to learn of their secrets, or perhaps to get the chance to study one of these ghosts directly. Blunt and to the point, they rarely see the shades they study as deserving much more respect than an odd bit of flora or fauna, a little cold to them even when they work to assist them. Rumors spread of those that even go so far as to warp the still-aware spectres into odd shapes and forms, creating otherworldly artifacts fueled by the essence of the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T22:14:43-07:00","id":239924,"title":"","content":"So when it comes to &quot;Seemings as how you escaped&quot;, what I want to know is this:<br /> <br /> Say you have a changeling who was taken to be the perfect lover for a True Fae. At first it was grand, yadda yadda, but then it wasn't so great, and the changeling wanted to leave, but they couldn't for as long as they could love, so they cut their heart out and replaced it with ice.<br /> <br /> Would this Changeling be an Elemental (icy/inhuman heart), a Darkling (sacrificing a very human part of themselves) or a Fairest (since the focus is so heavily on interpersonal relations/love specifically?)<br /> <br /> An Artist is taken to be the official poet of a Fae court, and escapes by weaving a bridge from his Keeper's hair -- they're obviously a Wizened, but what about someone taken to be a soldier who &quot;died&quot; to escape, setting down their weapon before an enemy who was innocent but still dangerous, and letting them cut the soldier through? Darkling (losing their life), Ogre (letting themselves be killed violently by someone who was &quot;good&quot; in comparison), Fairest (again, interpersonal relations / focus on purity)<br /> <br /> What about the Hunterheart who literally hunted their Keeper down to their lair and killed them? Ogre (escaping through violence), Beast (it <i>is</i> natural for a hunter to hunt, after all), or Darkling (for the fear caused by the Hunterheart's pursuit?)<br /> <br /> I think &quot;seeming as agency&quot; is confusing the issue a little. . . but then again, I may be overthinking a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","user":"Murder-chan","date":". 08-25-2014, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T23:08:22-07:00","id":239949,"title":"","content":"I feel like that would depend on which aspect of the escape you'd want to emphasize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T23:31:53-07:00","id":239963,"title":"","content":"<i>From the pen of my player Isabella, who does not have an account here yet</i>:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">It all sounds cool but I'm seeing a few issues. The first is there will always be some conceptual overlaps: If a changeling shoves their keeper off a cliff on an impulse, are they a beast or an ogre? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The second is this format by necessity locks out certain character concepts, which I tend to hate. for instance, if your standard faithful butler decides to poison their True Fae master, it seems like they're going to end up a darkling instead of a wizened, and <i>you can't be an wizened without changing your backstory</i> - I hate this. It <i>could</i> be fine if it weren't for contracts being tied to Seeming. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I also do not know if I like the idea that someone &quot;let go&quot; has no Seeming, just because of the mechanics aspect - likewise, it seems like Loyalitsts are essentially going to be screwed mechanics-wise, if they're not careful.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This system may also lead to some weird idiosyncrasies, where a changeling who simply snuck out isn't able to be a Darkling. Not necessarily a gamebreaker, but kind of weird. Another character might wind up out in the cold without a lot of contrived explanation (there's no real &quot;agency&quot; behind &quot;my Keeper got bored&quot;, and there's no real Seeming for &quot;I broke out of the abuse victim mindset and left&quot;, unless you claim it counts under ogre). </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">There's also a minor silly issue in that the &quot;No Seeming&quot; merit means you're &quot;more human&quot;, which would be directly at odds with the idea that the changeling never escaped on their own.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T23:38:54-07:00","id":239964,"title":"","content":"One thing I want to bring up in regards to Agency, No Seeming, and Loyalists:<br /> <br /> No one ever said your method of agency involved escaping, even as a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:10:29-07:00","id":239980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=239964#post239964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I want to bring up in regards to Agency, No Seeming, and Loyalists:<br /> <br /> No one ever said your method of agency involved escaping, even as a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I hoped that was implied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:46:33-07:00","id":239999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=239963#post239963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first is there will always be some conceptual overlaps:</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how big of an issue this is. Conceptual overlaps essentially nullify the second issue because edge cases can go either way depending on what the player wants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second is this format by necessity locks out certain character concepts, which I tend to hate. for instance, if your standard faithful butler decides to poison their True Fae master, it seems like they're going to end up a darkling instead of a wizened, and <i>you can't be an wizened without changing your backstory</i> - I hate this. It <i>could</i> be fine if it weren't for contracts being tied to Seeming. </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm not understanding something, but what's the problem here? What concept is being locked out?<br /> <br /> Why shouldn't the &quot;loyal butler&quot; (aka the new Kith concept) have a different backstory for the Darkling version over the Wizened version? They're different characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:58:25-07:00","id":240005,"title":"","content":"Wondering why none of the theorizing about Wizened Agency has seemed to engage with the 1e commonality of the seeming.<br /> <br /> Persistence, spite and self-lessening paint a fairly clear picture of how the Little Folk might have retaken the wheel of their fortunes, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T04:55:10-07:00","id":240148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=239980#post239980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. I hoped that was implied.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really interested in how you plan on making Seemings work. To go back to the Zen of Elementals thing I put up earlier, would that sort of concept be more in line with your imagining of 2.0 Seemings rather than &quot;You seduced a guard, you are now a Fairest&quot; or some other specific act? I guess what I'm asking is if Seemings are less the actions of seizing freedom and more the methods in which a Changeling copes with their suffering? IE - Elementals letting go of their &quot;self,&quot; Ogres fighting tooth and nail, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T05:48:24-07:00","id":240173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240148#post240148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm really interested in how you plan on making Seemings work. To go back to the Zen of Elementals thing I put up earlier, would that sort of concept be more in line with your imagining of 2.0 Seemings rather than &quot;You seduced a guard, you are now a Fairest&quot; or some other specific act? I guess what I'm asking is if Seemings are less the actions of seizing freedom and more the methods in which a Changeling copes with their suffering? IE - Elementals letting go of their &quot;self,&quot; Ogres fighting tooth and nail, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to let the author of that section, whomever it ends up being, flavor that. I can wax philosophical about how I perceive it, but in the end, this is one of those places where I hire the authors for their particular talent and poetry. I want to see how they make it sing before I put a hard foot down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T07:52:57-07:00","id":240286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=239964#post239964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I want to bring up in regards to Agency, No Seeming, and Loyalists:<br /> <br /> No one ever said your method of agency involved escaping, even as a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. <br /> <br /> This perhaps could be then one reclaiming themselves from their Keeper, and by extension, Faire, which changes things a bit here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T07:57:03-07:00","id":240290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=239963#post239963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>From the pen of my player Isabella, who does not have an account here yet</i>:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">It all sounds cool but I'm seeing a few issues. The first is there will always be some conceptual overlaps: If a changeling shoves their keeper off a cliff on an impulse, are they a beast or an ogre? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The second is this format by necessity locks out certain character concepts, which I tend to hate. for instance, if your standard faithful butler decides to poison their True Fae master, it seems like they're going to end up a darkling instead of a wizened, and <i>you can't be an wizened without changing your backstory</i> - I hate this. It <i>could</i> be fine if it weren't for contracts being tied to Seeming. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I also do not know if I like the idea that someone &quot;let go&quot; has no Seeming, just because of the mechanics aspect - likewise, it seems like Loyalitsts are essentially going to be screwed mechanics-wise, if they're not careful.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This system may also lead to some weird idiosyncrasies, where a changeling who simply snuck out isn't able to be a Darkling. Not necessarily a gamebreaker, but kind of weird. Another character might wind up out in the cold without a lot of contrived explanation (there's no real &quot;agency&quot; behind &quot;my Keeper got bored&quot;, and there's no real Seeming for &quot;I broke out of the abuse victim mindset and left&quot;, unless you claim it counts under ogre). </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">There's also a minor silly issue in that the &quot;No Seeming&quot; merit means you're &quot;more human&quot;, which would be directly at odds with the idea that the changeling never escaped on their own.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, here's something for some of those.<br /> <br /> For the poison necessitating poison, I don't see that. Darklings are about fear, so I more see it you whispered dark things into your Keeper's ear and drove them nuts(well, more nuts), if you were their butler. A Wizened could still use poison, and would I'd argue fit more if their job involved say, making wine.<br /> <br /> But really, the key here is with the details. How you poisoned your Keeper could in theory give you any Seeming. Did you force the poison down their throat? Ogre. Did you hide it with social edict? Fairest. Did your usage of it involve fear, for example, somehow? Darkling. Did you craft an irresistible wine before poisoning it to give your Keeper? Wizened. Beast I admit I'm not sure, same goes for Elemental, but I'm sure someone could work with those to get something.<br /> <br /> As breaking out of your abuse mindset, that could easily be a part of some other Seeming, and is really more a general concept.<br /> <br /> As for Loyalists getting screwed... yeah, that's a point I don't have a counter for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-25-2014, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:01:38-07:00","id":240296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=239812#post239812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the fun of it, how about a Kith that's usually never thought of with anything BUT darklings; Gravewights?<br /> <br /> A Beast would be those who take the superstitions about animals to the extreme; a black cat is a harbringer of death, the crows and ravens act as a messenger between worlds, and an owl is able to see the lingering souls in the world, and perhaps sense when new ones are to form. Acting as psychopomps and instinctive guides, these companions do their best to move the dead on. Some may then attempt to keep the living from interacting with the dead, while others might take their duty as harbringer of death seriously, choosing who among the living should be moved on with little more than a whim as guidance.<br /> <br /> A Darkling has severed their proper ties to the living in their mind, instead taking a grim comfort in consorting with the dead. Slowly losing touch with the living, the comfortably predictable patterns of earthly spectres seems to comfort them in a way, a reminder of how they've managed to escape the world of the ever-changing Fae. This separation, of course, has a cost, making it difficult for them amongst humankind, and they all too often find themselves mirroring the haunting games of spectres and shades in order to keep their solitude.<br /> <br /> An Elemental is as much flesh as ephemera, a being half formed of the ectoplasmic essence that makes up the lingering dead. While a Darkling consorts with the dead, an elemental becomes them, not purposely withdrawing so much as simply finding their minds forming an entirely different sort of thought process than any human would. They find it difficult to do more than follow and watch their loved ones at a distance, unsure how to connect firsthand.<br /> <br /> A Fairest commands an otherworldly allure, pale skin and blackened hair somehow enhancing them instead of detracting. The shades flock to them like moths to the swamp light, and their reach extends beyond the realm of the living to networks of undead informants and allies, working to spread word of their beauty and worth. That's not to say that the deceased are their only followers; their eerie grace and exotic form of beauty seems to captivate the living just as easily, putting a shiver down mortal spines while they long for the courage to get closer.<br /> <br /> An Ogre finds themselves as brutal protectors of the sanctity of death, stalking graveyards to punish those that might vandalize graves or uproot bodies. The spectres act as their eyes and ears, guiding the fury of one who knows all too well what it's like to have one's body taken and mutilated with no care for proper respect. No small number of tales of creatures guarding graveyards are actually about the Ogre guarding them, rather than the dead themselves.<br /> <br /> A Wizened is a necromancer and wisdom keeper, performing small favors for the deceased to learn of their secrets, or perhaps to get the chance to study one of these ghosts directly. Blunt and to the point, they rarely see the shades they study as deserving much more respect than an odd bit of flora or fauna, a little cold to them even when they work to assist them. Rumors spread of those that even go so far as to warp the still-aware spectres into odd shapes and forms, creating otherworldly artifacts fueled by the essence of the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! Cool! Definitely some interesting ideas here, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:27:25-07:00","id":240313,"title":"","content":"I think it's entirely okay for the Defining Action of your Escape to have multiple possible interpretations. You still have to choose just one, but having multiple options to make a choice <i>from</i> seems perfectly valid.<br /> <br /> And here's an interesting possibility: what if you could change your Seeming if you decided one day to interpret your escape differently? Not saying it would be easy, but... what if?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":2758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","user":"Errol216","date":". 08-25-2014, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T11:28:11-07:00","id":240450,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I'm just going to go on a long brain barf about Elementals and see what we can get out of it.<br /> <br /> Elementals in the old version were the products of being made part of the environment, of being made one with the world. This implies a direct connection to the Stranger in question more so than most, because the world is their Domains, sometimes their Realms. No wonder the bastards have humanity issues-,they've been twice infected, once from that perspective of the breathing world(as opposed to the bleeding world, ala Beasts) and once by sheer Fae effect. In a sense, this means that when a changeling uproots itself from the Domain and walks out, or about, the Elemental is more of a direct thief than any other-they literally became part of the Stranger and them ripped themselves off and out. It's like if your elbow skin just said &quot;Welp, I'm out&quot;, and tore itself brutally from your arm and preceded to run for the nearest bar.<br /> <br /> Elementals seem like kind of rude bastards that way. That's not relevant.<br /> <br /> It might seem like I'm suggesting &quot;Agency through theft&quot;, but that's not it, it doesn't parse, not with the examples handed out by Dave-burn the manor down, bury the dogs in a landslide, hold your breath and count to ten minutes(Guybrush). Still, it informs it a little.<br /> <br /> One thing that strikes me is that in the varied aspects of many Domains, it seems like Elementals are consistently baser and rawer. We have places where there place is a playpen, where an Elemental might be born from the surging mass of teddy bears and thus be a teddy bear themselves, one cotton and cloth drop in a plush friend ocean. Instead we get examples of Sand and Metal and Water and Fire and Earth and Wood and Lightning and Wind-we get those because they are archetypal, they're what we expect, but it also feels rawer. In fact, along with that rawness comes the feeling of power, of might, of something barely contained-each Domain that was marked as being Elementally favored had that sort of feeling, of action and energy just waiting to leap. You never had limpid pools, you had surging oceans. You had castles of glass and wire in the middle of the storm, and the lightning running through them was leaping, struggling,seething through. It feels ready to rip everything apart, even at it's most controlled-or at least that's how I remember it.<br /> <br /> And with that comes the sense of overwhelming power-not in the same way as a Ogre. Elementals were often marked as tough and power-partly because of their Blessing, sure, also largely in part of the simple and brutal elegance of the Contract of Elements(and even Communion and Wyld). But I think a larger part of it has to do with the fact that they are used to being part of the environment, used to having it be them. Admit it-when you see an Elemental in your head going nuts, the element is filling the room, the element consumes the subject matter. It floods, it snarls and grows, it eats with it's many flickering tongues, the wind pierces all, the lightning is in our roofs, our steeds, <i>our blood</i>, the Earth quakes, the sand and snow twists and blinds and binds. It doesn't even matter if the natural element is there, the Elementals <i>bleed it</i>. They become powerful because they are walking Domains. They control the place.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that, of the aspects of a Fae, it really is the Domain that makes the Elementals. You can make a (poor) argument that the aspects of a Fae all tie to the Seemings in ways-Props to Wizened, Actors to Fairest, other things where the metaphor falls apart. But Domains are <i>very</i> Elemental, a part of the world that is not more directly part of the fae-Elementals could but probably don't come from Realms. The main thing that marks the two apart is that the Stranger is in control of a Realm, it is not in control of a Domain, even if it <i>is</i> a part of them. It's a place where power like that can come unchecked, where the Stranger is most likely on the wrong foot.<br /> <br /> Okay. I think I got a simple sell for the Elementals.<br /> <br /> Agency through chaos, power from unity and control.<br /> <br /> Elementals take the raw, unbridled power of the Fae, and in an Autumn-like twist, throw it back at them(Hi Granfather Thunder) They create chaos and destruction and problems on the large scale. They burn the house down, the cause the landslide. They bury Strangers in a sea of teddy bears and <i>run like hell</i>. Chaos is a great equalizer-when no one knows what's going on and no one has the power to handle it, everyone is equally unable to act. Elementals are the earthquakes the Strangers never expected, and they get the power to express that agency by dominating the world they are in-and continue to do so. THey become one with the world they are in and seek to control it's every aspect, and gain the upper hand on people by throwing their expectations out the windows. Elementals are the ones who <i>change the game</i>. They learn to control the board, and deny others(Others) the chance to do so.<br /> <br /> How's that for a thought?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T12:23:42-07:00","id":240489,"title":"","content":"For me, the elemental Agency is, weirdly, more nihilistic. They escaped because they shed the weakness of humanity, the fears and hopes and dreams and horror. The river may be dammed, but it doesn't care, it build and builds until it bursts. The fire consumes all that come before it. The bends bends to the howling tempest. They build a big, artificial shell around them and march to the very gates of hell because if they fail, then they;re no worse off. The Beast howls and rages against the dying of the light, but the Elementals endure. They are inexorable and determined not ebcause they know they will succeed, but they have no fear of failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T12:51:28-07:00","id":240521,"title":"","content":"It says something when you can't out-violence, out-know, out-exploit, or out-act your captors and have to rely on the world around you-hen you have to steal from them- in order to really show agency. You do have a certain amount of rejection going on.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't like the idea of endurance being a expression of agency. It doesn't feel proactive to me, and on a more disturbing level creates the idea of a victim just taking it. That said, I imagine you have to be pretty tough to basically make an area go into pure chaos and get out of it alive. Endurance can also manifest in what it takes to make that work-it can be a lot of long, hard nights in the cold desert with the sands eating you up before you can creat the moment of choas that lets you out.<br /> <br /> I also don't want to make assertions for or against trans-humanism by touching on the rejection of support of humanity. I think that's for the characters to decide on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T13:01:44-07:00","id":240549,"title":"","content":"It's not so much about 'just taking it', it's about 'pushing through regardless'<br /> <br /> As for the transhuman part, that wasn't my intent, I'm more of the pinion that the Semings don't just represent the past, but also the present. Your Seeming is who you are in the dark - caging your heart and pushing through against your Durance makes you an Elemental, it is the scar you gave yourself, where the Kith is the scar your Keeper gave you. You could have raged and destroyed and become an Ogre, you could have tricked and snuck your way as a Darkling, but you set your jaw and marched through the fires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T13:14:45-07:00","id":240602,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion a Seeming is a scar you give yourself too-but let's acknowledge that you are giving yourself a scar.<br /> <br /> The Seeming is the Moment. It is a moment in time where you did something to take control of your life.<br /> <br /> No one said it was a moment you should be proud of, regardless of what Summer says. No one said it was a moment you don't regret.<br /> <br /> That might have been the moment you found out just how much of a monster you can be.<br /> <br /> Anyways, that's not wholly related.<br /> <br /> Still, I must say this again: I don't like the the idea of pushing through regardless. People don't get out of bad situations just pushing through regardless. People don't grow, don't control themselves and their lives by just pushing through regardless. Nothing <i>changes</i> when you just push through regardless.<br /> <br /> You have to do something, change the situation, before pushing through regardless becomes meaningful.<br /> <br /> You have to let the cops arrest your husband before you can stick to your guns and never deviate from the path that will put him in prison. You have to decide to leave him before you can stick to your guns and never go back. You can't stick to your guns when sticking to your guns means you're still getting hit every night.<br /> <br /> No one who improves their lot in life does it by just enduring.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In fact, I'll just say it outright-endurance, by itself, has <i>nothing</i> to do with agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-25-2014, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T14:08:58-07:00","id":240728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240602#post240602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: In fact, I'll just say it outright-endurance, by itself, has <i>nothing</i> to do with agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we'l have to agree to disagree, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T14:17:29-07:00","id":240734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240728#post240728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we'l have to agree to disagree, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>With apologies to those this might depress, I can only assume you've never been there.<br /> <br /> We can agree to disagree, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T14:40:58-07:00","id":240757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240734#post240734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With apologies to those this might depress, I can only assume you've never been there.</div> </div> </div> </div>...this is untrue and I am disappointed that you would make that assumption. You don't know anything about my life or what I and my family have been through.<br /> <br /> Don't <i>ever</i> make that assumption about someone just because they fucking disagree with you. How <i>dare</i> you. Just because I don't want to make a huge fucking post about deeply personal shit explaining my situation you think I haven't been there?<br /> <br /> Whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T15:03:48-07:00","id":240788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240757#post240757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...this is untrue and I am disappointed that you would make that assumption. You don't know anything about my life or what I and my family have been through.<br /> <br /> Don't <i>ever</i> make that assumption about someone just because they fucking disagree with you. How <i>dare</i> you. Just because I don't want to make a huge fucking post about deeply personal shit explaining my situation you think I haven't been there?<br /> <br /> Whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now I feel like a douche.<br /> <br /> You're right.That was wrong of me. I'm sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T15:15:03-07:00","id":240798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240788#post240788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now I feel like a douche.<br /> <br /> You're right.That was wrong of me. I'm sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ok, just... be careful<br /> <br /> The long and the short of what I was going to write (and didn't, due to lack of spoons) is the 'endurance' I speak of is the catalyst -the Elemental cuts away all that makes them 'weak' and 'human', that is to say what the Keepers have over them, and march out of the Keeper's grasp. They make themselves both less and more through this action - the Darkling may betray another, but the Elemental betrays themselves. They know that their choice means they are even less whole than other Changelings, more akin to the inanimate world than the living one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:54:46-07:00","id":240897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240296#post240296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh! Cool! Definitely some interesting ideas here, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I know Elemental and Darkling overlap a fair bit there, but I was just sort of throwing things together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T21:55:20-07:00","id":241071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240798#post240798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They make themselves both less and more through this action - the Darkling may betray another, but the Elemental betrays themselves. They know that their choice means they are even less whole than other Changelings, more akin to the inanimate world than the living one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So coming back to this.<br /> <br /> I know some people says some of my suggestions have been an all changeling thing, and this is that for me.<br /> <br /> I think some parts of the issue is hueing too closely to the old version. I get that, I like the issues with their own personal humanity that the Elementals had. But under the new context I find myself saying &quot;Shouldn't this be something all changelings can suffer or grow from?&quot;<br /> <br /> It may be more direct with Elementals, but the idea of betraying one's self for agency is across the board. A Fairest sleeps with a Stranger(...), a Darkling hamstrings their buddy to ensure they're slower, an Ogre breaks the Stranger's arm with the same cruelty and malice that it broke his own, the Wizened causes trouble for his mates elsewhere to disrupt the system, a Beast eats a goblin's heart.<br /> <br /> Aren't <i>all</i> of these betrayal of self? It depends on the person, but for most people, doing this betrays the average persons's sense of right and wrong on several fronts. Do the circumstances justify the actions? Maybe, but the psyche isn't always prepared to accept that.<br /> <br /> In fact, compared to some of these, a simple &quot;Abandon humanity for power of the world&quot; seems small, almost laughable. I can almost hear someone say &quot;Oh, you had to become a tree? Oh babe, I'm so sorry. I had to shoot someone. They didn't die on the first shot. They didn't die on the second one either.&quot;<br /> <br /> I want the door open for all of them. Sometimes, the moment you took agency is a proud, shining moment. It shows your composure, your cunning, your knowledge, your boldness, maybe even your kindness, if you're lucky. It might be your most human moment ever. Sometimes, the moment you took agency is a terrible thing you hope you'll never have to do again. It shows your selfishness, your capriciousness, your cruelty, your deceitfulness, maybe even your misanthropy, if you're unlucky. It might be your most alien(monstrous) moment ever.<br /> <br /> Embrace it or run from it, the Seeming is a Moment, and that Moment is Endless. You will be marked forever by your answer to the question of what you felt you were worth, and how you define yourself from then on is going to come back to how you feel about that Moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T22:04:20-07:00","id":241075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=241071#post241071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embrace it or run from it, the Seeming is a Moment, and that Moment is Endless. You will be marked forever by your answer to the question of what you felt you were worth, and how you define yourself from then on is going to come back to how you feel about that Moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It\u2019s hard for anyone to watch that. It\u2019s harder for one of us, because we know about hopelessness. <b>We remember what it\u2019s like to be trapped someplace where the possibility of escape doesn\u2019t exist. At least, until something changes.<br /> <br /> Something changes. Ha. To escape Arcadia, <i>you</i> have to change. You have to let it into you.</b> My skin became smooth, polished glass. My name faded away, turned backwards, and disappeared like a reflection when the light goes out. I had to become a mirror image before I could get loose.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve got this sneaking feeling, though, that to get back in to Arcadia, you\u2019ve got to change even more.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T22:08:01-07:00","id":241079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=241075#post241075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It\u2019s hard for anyone to watch that. It\u2019s harder for one of us, because we know about hopelessness. <b>We remember what it\u2019s like to be trapped someplace where the possibility of escape doesn\u2019t exist. At least, until something changes.<br /> <br /> Something changes. Ha. To escape Arcadia, <i>you</i> have to change. You have to let it into you.</b> My skin became smooth, polished glass. My name faded away, turned backwards, and disappeared like a reflection when the light goes out. I had to become a mirror image before I could get loose.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve got this sneaking feeling, though, that to get back in to Arcadia, you\u2019ve got to change even more.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which book was that in? EDIT:The Icicle Melts, opening to Equinox Road, got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T07:43:37-07:00","id":241320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=239047#post239047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. It's a nitpick. But that sounds like it takes the power out of the character's hand. It gives the credit to the Seeming, not to the character. The character took control; the Seeming reflects that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally unintended, if that is how it was read.<br /> I agree the Character decision to make a difference is what the Seeming should reflect.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T09:11:37-07:00","id":241400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240602#post240602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seeming is the Moment. It is a moment in time where you did something to take control of your life.<br /> <br /> That might have been the moment you found out just how much of a monster you can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to explore this idea moreso with Elementals than any other Seeming. It needs to be stronger or more pure, however. How do we do that and provide Agency?<br /> <br /> To me, no matter how twisted or strange, most of the Seemings cling to their Humanity even as they suffer. Elementals seem to be the one by design where the Monstrous became not strange at all. Where the Changeling took up the Wyrd and decided to be Monstrously Other. The alien quality that even other Changelings sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T11:34:50-07:00","id":242354,"title":"","content":"Threads stalling a bit. Lets keep fiddling.<br /> <br /> Darklings were motivated by <b>Fear</b>. They killed before they could be killed, betrayed before they could be betrayed. They ran, they hid, they took the most confusing route they could just to ensure they weren't followed.<br /> <br /> Fairest were motivated by <b>Beauty</b>. Maybe it was a fellow captive, or a memory of home. Maybe it was a dream or a glimpse of sunset. They were snapped from their fugues by these flashes of beauty and drove themselves forward, however they could, hoping to reach them.<br /> <br /> Ogres were motivated by <b>Anger</b>. One too many beatings, one too many traumas. Enough is enough. &quot;Live free or die,&quot; isn't that the saying? They tore through their chains in their rage and cut themselves a warpath, all the way home.<br /> <br /> Wizened were motivated by <b>Reason</b>. They didn't just react. They <i>planned</i>. Their masters gave them powers and crafts and otherworldly knowledge, and they wouldn't let <i>any</i> of it go to waste. <br /> <br /> Beasts were motivated by <b>Instinct</b>. They saw an opening and they took it. It didn't matter the means, it didn't matter the cost. There were no plans or grand triggers, only action. &quot;Don't think, just do.&quot;<br /> <br /> Elementals were motivated by <b>Desperation</b>. They could see the signs, <i>feel</i> the signs. Their time in Arcadia was warping them too much and they were beginning to lose what little humanity they had left. They let go of their burdens and trivialities, focused on retaining what was <i>truly</i> important, and trudged their way back, losing more of themselves with every step.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely satisfied with the Elementals' drive, but I can't think of how to turn &quot;Zenning Out&quot; into a basic concept like the others. I think the major defining trait Elementals should be keep in 2.0, though, is alienation. The &quot;Fury of Nature&quot; is basically window dressing to a Seeming that even the other Lost agree is really, really weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T11:43:43-07:00","id":242357,"title":"","content":"Sooner or later I'm gonna do a brain-barf on Beasts. Again, I don't know if these write ups are helping, but if anything I think it's tackling the Seemings at different angles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T12:55:20-07:00","id":242471,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I like over-associating darklings with fear. While it's a big part of their essential nature, at least in first edition, I feel like it would be weird to have two splats (darkling and autumn court) drawing from that. I think I recall something in the core book about darklings often ending up in arcadia because they broke some fae law or somesuch, particularly when they dug too deep for some kind of secret. That, I think, would be an interesting starting point. Perhaps, rather than just breaking the myth the keeper set for them, a darkling broke some fundimental law of the realm he was in, or even of arcadia itself (if such a thing is even possible). The shadier, more monstrous aspects often associated with them could perhaps be the stain they bear for such defiance. I'm not totally sure about the idea but it's an interesting thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T14:25:55-07:00","id":242538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240450#post240450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so I'm just going to go on a long brain barf about Elementals and see what we can get out of it.<br /> <br /> Elementals in the old version were the products of being made part of the environment, of being made one with the world. This implies a direct connection to the Stranger in question more so than most, because the world is their Domains, sometimes their Realms. No wonder the bastards have humanity issues-,they've been twice infected, once from that perspective of the breathing world(as opposed to the bleeding world, ala Beasts) and once by sheer Fae effect. In a sense, this means that when a changeling uproots itself from the Domain and walks out, or about, the Elemental is more of a direct thief than any other-they literally became part of the Stranger and them ripped themselves off and out. It's like if your elbow skin just said &quot;Welp, I'm out&quot;, and tore itself brutally from your arm and preceded to run for the nearest bar.<br /> <br /> Elementals seem like kind of rude bastards that way. That's not relevant.<br /> <br /> It might seem like I'm suggesting &quot;Agency through theft&quot;, but that's not it, it doesn't parse, not with the examples handed out by Dave-burn the manor down, bury the dogs in a landslide, hold your breath and count to ten minutes(Guybrush). Still, it informs it a little.<br /> <br /> One thing that strikes me is that in the varied aspects of many Domains, it seems like Elementals are consistently baser and rawer. We have places where there place is a playpen, where an Elemental might be born from the surging mass of teddy bears and thus be a teddy bear themselves, one cotton and cloth drop in a plush friend ocean. Instead we get examples of Sand and Metal and Water and Fire and Earth and Wood and Lightning and Wind-we get those because they are archetypal, they're what we expect, but it also feels rawer. In fact, along with that rawness comes the feeling of power, of might, of something barely contained-each Domain that was marked as being Elementally favored had that sort of feeling, of action and energy just waiting to leap. You never had limpid pools, you had surging oceans. You had castles of glass and wire in the middle of the storm, and the lightning running through them was leaping, struggling,seething through. It feels ready to rip everything apart, even at it's most controlled-or at least that's how I remember it.<br /> <br /> And with that comes the sense of overwhelming power-not in the same way as a Ogre. Elementals were often marked as tough and power-partly because of their Blessing, sure, also largely in part of the simple and brutal elegance of the Contract of Elements(and even Communion and Wyld). But I think a larger part of it has to do with the fact that they are used to being part of the environment, used to having it be them. Admit it-when you see an Elemental in your head going nuts, the element is filling the room, the element consumes the subject matter. It floods, it snarls and grows, it eats with it's many flickering tongues, the wind pierces all, the lightning is in our roofs, our steeds, <i>our blood</i>, the Earth quakes, the sand and snow twists and blinds and binds. It doesn't even matter if the natural element is there, the Elementals <i>bleed it</i>. They become powerful because they are walking Domains. They control the place.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that, of the aspects of a Fae, it really is the Domain that makes the Elementals. You can make a (poor) argument that the aspects of a Fae all tie to the Seemings in ways-Props to Wizened, Actors to Fairest, other things where the metaphor falls apart. But Domains are <i>very</i> Elemental, a part of the world that is not more directly part of the fae-Elementals could but probably don't come from Realms. The main thing that marks the two apart is that the Stranger is in control of a Realm, it is not in control of a Domain, even if it <i>is</i> a part of them. It's a place where power like that can come unchecked, where the Stranger is most likely on the wrong foot.<br /> <br /> Okay. I think I got a simple sell for the Elementals.<br /> <br /> Agency through chaos, power from unity and control.<br /> <br /> Elementals take the raw, unbridled power of the Fae, and in an Autumn-like twist, throw it back at them(Hi Granfather Thunder) They create chaos and destruction and problems on the large scale. They burn the house down, the cause the landslide. They bury Strangers in a sea of teddy bears and <i>run like hell</i>. Chaos is a great equalizer-when no one knows what's going on and no one has the power to handle it, everyone is equally unable to act. Elementals are the earthquakes the Strangers never expected, and they get the power to express that agency by dominating the world they are in-and continue to do so. THey become one with the world they are in and seek to control it's every aspect, and gain the upper hand on people by throwing their expectations out the windows. Elementals are the ones who <i>change the game</i>. They learn to control the board, and deny others(Others) the chance to do so.<br /> <br /> How's that for a thought?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting, and also does explain elements of them being raw, although the Mankin and the like mess with this, but Kiths changing should fix that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T14:37:14-07:00","id":242544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=242357#post242357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooner or later I'm gonna do a brain-barf on Beasts. Again, I don't know if these write ups are helping, but if anything I think it's tackling the Seemings at different angles.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't yet know if I agree with everything you've put out (still very much in the &quot;rolling thoughts around&quot; stage, over here), they've been thoughtful and enjoyable brain-barfs. I've looked forward to reading them whenever you've put out a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T14:41:21-07:00","id":242546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=242471#post242471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I like over-associating darklings with fear. While it's a big part of their essential nature, at least in first edition, I feel like it would be weird to have two splats (darkling and autumn court) drawing from that. I think I recall something in the core book about darklings often ending up in arcadia because they broke some fae law or somesuch, particularly when they dug too deep for some kind of secret. That, I think, would be an interesting starting point. Perhaps, rather than just breaking the myth the keeper set for them, a darkling broke some fundimental law of the realm he was in, or even of arcadia itself (if such a thing is even possible). The shadier, more monstrous aspects often associated with them could perhaps be the stain they bear for such defiance. I'm not totally sure about the idea but it's an interesting thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...<br /> <br /> Okay, this gives me an idea. <br /> <br /> Now, we already have the association of fear, and we also have the aspect of breaking rules. Who violates traditions in mythology? Tricksters! <br /> <br /> Of course, Tricksters are something any Changeling could embody, to say the least, and Beasts, for example, could easily embody what mythology will frequently call the amorous Trickster(i.e., sexual. Example is in some myths featuring Coyote.)<br /> <br /> However, what if the Darkling is the really cruel Trickster? Sure, we have other Changelings being cruel, but its in different ways. To compare, <br /> <br /> Fairest are cruel in a social way, and in becoming like their Keepers. Sure, they'll trick you, using the tools of social edict and charisma, but that's not the only type of trickery. Ogres... well, their brute force, and later on, also have aspects, ironically, of being the one who punish rule breakers. Beasts meanwhile, if we go with them being amorphous tricksters at times, well, that's a trickster, but not really as mean spirited, if you will. Wizened meanwhile are expertise and magic. They could certainly use trickery, but they're more the type that breaks out of prison with an elaborate plan, if you will. <br /> <br /> So, where does this leave Darklings? Well, what about trickery being a bit harsher? Also, remember an origin for Fae vulnerability to iron is that they broke a contract with Iron, and so, Iron took revenge. Well, what if someone like a Darkling did that? It would make sense with their origin too, because they got sent to Arcadia from breaking an obscure rule, well, might as well do it to your Keeper. Fear can come into this too, because they also represent the fate of breaking rules society tells you not to. <br /> <br /> Consider that, in myths featuring tricksters, they frequently, in the society they appeared, represented behaviors normal citizens weren't supposed to do, such as theft and the like. Expanding that to Darklings isn't a huge leap with their origins in 1.0, and could be an interesting response to being taken to Arcadia if they try becoming scary con artists, if you will. <br /> <br /> Sorry, bit of a brain spew of my own, tell me if you guys like it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T16:37:34-07:00","id":242649,"title":"","content":"Decoupling Seeming and Kith is awesome. My group's been doing that for years. I also really like the idea of a major character component being attached to the Changeling's escape. I've always been of the opinion that it is an under-treated aspect of the game. That said, I feel like Seeming is a bad fit for it. I've always loved Seeming for its broad archetypes not just in types of physical alterations, but also in psychological effects of the Durance. For me, being an Elemental is not just about being an object, but being removed from your humanity by your durance such that you have trouble relating to people. Being a Wizened isn't just about being turning into a goblin, but being subjected to torment such that spite becomes second-nature. People of the same Seeming shared a bond of common experience. A Beast lion is going to have more in common with a Beast rabbit than a Fairest lion, the superficial similarity with the latter notwithstanding. Kith, on the other hand, was a toolkit to fine tune your Seeming's physical characteristics. I'd be fine with kiths turning into a grab bag of physical aspects like those used in Demon to define Demonic Form. I'm less interested in going back to CtD's list of kiths as the primary splat.<br /> <br /> With the changes to Court, I'd almost prefer a new &quot;splat&quot; be added to reflect the escape. Not having any great insights into what it should be, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T16:39:31-07:00","id":242650,"title":"","content":"Yeah this one's gonna be a bit spewy too. I hope we're not overloading whoever eventually has to go back and read this for their chapter. Ah well, for the moment on with the stream of conciousness:<br /> <br /> I always sorta looked at wizened as the tricksy bunch but I suppose darklings can swing that way too. Come to think of it, changelings are probably just a sort of tricksy bunch in general. The way I'd always thought of Darklings really had more to do with essentially being shadow and night than being tricky and scary, everything else just sort of branched out from that core thematic point. It's kinda hard to make that work in the context of the current seeming setup though.I like the idea of saying that a darkling is someone whose first thought when presented with the challenge of escaping arcadia is to take the darkened road, to walk in shadow until they become shade, to take the path that seems most dangerous for the greater chance of going unseen but I don't think that'll work on a broad enough level for the second edition stuff. I like the tricky thing but I feel like that would kind of overlap a bit much with other seeming escapes. I suppose overlap isn't really a bad thing (actually I kind of like the idea that an entire group can escape together, through the same method, and come out with different seemings just by thinking of their escape in different ways) but I'd kind of like to be able to make a wizened or beast character and define them by their trickster nature, though I think a large part of that is probably just that I like tricksters and I like wizened and I want to play a wizened trickster which\u2026 is actually a really bad reason to vote against the idea of tricksy darklings but I should probably throw my bias out there for full disclosure. Even without that though, I think trickery might be too broad, as you sort of noted with the fairest and beast examples. maybe escape by deceit? It carries a lot of the same meaning as trickery but I feel like it's more evocative of the seeming and it makes room for trickery in other seemings where they can look at it from different angles and contextualize it as whatever the key &quot;thing&quot; for their seeming is, plus it can include anything they already had thought out for betrayal since betrayal is kind of a subset of deceit.<br /> <br /> on a side note, I am sort of hoping that the seeming ideas come out broad enough that between all of them they cover at least the vast majority of ways one could have escaped their keeper. The initial idea of betrayal feels a bit overly specific to me, I'd like (though I recognize it's not necessarily reasonable to expect, this is just tossing out ideas) if someone could just give me a story about their escape without knowing about the seemings and have the way they did it represented in some way by at least one seeming. I have a friend who did something like this with geist (he started the game with &quot;how do you want to die?&quot;) and it went over really well. I think it would be cool to be able to at least have the option for that sort of thing in changeling, particularly since the big escape is usually the centerpiece of most preludes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T18:43:11-07:00","id":242760,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Okay, let me see if I can help things at all by trying another Kith, this time by thinking about the Seemings through the new ideas some have posted here. Namely, Draconic. <br /> <br /> A <b>Beast </b>Draconic is the ultimate predator, doing whatever they want to whomever they want to or who dares to threaten their power. Everything to them is a conquest to be forcefully achieved, whether its in the physical or social arena.<br /> <br /> A <b>Darkling </b>Draconic embodies both darkness, but also its allure. They know what words to whisper to extract pledges from mortals, but also when to appear as their worst nightmares. <br /> <br /> A <b>Elemental </b>Draconic appears aloof, not engaging socially much, but when contested, become a fierce opponent, however once they smash their opponents, they once again withdraw from affairs. <br /> <br /> A <b>Fairest </b>Draconic is the embodiment of majesty, and a forceful presence. Their voices could make a crowd into a mob, and their enemies cower in fear. <br /> <br /> A <b>Ogre </b>Draconic is fierce, slashing their enemies with powerful claws, and ripping them apart with their grand teeth. Their strength makes them hard to escape as well, refusing to back down for anyone. <br /> <br /> A <b>Wizened </b>Draconic is truly an amazing administrator, always knowing who needs what, and builds the grandest of homes for themselves. <br /> <br /> <br /> So... yeah, essentially, tried to take different chunks of both Dragons and perhaps more violent demons to get somewhere. This probably has quite a few issues, but still, hopefully something to help discussion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T19:28:58-07:00","id":242791,"title":"","content":"Probably going to do a brainspew on Elementals at some point here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=242471#post242471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I like over-associating darklings with fear. While it's a big part of their essential nature, at least in first edition, I feel like it would be weird to have two splats (darkling and autumn court) drawing from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Courts are coping mechanisms/stages of grief. Seemings strike me as this sort of explosion of action that you then have to deal with the psychological effects of afterwards. (The exception potentially being Wizened, who think their way through it a bit more.)<br /> <br /> Courts are about what you tell yourself, Seemings are about who you are (or, more accurately, were). The Summer Darkling can pound her chest and draw her sword and fight with the best of them, but she still remembers that when the cards were down and it really counted she was <i>afraid. </i>Maybe she refuses to let herself feel that way again, maybe she's just lying to herself, maybe she accepts it as part of her and drives forward along her chosen path regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T19:32:17-07:00","id":242793,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=240450#post240450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agency through chaos, power from unity and control.</div> </div> </div> </div>The word <i>chaos </i>used here does not match up with Elementals/Primal/Raw/Wyrd to me. Chaos also speaks destruction in a way that pulls against Agency and overlaps towards Ogres? Maybe just me. (chaos = state of confusion or disorder)<br /> <br /> The original descriptions of Elementals made them seem like living Supernature and/or expressions of raw Wyrd. The narrative emphasis was on their Otherness.<br /> I still think that's the cool aspect of being Elemental. An Elemental profile would subtract from Social and add to Wyrd.<br /> <br /> All the Lost drag themselves back to the mortal lands. All the Lost are <b>scarred </b>from the Durance. You can hide your scars. You can be proud of them also.<br /> <br /> Elementals dragged Domain back with them (using a descriptive offered earlier). They are still <b>wearing </b>their Durance in a way other Lost are not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T19:36:40-07:00","id":242795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=242793#post242793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The word <i>chaos </i>used here does not match up with Elementals/Primal/Raw/Wyrd to me. Chaos also speaks destruction in a way that pulls against Agency and overlaps towards Ogres? Maybe just me. (chaos = state of confusion or disorder)<br /> <br /> The original descriptions of Elementals made them seem like living Supernature and/or expressions of raw Wyrd. The narrative emphasis was on their Otherness.<br /> I still think that's the cool aspect of being Elemental. An Elemental profile would subtract from Social and add to Wyrd.<br /> <br /> All the Lost drag themselves back to the mortal lands. All the Lost are <b>scarred </b>from the Durance. You can hide your scars. You can be proud of them also.<br /> <br /> Elementals dragged Domain back with them (using a descriptive offered earlier). They are still <b>wearing </b>their Durance in a way other Lost are not.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This, really. <br /> <br /> Darklings are really what now is a little more difficult because I admit, Fear alone isn't really a way to define the splat per say.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T20:08:53-07:00","id":242807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=242795#post242795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, really.<br /> <br /> Darklings are really what now is a little more difficult because I admit, Fear alone isn't really a way to define the splat per say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that it's all pretty difficult, because we're not really sure <i>how</i> a lot of these things are coming together. The most we can do is just sort of lob ideas around haphazardly and see what sticks.<br /> <br /> Think I might just wind up making a megapost with as much concept-based stuff as I can fit in. Like recapping what each Seeming is about in 1.0 and potential ideas for what the whole Seeming Agency thing could mean in 2.0 just to get it all in one place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T22:10:22-07:00","id":242844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=242793#post242793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The word <i>chaos </i>used here does not match up with Elementals/Primal/Raw/Wyrd to me. Chaos also speaks destruction in a way that pulls against Agency and overlaps towards Ogres? Maybe just me. (chaos = state of confusion or disorder)<br /> <br /> The original descriptions of Elementals made them seem like living Supernature and/or expressions of raw Wyrd. The narrative emphasis was on their Otherness.<br /> I still think that's the cool aspect of being Elemental. An Elemental profile would subtract from Social and add to Wyrd.<br /> <br /> All the Lost drag themselves back to the mortal lands. All the Lost are <b>scarred </b>from the Durance. You can hide your scars. You can be proud of them also.<br /> <br /> Elementals dragged Domain back with them (using a descriptive offered earlier). They are still <b>wearing </b>their Durance in a way other Lost are not.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think some things need to be clarified about my approach and reasoning.<br /> <br /> Broad strokes first.<br /> <br /> 1)I don't feel beholden to obey the standards of the first edition.<br /> <br /> Okay, that's not true. I always begin each seeming with what was said in the first version. I work from that groundwork. Of course I do-I love the old material to no end.<br /> <br /> That said, keeping strictly to the old is not useful. It helps to think outside of the box and reinvent the wheel sometimes, and sticking to the old material like it was scripture does not allow the series to grow and evolve. I look to reinvent and reinterpret to breathe new life into the framework of changeling. I'm swapping the old lens with new ones and seeing if I get a brighter color. I don't want to settle.<br /> <br /> 2)This is immensely helpful for the new take on Seemings and Kiths. In the first version, Seeming and Kith were what happened to you. It may have traces of you in it-they can't make something from nothing, it has to be in you, but by and large you are crafted to serve Their purpose. Thus, certain things make sense within that context.<br /> <br /> But Huntsmen has clarified it's position on Seemings, and it's the exact opposite score. Kiths are inflicted on you by other, but your Seeming is <i>self-inflicted</i>, for better or for worse. This is why I think of Seemings as kinds of actions, particularly the further along I get in the writing process. I want to experiment more with that idea because it seems functional and useful.<br /> <br /> That's deviating. The point is that we can't keep <i>thinking</i> about the Seemings in the way we were taught, because those answers <i>don't</i> <i>apply</i>. The old should be incorporated and inform the new direction, sure, yeah, but it shouldn't drive it. And if you want proof that that works, allow me to refer you to Blood and Smoke(Which, by the way, is the only thing in Vampire that caused me to <i>like</i> Vampire, as context)<br /> <br /> 3)This becomes really, <i>really</i> important when you remember the first half of the debate was kind of about whether or not Elementals and/or Beasts served any kind of purpose and had any thematic strength of their own. I know there was at least one nostalgia ridden fool who really didn't want to let go of them(that fool was me), while other people were sad at the idea of it going(that was everyone else), but there wasn't compelling arguments based simply on the old to keep them around. We've been told they are staying, and I imagine that's because Dymphna has some great ideas for them(Don't disappoint us, we're counting on you!), but without information, it seems folly to assume the old stuff is strong enough to keep going. So, we find a better, sharper angle to make a compelling argument for their standing.<br /> <br /> Okay, so specific responses now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word <i>chaos </i>used here does not match up with Elementals/Primal/Raw/Wyrd to me. Chaos also speaks destruction in a way that pulls against Agency and overlaps towards Ogres? Maybe just me. (chaos = state of confusion or disorder)</div> </div> </div> </div>1)Minor Deviation: If there's something I like from DnD 4th Edition, it was their planes. Keeping relevant, the Elemental Chaos in particular was really appealing, this seething, chaotic ocean of creation and destruction that had no thought for longevity or purpose-that was for the Gods.<br /> <br /> To me, that's what nature feels like. Nevermind personal belief in creator figures with purposes for reality(Hey Brahma!), nature is one chaotic mess. THe purer it gets, the less controlled it is. Forces just go, consequences be damned. I'm not moved, personally, much by the idea of limpid pools or casually burning fireplaces or gentle breezes. The elements that make up this world are in action, in motion, never stopping, because where's the point in that? THe endurance argument from earlier ties into that-they don't endure for endurance sake, they endure because <i>why stop</i>. Even mountains and trees invite motion in and of themselves, in my mind anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Anyways</b>, back to chaos. Well, Okay, I needed that. I need to establish my thoughts of a world in motion before talking about that. Chaos in this case means confusion, it means kinetic energy, it means not giving people time to breathe. I imagine Elementals escaping because they took the motion and energy of the world and let it do it's things in unconventional ways. It seems to fit with what Dave said on the subject:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David A. Hill Jr.</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appeal to the outside world. Appeal to the environment. Did you burn your Keeper's mansion? Did you trap his hounds in a rockslide during your escape? Did you set a trap?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about <i>destruction</i>, It's about <i>distraction</i>. It's about having so much going on you can't even hope to think straight(ironically, that's a set up for the Beasts, but I need to brew on that still).<br /> <br /> It fit in with other motifs I noticed with Elementals-their Stranger like tendency to control the area, or at least create the impression they do, as well as the fact they more directly tap into and wear a Keeper's power. If everyone is disoriented and unable to act, then that means everyone's equal in that moment, meaning you can actually enact agency freely. And when you work to ensure nothing happens to you again, you want to be the only person who, in a sea of chaos, is the one who knows what's going on and can act <i>without</i> disorientation. Easy way to do that? Control the world around you <i>intimately</i>.<br /> <br /> Ogres don't do that. Ogres are the little kids who snap and stab their bullies a number of times before telling them to leave them the fuck alone or they'll finish the job(if they don't inherently). Sure, the source of strife is confused, but that's not what's really letting an Ogre decide the course of his life-it's the threat to their life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original descriptions of Elementals made them seem like living Supernature and/or expressions of raw Wyrd. The narrative emphasis was on their Otherness.<br /> I still think that's the cool aspect of being Elemental. An Elemental profile would subtract from Social and add to Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my spliel on why I'm doing things differently.<br /> <br /> Still, I keep those elements in there. Remember that essentially everything within a domain <i>is </i>a Stranger. When you turn their world against Them, use <i>Them</i> as your method of Agency, that's going to bleed itself into you. It's like becoming cancer in a Stranger's body. When you get back, that just makes you a walking tumor of the enemy.<br /> <br /> Er, with all due respect to Promethean, that actually <i>has </i>walking tumors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the Lost drag themselves back to the mortal lands. All the Lost are <b>scarred </b>from the Durance. You can hide your scars. You can be proud of them also.<br /> <br /> Elementals dragged Domain back with them (using a descriptive offered earlier). They are still <b>wearing </b>their Durance in a way other Lost are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of find myself back at the entire &quot;This is my version of the 'Don't they all do that?' thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the one hand, yes. Again, I would describe Elementals as living, mobile Domains. They got involved with their world in an intimate way others didn't.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, and refraining from the entire &quot;Dreamscapes as an expression of inner worlds bearing Strange scars&quot; angle....well, don't they all?<br /> <br /> Elementals wear a <i>place</i> for a face, and that's hard to get around, but is a Fairest's majesty or a Ogre's roughness really that different? Aren't they all wearing their Durance(Kith)? Aren't they all wearing the choices they made to get out of it(Seeming)?<br /> <br /> In fact, what's the difference between the Fairest and the Elemental on that score? Yes, Elementals became the board, but Fairest <i>became the players</i>. That's not a great argument, there's always been a certain kinship between Elementals and Fairest on that front, but still.<br /> <br /> I dunno, within the old version that was an easy thing to accept. But within the new one, where you bear a Seeming on your shoulders for your own choice and reasons, I have trouble swallowing it.<br /> <br /> .......................................<br /> <br /> And that's it for my response. Again, I'm not sure how much it matters that I put this out there. It's food for thought, and it would give me a second place to touch off from while writing Elementals. I don't expect people to agree with me, I'm just making do with what I have and trying to find some solutions, rather than continue walking around in circles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-28-2014, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T23:52:03-07:00","id":242870,"title":"","content":"Going off your response, <br /> <br /> You say self-inflicted. Well... let me see if I can interpret that for more pain, which I say because I'd argue Agency has a cost, even if it is far preferable to being held by a Keeper.<br /> <br /> To go to the Elemental, who I insist is not solely defined by being part of nature, means to me making a conscious choice to give up part of your humanity in order to get free to your Environment. <br /> <br /> As I said, I don't view Elementals as purely natural, or even close, not when we had ones of Pollution, the Mankin(I admit, that was an odd one out to the point of spawning a new Seeming, but still), and in a way, ones made of Electricity I wouldn't necessarily call natural. <br /> <br /> Why does that matter? Well, to me, that's because one of the things holding Elementals back earlier in the discussion was that I think we were tying them too much to nature, when that wasn't inherently the case in 1.0, with all the exception Kiths for example, and for that matter, where in 1.0 it was suggested they came from in supplements, such as massive cities. Cities are hardly nature, and that was one of the big locations for Elementals to originate from. <br /> <br /> It also matters because I think this could define them far more in 2.0. Now, being an Elemental meant that you chose to do something with your Environment. You chose to try becoming more in tune with rocks, wind, glass, or what have you, and in the process, became partially like that. Alienation is still a theme, but now that Choice hangs over everything you do when you escape Arcadia. The same dilemma happens to every Seeming, which is that you chose to become something different from, and in some cases less than in some ways, human, in order to get free. <br /> <br /> Going off that last one, Fairest chose to become like their Keepers to escape them. Beasts chose to embrace animalistic parts of themselves to escape. Darklings chose to be willing to use fear, and anything else needed really, to escape. Ogres chose to become violent, to the point where that violence now defines who they are on some level. Even Wizened had to choose to embrace a craft to the point where it changed who they were in ways that are irreversible. <br /> <br /> And painful change is what Changeling the Lost is all about, whether its inflicted by someone else upon you, or you inflict it on yourself.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Trying to figure out a different way to approach 2.0, if you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T23:53:48-07:00","id":242871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=242807#post242807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that it's all pretty difficult, because we're not really sure <i>how</i> a lot of these things are coming together. The most we can do is just sort of lob ideas around haphazardly and see what sticks.<br /> <br /> Think I might just wind up making a megapost with as much concept-based stuff as I can fit in. Like recapping what each Seeming is about in 1.0 and potential ideas for what the whole Seeming Agency thing could mean in 2.0 just to get it all in one place.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. <br /> <br /> Now added more thoughts on Agency, which I'll now focus on more to try and grasp ideas for 2.0 better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T00:57:55-07:00","id":242889,"title":"","content":"I suppose my thing is that I'm a little more divorced from the entire &quot;Sacrifice Humanity&quot; spliel. There's a few reasons for that.<br /> <br /> Not really a substantial reason on it's own) I don't feel like going pro- or -anti-transhumanism with this sort of stuff.<br /> <br /> 1) On a physical=spiritual level, I've never understood nor brooked with the entire changing of physicality makes you more or less human. I'm thinking of Shadowrun here, for the record, where you literally lose your soul each time you got cybernetic implants(that translated into a diminished ability to do magic or whatever). I think the mentality of a person who would gladly swap their body for cybernetics is more likely to diminish humanity, but that's because the person is already setting a stage, which they don't nessecarily need to act on. I believe in humanity being stripped from you, and I believed in the entire &quot;Live like a tree for so long and you lose humanity&quot; thing the Fae did, but when you accept something to yourself, I don't see that as voluntarily giving up your humanity.<br /> <br /> I really don't believe that in the context of the sort of moment Seemings seem to exist in either. I mean, granted, Seemings are probably actually things that take time to be grafted on-if anything, I will freely admit I probably have been presenting this as a snap change where it's more likely at least months worth of slowly acclimating, which is where the inhumanity comes in. But that said, I have trouble with seeing that as a deliberate slicing off of humanity.<br /> <br /> 2)In fact, I have some problem with the words &quot;Sacrifice Humanity&quot; to begin with, namely because I find myself asking a question:<br /> <br /> What, exactly, does that mean?<br /> <br /> Like, I get it on the prolonged exposure front. It takes time to become the Sand Dune that is also the Guy You Are Screwing Over. But let's put this in, well ,moments. Because I have trouble seeing it outside of the exposure front.<br /> <br /> See, I can see shooting a guy as sacrifice humanity. I can see breaking a Keeper's leg while he's crying and begging you to stop as sacrificing humanity. I can see whispering dirty lies in the wrong circumstances for visitors as sacrificing humanity. I can see a lot of things done as sacrificing humanity.<br /> <br /> But, like endurance, you just say &quot;Sacrifice humanity&quot; and I'm like &quot;What does that mean?&quot;. Because by itself, it's almost meaningless.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying mentality doesn't play a part. I have been, at times, an inhuman fuck, and it's not because I did anything(although let's not pretend there weren't times), but simply because I framed my mind to think...well, to diminish people by huge scores. But you <i>have</i> to do something, and <i>you have to suggest the nature of it</i>.<br /> <br /> Let's get a little frank here.Doing something to assert your agency, particularly in the way you'd need to escape Arcadia, runs the risk of psychopathic behavior, if not solipsistic. You are literally telling the world-a far more literal breathing, thinking world with purpose-that <i>you</i> come first. <i>You</i> are more important. What <i>you want</i> is more important than <i>anything else</i> there. That what <i>you</i> say <i>goes</i>. You have to! You need to be bigger than the world in order to get out! You need to take the world's lunch money! Or at least make it think you will.<br /> <br /> But doesn't that mean <i>everyone who does that risks sacrificing humanity?</i> Particularly if there are others you aren't saving?<br /> <br /> That's an extremely pessmistic view on that last note, but at the same time-you do have to admit you're making choices, and that does mean you elevate some people's worth over others, and it comes down to you asserting your priorities over everyone else. There may be nothing you can do about it the choices you have, but it's still a choice.<br /> <br /> God damn, that's really pessimistic.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the point of the matter is that you can't just tell me &quot;Sacrifice humanity for power/agency&quot;-or, rather, you can, but it doesn't satisfy me. I need to know what you did. I need it to suggest what sort of person and decisions make an Elemental, and &quot;Sacrifice humanity&quot; doesn't mean anything to me in that context.<br /> <br /> Of course, all this needs to be framed in with the following in mind.<br /> <br /> 3)<i>Of course &quot;sacrifice humanity&quot; is part of it.</i><br /> <br /> I suppose I need to clarify that this is like endurance. How?<br /> <br /> In that I'm not saying this isn't important or this isn't a thing.<br /> <br /> Because it is. It's an important thing. This is totally a thing that is part of Elementals. It's there for a reason.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with <i>sacrificing humanity</i>. I don't have a problem with <i>endurance.</i><br /> <br /> My problem is that those things, by themselves, only worked in the first edition. In the new one, it needs context. It cannot stand by itself, or at least I think so. I think they are natural consequences of the things that make Elementals, but that said, <i>they are consequences</i>. They are effects in need of a cause, branches in search of a tree trunk.<br /> <br /> And of course, you may disagree with me. I felt like looking at those,I was looking inside the box. I moved out, I read everything the old books had on Elementals, I looked at what they could do, I looked at the in-depths discussions, and I reworked the material to find something that felt like a root answer from the new direction that fulfilled what was said. And again, feel free to disagree.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of someone who feels they can express their choice and persona through throwing everyone else off their game(Agency through chaos), who strives to do so by being intimately in control of their surroundings and uniting with other elements/aspects(Power from unity and control/The Ones Who Change The Game) leads to someone who has the power to handle the odd twists, turns, and winds of the adversaries(Endurance) and someone who objectifies their world and understands it as their own game rig and what any element can be used for(Sacrificing humanity,specifically on the social level).<br /> <br /> I can totally be wrong!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:30:46-07:00","id":243056,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the notion of \u201cElement\u201d needs some broadening beyond the classical elements. I was just thinking of Steve Jackson Games\u2019 <b><i>In Nomine</i></b>, and particularly about its <b><i>Ethereal Player\u2019s Guide</i></b>; in that book, an Element could be one of the Classical Elements (Earth, Air, Fire, or Water); but it could also be an Astronomical Concept (e.g., the Sun), an Emotion (e.g., Fear), a kind of Information (e.g., News), a type of Life (e.g., Beasts), a Sense (e.g., Light), an element of Society (e.g., Family), a type of Structure (e.g., a Home), a form of Struggle, a kind of Tech, Terrain, Wealth, or Weather. <br /> <br /> In <b><i>Changeling</i></b>, I think that an Elemental needs to be very Kith-specific: to an Elemental, every Kith represents a concept, an <i>idea</i> around which the Kith is built \u2014 and the Elemental internalizes the Kith\u2019s essential concept and starts identifying with <i>what the Kith is</i> more than with people: an Elemental Smith is going to be more comfortable around the things the Smith makes than around people; an Elemental Hunterheart identifies more with predatory animals than with people; an Elemental Muse identifies more with the notion of inspiring people than with the people that he tries to inspire; an Elemental Snowskin becomes a personification of ice and snow. <br /> <br /> And, like a Chinese Finger Puzzle, by internalizing the core element of his Kith, the Elemental loosens the strictures that were placed on him, gaining more freedom to wander Arcadia on his own \u2014 and to leave. That paradox \u2014 gaining freedom by surrendering it \u2014 is the heart of the Elemental\u2019s agency. <br /> <br /> As for the distinction between Beasts and Elementals: Beasts are very visceral, driven by emotions and instincts; Elementals are very cerebral, driven by concepts and abstractions. <br /> <br /> \u2026which gets me thinking: maybe the Seemings exist in opposing pairs? Beasts and Elementals; Darklings and Fairest; Ogres and Wizened. Or not; I\u2019m just spitballing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T07:21:54-07:00","id":243079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=243056#post243056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Elemental loosens the strictures that were placed on him, gaining more freedom to wander Arcadia on his own \u2014 and to leave. That paradox \u2014 gaining freedom by surrendering it \u2014 is the heart of the Elemental\u2019s agency.<br /> <br /> As for the distinction between Beasts and Elementals: Beasts are very visceral, driven by emotions and instincts; Elementals are very cerebral, driven by concepts and abstractions.<br /> <br /> \u2026which gets me thinking: maybe the Seemings exist in opposing pairs? Beasts and Elementals; Darklings and Fairest; Ogres and Wizened. Or not; I\u2019m just spitballing here.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems pretty good. I like it.<br /> <br /> And it may be worth looking at the Seemings as Yin/Yang.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:07:42-07:00","id":243102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=242889#post242889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...of course, you may disagree with me. I felt like looking at those,I was looking inside the box. I moved out, I read everything the old books had on Elementals, I looked at what they could do, I looked at the in-depths discussions, and I reworked the material to find something that felt like a root answer from the new direction that fulfilled what was said. And again, feel free to disagree.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of someone who feels they can express their choice and persona through throwing everyone else off their game (Agency through chaos), who strives to do so by being intimately in control of their surroundings and uniting with other elements/aspects (Power from unity and control/The Ones Who Change The Game) leads to someone who has the power to handle the odd twists, turns, and winds of the adversaries (Endurance) and someone who objectifies their world and understands it as their own game rig and what any element can be used for(Sacrificing humanity,specifically on the social level).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you just promoted the Kith Tricksters to a new Seeming: Tricksters.<br /> <br /> I agree with a lot of what you're saying about approach and appreciate the extra bits about how you'd like Elementals to work.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:55:46-07:00","id":243180,"title":"","content":"<b>--Seeming as Agency--</b><br /> <br /> We can really break this down into three possible options. <b> What</b>, <b>How</b>, and <b>Why</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>What</b> is the simplest, it is the act itself. While it strikes me as a bit limiting, thematically, it's also surprisingly flexible as far as grey areas go. Say you seduce someone and stab them in the back when their guard is down. Would this make you a Fairest or a Darkling? You could make convincing arguments for each, really.<br /> <br /> <b>How</b> is a little more open to interpretation. Rather than limit specific actions to specific Seemings, it places the focus on performance and context. This is my guess as to what the final product will most likely be. It's just defined enough to be limiting and just broad enough to be accommodating to players' concepts.<br /> <br /> <b>Why</b> focuses on the motivations of the characters. It forgoes the actions themselves and looks to the source of the characters' agency. These are the least defined, sticking to very general emotions and concepts. Take my previous example, with actions driven by Fear, Beauty, Anger, etc. I generally view these as less of a slow build and more of a spur of the moment revelation or surge of action. They're the thing in you that kicks off the &quot;Enough is Enough&quot; moment.<br /> <br /> <b>--Six Seemings--</b><br /> <br /> <b>Beasts</b> (and Elementals, who we'll get to later) have the problem of coming from a catchall seeming. In 1.0 they were mostly defined as a collection of &quot;Beast Kiths&quot; and even with the new rules, it would be easy for someone to just group all the beastial Kiths together for the sake of organization. So far, the major thing I'm seeing people try to carry over is the focus on Instinct. I would argue that's a solid enough concept for a foundation and in keeping with the spirit of 1.0's Beasts without focusing too much on a certain type of Beast-ness. (IE - Loyalty leaves out the nasty buggers, Ferociousness leaves out the bunnies or w/e.) The other issue I feel Beasts (and again Elementals) have is the 1.0-style physical manifestations of their seemings. With 2.0's seemings being a little more subtle and not something, as David mentioned, people will wear on their sleeves, it seems a bit odd for someone to roll around with big ol' lobster claws for hands. Granted, it could be assumed that maybe their durance was spent as some sort of lobster-carpenter or something, but I think it would probably work a bit better if the Beast seeming worked a bit more subtley than a simple kith. IE - Animal Eyes, Feral Presence, the nondescript claws/pointy teeth that like every changeling piece of art has, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Darklings</b> are a simple enough concept. Sneaky, creepy, crawly, slimy, and a bunch of other not so fun things. Their most common themes are things like Fear, Moral Ambiguity, and Stealth. I see their escapes as being defined by at least one of those three things, fairly easily as it is. As for manifestation, &quot;Dark and Shadowy&quot; seems to be popular. To be honest, Darklings feel pretty cut and dry.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest</b> are a teensy bit tougher. There seems to be a tendency to jump straight to sexy and gorgeous. Aesthetics are certainly a major part of them, and I think that should reflect in the manifestation of their seeming without a doubt, but I think its a bit more complex when you try to link it to agency. The first thing everyone jumps to is &quot;Seduced the Guard,&quot; which I think fits, but there's definitely more to Fairest than just bonkfests. Besides aesthetics and the appreciation thereof, other major themes with Fairest seem to be artistry, majesty, brilliance, and just about anything else you could think of as beautiful. On the darker side of things you see stuff like social manipulation, addiction/desire, borderline sociopathy, and more social manipulation.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogres</b>, like Darklings, are pretty cut and dry. Anger, aggression, and violence. I think they might be the one seeming that nobody has any real arguments about, which can be a good or bad thing depending on how you look at it.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened</b> are about the only ones I can see premeditating their escapes. If any seeming could be a slow-burn its them. Their time in Arcadia has granted them a certain set of skills... skills that make them a nightmare fo- Anyway, they seem to be defined by their crafts, their intellect, and their skill with magic. Though all changelings are good with magic, Wizened are definitely a bit more Gandalf about it. I think with the breakdown of the 1.0 Seeming/Kith system, the focus on crafts will have to broaden a bit. They might need to start bringing in some of the stranger changeling jobs, like living torch (or lobster-carpenter!) As far as how their seeming manifests itself? I honestly have no idea.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver saved me some time:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=243056#post243056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the notion of \u201cElement\u201d needs some broadening beyond the classical elements. I was just thinking of Steve Jackson Games\u2019 <b><i>In Nomine</i></b>, and particularly about its <b><i>Ethereal Player\u2019s Guide</i></b>; in that book, an Element could be one of the Classical Elements (Earth, Air, Fire, or Water); but it could also be an Astronomical Concept (e.g., the Sun), an Emotion (e.g., Fear), a kind of Information (e.g., News), a type of Life (e.g., Beasts), a Sense (e.g., Light), an element of Society (e.g., Family), a type of Structure (e.g., a Home), a form of Struggle, a kind of Tech, Terrain, Wealth, or Weather.<br /> <br /> In <b><i>Changeling</i></b>, I think that an Elemental needs to be very Kith-specific: to an Elemental, every Kith represents a concept, an <i>idea</i> around which the Kith is built \u2014 and the Elemental internalizes the Kith\u2019s essential concept and starts identifying with <i>what the Kith is</i> more than with people: an Elemental Smith is going to be more comfortable around the things the Smith makes than around people; an Elemental Hunterheart identifies more with predatory animals than with people; an Elemental Muse identifies more with the notion of inspiring people than with the people that he tries to inspire; an Elemental Snowskin becomes a personification of ice and snow.<br /> <br /> And, like a Chinese Finger Puzzle, by internalizing the core element of his Kith, the Elemental loosens the strictures that were placed on him, gaining more freedom to wander Arcadia on his own \u2014 and to leave. That paradox \u2014 gaining freedom by surrendering it \u2014 is the heart of the Elemental\u2019s agency.<br /> <br /> As for the distinction between Beasts and Elementals: Beasts are very visceral, driven by emotions and instincts; Elementals are very cerebral, driven by concepts and abstractions.<br /> <br /> \u2026which gets me thinking: maybe the Seemings exist in opposing pairs? Beasts and Elementals; Darklings and Fairest; Ogres and Wizened. Or not; I\u2019m just spitballing here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thiiis. People forget the other definition of Elemental is &quot;basic, fundamental, or elementary.&quot; With the split of Kiths and Seemings, Elementals become less about earth, wind, and fire, and more about distillation of concept (IE - Kiths).<br /> <br /> Also, I absolutely think the pairs thing works, except I would pair off Fairest and Wizened because they're basically Art vs. Craft, Heart vs Mind. Darklings and Ogres then become avoidance vs confrontation or direct vs indirect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:34:37-07:00","id":243271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=243056#post243056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the distinction between Beasts and Elementals: Beasts are very visceral, driven by emotions and instincts; Elementals are very cerebral, driven by concepts and abstractions.<br /> <br /> \u2026which gets me thinking: maybe the Seemings exist in opposing pairs? Beasts and Elementals; Darklings and Fairest; Ogres and Wizened. Or not; I\u2019m just spitballing here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite, but I was thinking on this last night.<br /> <br /> I noticed in the original that Elementals seemed to have a spiritual kinship to both Beasts and to the Fairest,with certain similar themes running through on each side. I'm not 100% percent sure if others had it, but heaven knows I love this game's sense of symmetry.<br /> <br /> Not to pimp my own stuff, but I also noticed a correlation between the Wizened and Elementals as I described them-not a kinship, but definitely grounds for a stereotype.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, so you just ripped off their entire modus oeprandi to escape, and now you're relying on it? Why not just wear a 'Kick Me' sign around the guy you just booted, too?&quot;<br /> <br /> And ultimately that's my take on it-this sort of stuff, this kinship of sorts, is what makes for stereotypes. Ideally they should all have some things in common with each other, and some things that grate on them, Because people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In <b><i>Changeling</i></b>, I think that an Elemental needs to be very Kith-specific:</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the sort of mentality that led to us question whether or not Elementals deserved to stick around? I think we can engineer Elementals that aren't Kith specific, and indeed that's what the challenge is.<br /> <br /> As for divorcing from the classical elements, sure. I'm down with that. Teddy bear in an ocean of plush!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:35:49-07:00","id":243272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=243102#post243102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you just promoted the Kith Tricksters to a new Seeming: Tricksters.<br /> <br /> I agree with a lot of what you're saying about approach and appreciate the extra bits about how you'd like Elementals to work.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, a lot of tricksters ended up in the elemental section of Winter Masques.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T14:31:55-07:00","id":243429,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I say we focus on <b>Why.</b> To me, Agency is about choices, although I'll grant you ArcaneArts perhaps not sacrificing your humanity, and Why seems more the root of choice.<br /> For Dataweaver... you made some excellent points, although I still find myself sticking with the environment somehow. I've got an idea where I'll write a short story like segment for my idea of an Elemental, but, can't right now. Obviously, what an Elemental may be will change a lot with the more we learn, but I hope to at least get across an idea of what an Elemental could be in this new version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T19:10:25-07:00","id":243541,"title":"","content":"What I mean by \u201cKith-specific\u201d isn\u2019t \u201cElementals should be specific to certain Kiths\u201d, but rather \u201cwhat it means to be an Elemental is heavily reliant on what your Kith is\u201d. Illuminated Minutia summarized it quite well: a distillation of the core concept.<br /> <br /> On the \u201cenvironment\u201d thing, I can see that as being something that tends to show up when applying the Elemental Seeming to the elemental Kiths (note the use of capitalization); but as a general thing that could work well with <i>any</i> Kith? I\u2019m not seeing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-28-2014, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T21:00:48-07:00","id":243591,"title":"","content":"I'm looking through the list of Kiths and I can see several that can be grouped together and a few that I just can't see working with any other Seeming. I feel there will need to be a lot of abstraction of the Kiths.<br /> <br /> For those that enjoyed doing Kithless: maybe a sort of &quot;Blank Slate&quot; Kith where the choice of Seeming ends up being the primary definer as an option? Like, &quot;your keeper used you as whatever was needed at the time: playmate or prey, wildfire or guard, servant or thief; always different, always mutable&quot; and &quot;your agency finally defined you, before you were in a state of flux and by your own will you solidified into something more.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T23:49:53-07:00","id":243669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=243541#post243541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean by \u201cKith-specific\u201d isn\u2019t \u201cElementals should be specific to certain Kiths\u201d, but rather \u201cwhat it means to be an Elemental is heavily reliant on what your Kith is\u201d. Illuminated Minutia summarized it quite well: a distillation of the core concept.<br /> <br /> On the \u201cenvironment\u201d thing, I can see that as being something that tends to show up when applying the Elemental Seeming to the elemental Kiths (note the use of capitalization); but as a general thing that could work well with <i>any</i> Kith? I\u2019m not seeing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. You make an excellent point, in regards to the environment issue. Well... hmm.<br /> <br /> Need to think about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-29-2014, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T00:18:16-07:00","id":243696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=243591#post243591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those that enjoyed doing Kithless: maybe a sort of &amp;quot;Blank Slate&amp;quot; Kith where the choice of Seeming ends up being the primary definer as an option? Like, &amp;quot;your keeper used you as whatever was needed at the time: playmate or prey, wildfire or guard, servant or thief; always different, always mutable&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;your agency finally defined you, before you were in a state of flux and by your own will you solidified into something more.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like the notion of the Fae-Touched and Enchanted that appeared in <b>Equinox Road</b>, though their mechanics needed work: basically, they\u2019re humans who were taken to Faerie and who managed to get away before the transformation into a changeling was complete. In effect, Enchanted Mortals were only there long enough to acquire the ability to see through the Mask; and the Fae-Touched were there long enough that they started to transform, but didn\u2019t quite get far enough to become changelings. <br /> <br /> For the Enchanted, I could easily see taking the same route that <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> did with \u201cUnseen Sense: God-Machine\u201d: there are certain mortals who, for various reasons, automatically see through the Mask. The reasons can vary drastically, including but not limited to \u201cyou were taken to Faerie, but were rescued before it could change you too much\u201d. <br /> <br /> The Fae-Touched, OTOH, ought to be <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s counterpart to <b>Vampire</b>\u2019s Ghouls: they <i>were</i> taken to Arcadia, and it <i>did</i> start to change them; but they managed to get out before it had finished breaking down their soul. A Fae-Touched would be a lesser template with \u201cWyrd 0\u201d and several Changeling-like features; but they\u2019d still be human, having made the harrowing trip back through the Hedge before their Integrity was reduced to zero. The relevance to this thread: with the new takes on Kith and Seeming, I cannot see a Fae-Touched having a Kith: that becomes part and parcel of actually becoming a changeling, and you cannot have one without the other. But I <i>can</i> see them getting a Seeming under its new definition. So if you want a Seeming without a Kith, play a Fae-Touched mortal. <br /> <br /> Conversely, <i>very few humans</i> make it back as fae-touched; those who do had help, or get back half-mad (i.e., Integrity very nearly depleted); probably both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T06:08:02-07:00","id":243837,"title":"","content":"So I read this entire thread on two bus rides and am sad I wasn't part of this from the beginning - while I still haven't gotten to play a game of CtL, I love the fluff and have done some CtL-related writing.... Anywho, big apology if my phone, which I am posting on, kills my formatting - when I get home tonight I will correct it if I can.<br /> <br /> So two things which I think might start new conversation. <br /> <br /> Firstly: if Seeming is Agency, does that mean when your Keeper catches you, they will take it away? Seeming is an identity you have used as a launching-off point, the act or process which has reframed your invention of self, an active portion of you not made by your Keeper. They might want prey, but not clever prey - servants, but not brutal servants - etc. It is more integral to you than a mask they are taking off, but still little more than a bad habit or flaw they need to smooth out. I have this image of someone\u2019s Beast-ness being peeled away like the skin of a banana, leaving the poor re-captured Lost as baseless and stunned as could be possible. Y\u2019know. Awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, there has been alot of discussion about how Darklings betray or sacrifice, or Elementals unbind or disassociate, or whatever\u2026 that got me thinking of psychological defense mechanisms, which I think are just as quite flavorful to a game of Beautiful Madness. According to wikipedia, Anna Freud numbered them as<br /> <br /> 1. Repression<br /> 2. Regression<br /> 3. Reaction formation<br /> 4. Isolation<br /> 5. Undoing<br /> 6. Projection<br /> 7. Introjection<br /> 8. Turning against one\u2019s own person<br /> 9. Reversal into the opposite<br /> 10. Sublimation or displacement.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know about you, but I am immediately drawing parallels to different Seemings - different tactics and techniques of preserving or re-creating the self and different ways of leveraging your personal currency during your time of distress to move beyond it.<br /> <br /> Hope some of this helps! ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T15:43:19-07:00","id":244376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=243837#post243837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I read this entire thread on two bus rides and am sad I wasn't part of this from the beginning - while I still haven't gotten to play a game of CtL, I love the fluff and have done some CtL-related writing.... Anywho, big apology if my phone, which I am posting on, kills my formatting - when I get home tonight I will correct it if I can.<br /> <br /> So two things which I think might start new conversation.<br /> <br /> Firstly: if Seeming is Agency, does that mean when your Keeper catches you, they will take it away? Seeming is an identity you have used as a launching-off point, the act or process which has reframed your invention of self, an active portion of you not made by your Keeper. They might want prey, but not clever prey - servants, but not brutal servants - etc. It is more integral to you than a mask they are taking off, but still little more than a bad habit or flaw they need to smooth out. I have this image of someone\u2019s Beast-ness being peeled away like the skin of a banana, leaving the poor re-captured Lost as baseless and stunned as could be possible. Y\u2019know. Awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, there has been alot of discussion about how Darklings betray or sacrifice, or Elementals unbind or disassociate, or whatever\u2026 that got me thinking of psychological defense mechanisms, which I think are just as quite flavorful to a game of Beautiful Madness. According to wikipedia, Anna Freud numbered them as<br /> <br /> 1. Repression<br /> 2. Regression<br /> 3. Reaction formation<br /> 4. Isolation<br /> 5. Undoing<br /> 6. Projection<br /> 7. Introjection<br /> 8. Turning against one\u2019s own person<br /> 9. Reversal into the opposite<br /> 10. Sublimation or displacement.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know about you, but I am immediately drawing parallels to different Seemings - different tactics and techniques of preserving or re-creating the self and different ways of leveraging your personal currency during your time of distress to move beyond it.<br /> <br /> Hope some of this helps! ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>The second gives me a lot of ideas, to say the least, and was something I now wish I had thought of earlier!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T07:38:44-07:00","id":246798,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna have to be one of the people who disagree with the idea that Seemings decide your escape. Sure, Kiths deciding what a fae did to you, I mean, that's true of the last book too in a way, you are shaped by the fae and the end result is going to be an ice monster or a lizard creature or a walking statue, otherwise changelings would just be totally-normal-but-enchanted humans.<br /> <br /> Seemings defining escape though seems... limiting, to me. Maybe my strength-based ogre couldn't escape by strength alone, made a deal with the fae and now has to deal with the consequences of that deal throughout the story, their one moment of weakness, where physical strength wasn't enough.<br /> <br /> But under this, that'd make them a fairest, maybe, or something.<br /> <br /> Gameplay mechanics should guide a backstory, a character with high intelligence and intelligence-based skills will probably be well educated, but it shouldn't <i>decide</i> a backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3801-invertin","name":"invertin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T09:01:36-07:00","id":246846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>invertin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=246798#post246798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna have to be one of the people who disagree with the idea that Seemings decide your escape. Sure, Kiths deciding what a fae did to you, I mean, that's true of the last book too in a way, you are shaped by the fae and the end result is going to be an ice monster or a lizard creature or a walking statue, otherwise changelings would just be totally-normal-but-enchanted humans.<br /> <br /> Seemings defining escape though seems... limiting, to me. Maybe my strength-based ogre couldn't escape by strength alone, made a deal with the fae and now has to deal with the consequences of that deal throughout the story, their one moment of weakness, where physical strength wasn't enough.<br /> <br /> But under this, that'd make them a fairest, maybe, or something.<br /> <br /> Gameplay mechanics should guide a backstory, a character with high intelligence and intelligence-based skills will probably be well educated, but it shouldn't <i>decide</i> a backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I think defining your Seeming by the <b>Why</b> of your escape works better than the <b>What</b> or <b>How</b>. Like say your Ogre is just so angry that they'll cut a deal with the devil himself, damn the consequences. If the Seeming is a reflection of the motivatior it gives you a far more flexible system than simply saying &quot;Well if you punch something you're an ogre.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T10:08:30-07:00","id":246882,"title":"","content":"Its more the idea of nature vs. nurture though, isn't it? You aren't 'born' a musician - you might have good genes an intuitive grasp of the rules, and savant-like innate skills, but you still need to be introduced to the concept and given an instrument (or at least hear someone sing?).<br /> <br /> The kith is the role you are 'born' to when taken. The seeming is what you do with it? It might not be definitively 'in your escape you got ogrey' so much as 'the story of your durance and flight has shaped you into this role. On your way out of the Fae, please keep your legs and arms away fron the soul-shredding thorns, and here's your report card for the semester which says 'ogre' on it.<br /> <br /> Don't interpret it as &quot;seeming=escape plan&quot; so strictly. That way lies madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T10:31:04-07:00","id":246913,"title":"","content":"It also seems backwards to read it as &quot;Seeming decides your escape.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your escape decides your Seeming. If you write up a backstory first and apply the character traits second, your Seeming is determined by how you wrote the escape. You're only limited if you approach it from the intent of &quot;I'm making a Fairest,&quot; but that's because you're limiting yourself by deciding your Seeming first and then writing your background to match it.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with either approach from a player use perspective, but if you're picking traits first you're always going to limit your background options because you need to explain how those traits came about. The limitation is in the style of character design, not the concept of Seemings being defined by the character's escape from the Gentry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T10:50:46-07:00","id":246947,"title":"","content":"Another thing to remember is the Seeming is described as agency, not specifically escape, which is one reason I think it's important to focus on the <b>Why</b> aspect. It internalizes the conflict instead of making it about flipping switch X or performing action Y. While the end result can certainly be a burst of action or motion or decisiveness, what's important is the build up that. It might take years, it might take seconds, but that emotional tipping point strikes me as what's important about the way new Seemings are going to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T06:22:11-07:00","id":247786,"title":"","content":"I think the what and how are perfectly fine as long as it's viewed from the context of how the character thought about his or her escape. It avoids the &quot;everyone who does this specific thing becomes X&quot; while still playing well with the initial idea (again, kind of like geist where you can be poisoned by a snake bite and be striken, silent, or possibly even torn or forgotten). As I understand it, at least, the idea is that you get your seeming and your seeming is colored by your kith. The way that happens (and this may just be my interpretation) is that your choices Broke the kith in some small way, the same way that it broke the story the keeper was trying to push you through, and that's why it changes you enough on a metaphysical level that you read differently to different contracts and such. I'm not entirely opposed to the Why thing but I'm still not sold on it.<br /> <br /> Also, curiously (not intended as criticism), when do you see the seeming as forming for the changeling? would it come right when they resolve to leave (when the Why is fully formed) or when they actually take action (when the Why is followed through on). Also, if someone makes multiple escape attempts, potentially with different reasons between them, how does that affect their seeming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T07:26:44-07:00","id":247837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=247786#post247786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the what and how are perfectly fine as long as it's viewed from the context of how the character thought about his or her escape. It avoids the &quot;everyone who does this specific thing becomes X&quot; while still playing well with the initial idea (again, kind of like geist where you can be poisoned by a snake bite and be striken, silent, or possibly even torn or forgotten). As I understand it, at least, the idea is that you get your seeming and your seeming is colored by your kith. The way that happens (and this may just be my interpretation) is that your choices Broke the kith in some small way, the same way that it broke the story the keeper was trying to push you through, and that's why it changes you enough on a metaphysical level that you read differently to different contracts and such. I'm not entirely opposed to the Why thing but I'm still not sold on it.<br /> <br /> Also, curiously (not intended as criticism), when do you see the seeming as forming for the changeling? would it come right when they resolve to leave (when the Why is fully formed) or when they actually take action (when the Why is followed through on). Also, if someone makes multiple escape attempts, potentially with different reasons between them, how does that affect their seeming?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think Seeming is a little different for everyone. It comes during a defining moment. That could be when you get the gall to plan. It could be when you do some decisive thing in the escape. It could be when you reach the Hedge. It's at some point on that journey, it's the moment you're definitively said, &quot;I am my own person. You cannot have me anymore.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T10:16:33-07:00","id":247977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=247786#post247786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, curiously (not intended as criticism), when do you see the seeming as forming for the changeling? would it come right when they resolve to leave (when the Why is fully formed) or when they actually take action (when the Why is followed through on). Also, if someone makes multiple escape attempts, potentially with different reasons between them, how does that affect their seeming?</div> </div> </div> </div>I pictured it as a process that would kick off as soon as that internal threshold was passed and the changeling made their break (be it emotional, physical, however) from their bondage. So pretty much along the lines of what David just said. The multiple escape attempts thing raises a good point though. Or if someone is re-captured after escaping. Are Seemings a one-time deal or can you overwrite your old one? I agree with what you said, too. What and how can work too, as long as the conditions are kept broad enough that there will still be some wiggle room for players.<br /> <br /> One plus is I think all these talks have helped break down a lot of the seemings to their core bits. Elementals are still in a bit of a weird spot, despite being talked about the most (but they're Elementals, it's their job to be weird). Mostly I've just been trying to throw out ideas and perspectives I think might be interesting or useful for David and the writers (not sure how much of it actually falls into that and how much is just fanfiction, though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T13:54:25-07:00","id":251032,"title":"","content":"Please bear with me here, as I\u2019m still trying to organize my thoughts as I write this\u2026 (also, I don\u2019t have my books handy; so I may botch the terminology.)<br /> <br /> Maybe Kiths and Seemings shouldn\u2019t be <i>completely</i> decoupled. That is, give each Kith a \u201cfavored Seeming\u201d that serves to organize the Kiths into six groups that parallel the Seemings. Conceptually, a Kith\u2019s \u201cfavored Seeming\u201d hearkens back to 1e\u2019s conception of Seemings as collections of Kiths that are related by how the changeling was treated in captivity: Kiths that favor the Bestial Seeming were ones resulting from the Gentry treating the changeling like an animal; Kiths that favor the Fairest Seeming were ones resulting in being \u201cpampered\u201d by one\u2019s jailors; Kiths that favor the Wizened Seeming were ones that were somehow diminished by their time in Faerie; and so on. Mechanically, a Kith\u2019s \u201cfavored Seeming\u201d may manifest as a curse shared by all such Kiths. In terms of game design, the purpose of giving Kiths favored Seemings is to let you aggregate Kiths into thematically similar groups, and to speak in terms of 1e\u2019s definition of Seemings when it makes sense to do so: you can speak of Elemental Kiths (i.e., Kiths that favor the Elemental Seeming), Darkling Kiths (i.e., Kiths that favor the Darkling Seeming), Ogre Kiths, and so on. <br /> <br /> A Kith\u2019s Favored Seeming would not be the same as the changeling\u2019s <i>actual</i> Seeming, which would represent how the changeling regained her agency as described above. Conceptually, the relationship between a Kith\u2019s Favored Seeming and a changeling\u2019s Seeming is that the former represents the most natural means of reclaiming one\u2019s agency from the type of abuse the changeling endured in Faerie (which requires specifying the type of abuse), while the latter represents the actual means the changeling used to reclaim agency. Mechanically, 1e\u2019s Seeming mechanics would get broken up between these two things, with a 1e-style Seeming Curse going with 2e-style Kiths of a given Favored Seeming (and being directly reflective of the \u201cscars\u201d inflicted on them in their Durance) and a 1e-style Seeming Blessing going with a 2e-style Seeming (and being directly reflective of the changeling\u2019s agency). Also, a Kith\u2019s favored Seeming could be used as the basis for \u201cKith Contracts\u201d that are designed with a certain collection of Kiths in mind, existing alongside Seeming Contracts that are designed to capitalize on the changeling\u2019s \u201cSeeming Blessing\u201d in one way or another. <br /> <br /> I would <i>not</i> try to bias the selection of a changeling\u2019s Seeming toward his Kith\u2019s favored Seeming in any mechanical way: no \u201csystem bribes\u201d for correlating the two nor any form of \u201cdisincentives\u201d aimed at <i>not</i> correlating them. Keep any such biasing purely in the realm of \u201cfluff\u201d and out of the realm of \u201ccrunch\u201d. <br /> <br /> In a nutshell, break 1e-style Seemings in half, keeping their original role as \u201cgroupings of related Kiths\u201d, \u201cnature of the Durance\u201d, and \u201cfrailties\u201d in the half that gets incororated into Kiths while building 2e-style Seemings around 1e-style strengths and the notion of Seeming-as-agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T14:14:06-07:00","id":251045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=251032#post251032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please bear with me here, as I\u2019m still trying to organize my thoughts as I write this\u2026 (also, I don\u2019t have my books handy; so I may botch the terminology.)<br /> <br /> Maybe Kiths and Seemings shouldn\u2019t be <i>completely</i> decoupled. That is, give each Kith a \u201cfavored Seeming\u201d that serves to organize the Kiths into six groups that parallel the Seemings. Conceptually, a Kith\u2019s \u201cfavored Seeming\u201d hearkens back to 1e\u2019s conception of Seemings as collections of Kiths that are related by how the changeling was treated in captivity: Kiths that favor the Bestial Seeming were ones resulting from the Gentry treating the changeling like an animal; Kiths that favor the Fairest Seeming were ones resulting in being \u201cpampered\u201d by one\u2019s jailors; Kiths that favor the Wizened Seeming were ones that were somehow diminished by their time in Faerie; and so on. Mechanically, a Kith\u2019s \u201cfavored Seeming\u201d may manifest as a curse shared by all such Kiths. In terms of game design, the purpose of giving Kiths favored Seemings is to let you aggregate Kiths into thematically similar groups, and to speak in terms of 1e\u2019s definition of Seemings when it makes sense to do so: you can speak of Elemental Kiths (i.e., Kiths that favor the Elemental Seeming), Darkling Kiths (i.e., Kiths that favor the Darkling Seeming), Ogre Kiths, and so on.<br /> <br /> A Kith\u2019s Favored Seeming would not be the same as the changeling\u2019s <i>actual</i> Seeming, which would represent how the changeling regained her agency as described above. Conceptually, the relationship between a Kith\u2019s Favored Seeming and a changeling\u2019s Seeming is that the former represents the most natural means of reclaiming one\u2019s agency from the type of abuse the changeling endured in Faerie (which requires specifying the type of abuse), while the latter represents the actual means the changeling used to reclaim agency. Mechanically, 1e\u2019s Seeming mechanics would get broken up between these two things, with a 1e-style Seeming Curse going with 2e-style Kiths of a given Favored Seeming (and being directly reflective of the \u201cscars\u201d inflicted on them in their Durance) and a 1e-style Seeming Blessing going with a 2e-style Seeming (and being directly reflective of the changeling\u2019s agency). Also, a Kith\u2019s favored Seeming could be used as the basis for \u201cKith Contracts\u201d that are designed with a certain collection of Kiths in mind, existing alongside Seeming Contracts that are designed to capitalize on the changeling\u2019s \u201cSeeming Blessing\u201d in one way or another.<br /> <br /> I would <i>not</i> try to bias the selection of a changeling\u2019s Seeming toward his Kith\u2019s favored Seeming in any mechanical way: no \u201csystem bribes\u201d for correlating the two nor any form of \u201cdisincentives\u201d aimed at <i>not</i> correlating them. Keep any such biasing purely in the realm of \u201cfluff\u201d and out of the realm of \u201ccrunch\u201d.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, break 1e-style Seemings in half, keeping their original role as \u201cgroupings of related Kiths\u201d, \u201cnature of the Durance\u201d, and \u201cfrailties\u201d in the half that gets incororated into Kiths while building 2e-style Seemings around 1e-style strengths and the notion of Seeming-as-agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh I think that defeats the purpose of switching them around to begin with. I don't think this is really necessary. In fact, I think it, if anything, it hurts things, because not everyone's going to see kiths the same way in where they belong, especially with the current design goals of them being the 'primary' part of the splat. I'd much rather see them kept as is currently explained, letting individuals and storytellers decide what might be coupled together in their own setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T04:10:24-07:00","id":251379,"title":"","content":"I was reading this thread and pondering about what I think may be the defining feature of Elementals as a Seeming, decoupled from kiths and came to the conclussion that it maybe depersonalization/objetification.<br /> <br /> Elementals are those that became less like <i>beings</i> and more like <i>things</i>, though how could that tie into Agency is beyond me as it seems rather the opposite at first sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T10:06:21-07:00","id":251546,"title":"","content":"Accepting your role, but subliminating it into your own ends? 'Well I am just a candle, but wax melts and candles vanish and they have to be replaced. So I will vanish, they will just have to find another candle'? Being unfettered by the conventions of being a person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T11:00:01-07:00","id":251556,"title":"","content":"Yeah; you really seem to need to go the \u201cChinese finger puzzle\u201d route for the Elemental Seeming to make sense as agency: gaining freedom to act by doing the opposite of what your jailors would expect someone seeking their freedom to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T03:45:57-07:00","id":252175,"title":"","content":"For Elementals, I could see something like deciding &quot;I am a fire, nothing can tame me&quot; or &quot;I am a tree, and I will outgrow any prison built for me.&quot; Water will flow through any crack, earth can resist and shake, and air and smoke will just float away,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T14:36:20-07:00","id":252670,"title":"","content":"So maybe elementals are differentiated from other seemings by trying to be something else instead of trying to reclaim themselves, and in making that choice found themselves again? Not really sure about that one but it's an idea at the very least. Another option perhaps is to say they escaped by sorcery or something to that effect. They saw that their keeper's realm was not just their keeper's, it also belonged to the fire in the furnace and the wind that sailed through the streets and the stone in which the buildings are set and the sun in the sky, and turned to them for an escape. It's a pretty big deviation from how they're written now (though I'm not sure how close they'll be in any case) but it at least sounds like it would be interesting to play, take them in a vaguely shamanistic direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T05:00:58-07:00","id":253236,"title":"","content":"I don't think you want a seeming to define a player's goals - that isn't how the other ones work - but seeing being elemental as being intrinsic to your surroundings, and as a result free... That is pretty good, since logically you are saying, I am a prisoner, not only do I not belong here, but this isn't even the natural place in this world I should be in if I WAS to belong here. Like, being a captive is a parody of life, the falsehood, the unnaturalness of it is part of what peels you away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:47:27-07:00","id":253668,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this question asks for too fine a distinction for this thread, but it is related to Kiths, so here it goes: If a kith is sufficiently different from human (living flame, clockwork doll, that sort of thing), will that affect things like performing medical care on them (feeding fuel to the fire-man, re-aligning inner gears) and other actions upon them, or is that more a roleplaying concern than a mechanics issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T17:33:00-07:00","id":253687,"title":"","content":"I would look at Elementals as those who endured their Durance. For example, Mr. Teddy Bear is an Elemental because when his Keeper took him to his bed to be his plush friend forever he refused to engage him, he truly became a Teddy Bear completely still and unmoved by his Keeper's &quot;affections&quot; then, when his Keeper set him aside to play with more interesting toys he just got up and simply walked away.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Looking at my post again I realize that maybe phrasing it like that wasn't appropriate. Refusing to give their Keeper what it wants until it lets it's guard down is more accurate. Maybe refusal? denial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","user":"Ravraxas","date":". 09-09-2014, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T14:48:44-07:00","id":257613,"title":"","content":"Perhaps... hmm, here's a combo.<br /> <br /> Perhaps an Elemental is the core of something, a concept that has all its, &quot;extraneous,&quot; parts taken away. Sometimes, that makes it natural, but other times... not so much. They're like a drawing with no shading, or any of the tiny details that make something unique. A Draconic Elemental is nothing but that creature, without any of the hallmarks that would make it say, European or Asian style dragons. Now, how is this an expression of Agency?<br /> <br /> Well, that goes into the second bit, which is refusing to be apart of something else. This goes back to the original pile of bricks example, where from once being part of a building, you escaped. Well, separation could be refusing to have the details that the others have, instead becoming a core concept, without any of the needless shading. This would also fit the emotionally cold part of being an Elemental, by refusing to embrace the details of others, and become what someone else wants.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this has issues, not the least of which that it probably doesn't work with certain Kiths, but what are the thoughts on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T21:23:37-07:00","id":257841,"title":"","content":"A thought strikes me, and I'm not sure if it's because it's a good one or because it's 11:15 at night.<br /> <br /> It feels like some of the problem folks are having is trying to wrap the old Seemings up in this new paradigm of agency. Trying to work &quot;this is what ____ means as a statement on agency&quot; into the concepts behind the old Seemings. But why keep the old Seemings at all - at least, while in the planning phase?<br /> <br /> It feels like it might be more productive to instead go &quot;what statements do we want to make about those characters who manage to escape to become Changelings, and what concepts flow from that,&quot; and then, once those ideas are nailed down, either attach them to the old Seeming names or, if necessary, invent/combine Seeming names to suit them. Shoehorning old square concepts into new round holes will just lead to issues of setting consistency that'll cause issues down the line if and when they decide a third edition might be needed.<br /> <br /> So, what sort of &quot;agency archetypes&quot; might people be looking for, and what sorts of statements might such archetypes make, independently of labels such as &quot;Beast,&quot; &quot;Wizened,&quot; or &quot;Fairest?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T05:09:17-07:00","id":258048,"title":"","content":"So 'agency archetypes' sound more like a personality trait than a class/race splat. The coping mechanisms I listed earlier seem like pretty deep pigeonholes to stick a character in.<br /> <br /> Then we also have had Illuminated Minutae talking about What, How, and Why, which might lend better to the 'narrative' issue at the heart of Changeling.<br /> <br /> But then you also said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=257841#post257841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;what statements do we want to make about those characters who manage to escape to become Changelings, and what concepts flow from that&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's the whole conceit of the game - how do you as a roleplayed make this statement of escape and recovery and rebuilding and beautiful madness?<br /> <br /> &quot;Those who escape Fairie ... Lost something during their Durance.&quot; (Tragic, Needy, but also Wizened)<br /> <br /> &quot;Those who escape Fairie ... Are special compared to their fellows.&quot; (Fated, Heroic, but also Fairest)<br /> <br /> &quot;Those who escape Fairie ... Have experienced something beyond human ken.&quot; (Transcendent, Alien, Hallucinatory, but also Ogre, Elemental, Beast, Darkling...)<br /> <br /> Thinking about story archetypes: 'what makes a protgonist' -type-stuff... Is that what you meant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T05:31:44-07:00","id":258058,"title":"","content":"Mainly, I was thinking &quot;what do you want to set apart the different Seemings,&quot; then I figured that once those options have been laid out it might be easier to set down a selection that's internally consistent and makes whatever statement the line wants to make. As it is, people are discussing apples and oranges and bananas and VW Bugs at the same time, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T13:13:49-07:00","id":258396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=251032#post251032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Kiths and Seemings shouldn\u2019t be <i>completely</i> decoupled.<br /> <br /> (Block of Text)<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, break 1e-style Seemings in half, keeping their original role as \u201cgroupings of related Kiths\u201d, \u201cnature of the Durance\u201d, and \u201cfrailties\u201d in the half that gets incororated into Kiths while building 2e-style Seemings around 1e-style strengths and the notion of Seeming-as-agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gets me thinking that a Seeming could go one of two ways: Either it's the same as in 1e, as the beginning shape a keeper molds a Changeling into and that later clarifies into a Kith; or as it is currently suggested, a vague shaping of the Wyrd in response to how the Changeling takes back control of his life, a sort of instinctual, reflexive version of what the Keeper did to ingrain the Changeling's Kith.<br /> <br /> ...hmmm. Would it be feasible for a Changeling to have two Seemings, one reflecting her enslavement along with her Kith, and a second embodying her escape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T14:34:33-07:00","id":258450,"title":"","content":"Given the mechanical weight, it seems like that's still in the Dual-Kith territory of things rather than Dual-Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T12:05:41-07:00","id":263007,"title":"","content":"Having read most of this thread here is how I see the Seemings.<br /> <br /> Darkling: Sacrifice. As others have said they sacrificed something, a friend, deep held beliefs, a part of thier humanity, a literal part of themselves, and darkness filled the void within.<br /> <br /> Orge: Force. Could be violence, endurance, preseeverance, intimidation.<br /> <br /> Beast: Instinct. There no time for rational thought in the madness, you just had trust in your instincts, no plans, just your gut, and reactions.<br /> <br /> Elemental: Essentials. You boiled yourself down to your essential nature, to the point of becoming almost thw Platonic ideal of yourself, cutting off anything not essential to escaping. Removing all connections to others, cutting off the parts of your identity you didn't need, cutting off useless emotions to slip free.<br /> <br /> Fairest Connections. The Fairest Got out using there ability to connect with others, seduction, charm friendship, empathy.<br /> <br /> Wizen: Work. They had gain they're freedom via the <br /> old fashioned way, hard work, skill, and competence.<br /> <br /> And of course your mask and the wyrd interupt this fundmental nature through the lens of narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T12:18:32-07:00","id":263009,"title":"","content":"Examples using Draconian Kith<br /> <br /> Fairest: Gold Dragon, you used your ability to connect to others to gain they help in escaping, which marked you physically with scales of burnished gold.<br /> <br /> Orge: Red Draconian: You use raw violence to get free, fiery breath and rending claws.<br /> <br /> Elemental Archtypical Dragon: You become the essencial universal dragon, so bland, yet blending perfectly into your kith that you seemed less a changeling and more a natural part of Faire, slipping free as interest in you wanes.<br /> <br /> Darkling Draconian: Dracolich, you sacrifice apart of yourself, to gain freedom, lost something essential to yourself, and darkness took its place.<br /> <br /> Beast Dragonian: White Dragon, you gave into pure predatory instinct.<br /> <br /> Wizen: Dragonmount. You excellenced and worked hard, becoming so skilled in your task, that you found away to use your skill to get to freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T12:44:37-07:00","id":263029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=258396#post258396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This gets me thinking that a Seeming could go one of two ways: Either it's the same as in 1e, as the beginning shape a keeper molds a Changeling into and that later clarifies into a Kith; or as it is currently suggested, a vague shaping of the Wyrd in response to how the Changeling takes back control of his life, a sort of instinctual, reflexive version of what the Keeper did to ingrain the Changeling's Kith.<br /> <br /> ...hmmm. Would it be feasible for a Changeling to have two Seemings, one reflecting her enslavement along with her Kith, and a second embodying her escape?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn\u2019t really thinking &quot;dual Seemings&quot; so much as &quot;keep the 'groupings of related Kiths' thing in some form&quot;. And since Kiths are &quot;what the Gentry did to you&quot;, it seemed reasonable to me to have 2e Kiths, rather than 2e Seemings, include a Frailty. The bit about having groups of Kiths share a Frailty was an attempt at avoiding mechanical bloat: if there are essentially six Frailties, that takes up a lot less space and requires less demands on the designers than if every Kith has a unique Frailty of its own. <br /> <br /> OTOH, Kith Frailties wouldn\u2019t necessarily have to be limited to precisely six, each corresponding to a Seeming. That would be simplest; but there would be nothing preventing you from creating new Kiths with new Frailties if you want. That said, the proposed \u201cshared between Kiths\u201d nature of Kith-based Frailties ought to encourage someone creating a Kith with a new Frailty to ask \u201cwhat <i>other</i> Kiths with this Frailty might exist?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T17:14:21-07:00","id":263271,"title":"","content":"Hmm, it seems the, &quot;essentials,&quot; concept has caught on for Elementals. Interesting. That, or others just had a similar idea for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T09:49:31-07:00","id":265533,"title":"","content":"I've read through the thread and I've come to some conclusions.<br /> <br /> Seemings are what's on the outside, what you're Seeming to be. A Kith is what's on the inside, what you are. A Hunterheart Elemental was once a gun, used to kill many. His aim tracks foes and strikes them down. Since his escape he abhors violence and death, using it as a deterrent rather than a inevitability.<br /> <br /> This means while Beasts as a Seeming actually gives you the outer animal traits, the Kiths of a Beast are things Beasts do and are. Elementals as a Seeming makes you reminiscent of the inanimate and non-sentient, the Kiths give you the traits of these things. A Venombite can be a snake, spider, scorpion, platypus through the Beast Seeming, it can also be a poisonous orchid through the Elemental Seeming. A Blightbent can be garbage through the Elemental Seeming, it can also be a verminous animal like a cockroach through the Beast Seeming.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T10:00:53-07:00","id":265542,"title":"","content":"Elementals to me have always been the inanimate and non-sentient. They're things, they're objects, and for a time they are paid attention to and used or admired, and they are trapped into being this thing, and many accept being it and forget what they were. Elementals who don't forget, or who suddenly remember may find themselves forgotten or discarded, and in that moment can escape. I'm certain we've all had that moment where we use something and take it for granted, completely disregarding it until we need it again, things that we don't know what we have until it's gone, and then we go searching for it. The Agency of Elementals should be slipping away unnoticed in plain sight, forgotten until needed, and then hounded to get back. If we are the True Fae, the Changeling is the car keys or the other sock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T06:55:33-07:00","id":266129,"title":"","content":"So, these Seeming lists are a ... thing now? A thing we're doing?<br /> <br /> OK, here's my take.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bYour Seeming is how you used the Kith you were given to your own advantage. It's an approach, a way of doing things.<br /> <br /> You might hate doing things that way because it reminds you of Arcadia (well-rounded.) You might revel in it because it plays to your strengths (focused.)<br /> <br /> But you're <i>never</i> indifferent.<br /> <br /> With cats, because cats:<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> You became a terrifying, nightmarish version of yourself. A twisted, mangy stray with glowing eyes. You frightened the guards away.<br /> <br /> <b>Orge:</b> You became a tough, dangerous version of yourself. A big, rough-looking Tom with huge claws. You killed the guards.<br /> <br /> <b>Primal: </b>You became an unstoppable force (/immovable object.) A small lioness with muscles rippling under your pelt. You pushed past the guards.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> You became an impossibly-perfect paragon of your Kith. A stupidly fluffy cat that almost glows. The guards couldn't resist taking you in and helping you.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizen:</b> You became subtle and cunning. A little tabby, almost invisible against the ground. The guards never realized you were escaping until it was too late. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-26-2014, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T09:01:22-07:00","id":266198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232353#post232353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the only Changeling I ever got to play was a Bright One, and the obvious thought is, how do you do that with a Darkling?</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason, every time I look at this sentence, all I can think of is the Lady in the Light--she has a name, but I can't remember it--from Alan Wake.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T12:35:53-07:00","id":267605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=266198#post266198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason, every time I look at this sentence, all I can think of is the Lady in the Light--she has a name, but I can't remember it--from Alan Wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cynthia Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T17:51:12-07:00","id":268642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=266198#post266198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason, every time I look at this sentence, all I can think of is the Lady in the Light--she has a name, but I can't remember it--from Alan Wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another option is a take on the Angler Fish or Will-o-wisp <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T09:53:22-07:00","id":285084,"title":"","content":"Well I think we've pretty much covered Elementals and Seeming as Agency from just about every angle. Let's talk about Kiths!<br /> <br /> The Corebook has a total of 29 Kiths, that's a lot of write-ups. Plus five seeming combos for each one if you want to add those. Plus a stereotypes list from hell. I think one bonus from the old system was that you could give a brief overview of every Kith just by writing about a Seeming. Not so now. So let's see what we can do about that.<br /> <br /> The first solution most people would give would be to merge as many similar-concept Kiths as you can. Fair enough, let's give it a shot.<br /> <br /> Water-Dwellers and Swimmerskins can fuse into *STUFF THAT LIVES IN WATER,* keep Waterborn as a separate *STUFF THAT IS LITERALLY WATER* Kith.<br /> <br /> Flowering can be folded into the Woodbloods.<br /> <br /> Um... hm. The thing is, most of the Kiths in the core don't overlap. They're all pretty good about being their own separate ideas. Gristlegrinders evoke monsters that will gobble you up, Hunterhearts evoke predatory animals. Without <i>really</i> changing up Kiths, you're kind of stuck doing loads of write-ups. (Not that I'd mind as a reader, mind you.)<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T22:41:37-07:00","id":287278,"title":"","content":"Keep Kiths we have, just give option for people to combine them (I think it was done before as a Merit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T00:01:26-07:00","id":287316,"title":"","content":"The detachment for Kith from Seeming does mean that a lot of the current Kiths can be compressed. I'm pretty sure that's part of the point. Water-dwellers and Swimmerskins become one Kith expressed differently through the lenses of two Seemings (Ogres and Beasts in this case).<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean Dual-Kiths are out of the question or shouldn't exist. It just means that Dual-Kith can focus on its name and mean having two Kiths mechanically, instead of being a stop gap for concepts where the best fitting Kith doesn't match the best fitting Seeming and there isn't a printed Kith that removes that issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T09:22:30-08:00","id":379078,"title":"","content":"When it comes to contracts that are based on seemings, I don't think they should be blocked out from characters outside of them. They're contracts that were negotiated with the Wyrd. Any being from Arcadia should be able to use them. There is already an exp difference for taking them out of seeming. Some seemings are already punished by having fewer affinity contracts as well, with Darkling and Ogres.<br /> <br /> Changeling also don't have the unique contracts as well, as that's more of a Requiem thing with bloodline powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4809-ingordwetrust","name":"InGordWeTrust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T15:48:14-08:00","id":379577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InGordWeTrust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=379078#post379078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to contracts that are based on seemings, I don't think they should be blocked out from characters outside of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more or less settled. I won't be locking any Seemings out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InGordWeTrust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=379078#post379078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some seemings are already punished by having fewer affinity contracts as well, with Darkling and Ogres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you're talking about Changeling the Lost First Edition. I'm sorry, but this discussion is about the upcoming Changeling the Lost Second Edition. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InGordWeTrust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=379078#post379078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling also don't have the unique contracts as well, as that's more of a Requiem thing with bloodline powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not an inherently true statement. It's not something I've addressed. But it's not something that's actually set in stone yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T18:05:25-08:00","id":379701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=285084#post285084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I think we've pretty much covered Elementals and Seeming as Agency from just about every angle. Let's talk about Kiths!<br /> <br /> The Corebook has a total of 29 Kiths, that's a lot of write-ups. Plus five seeming combos for each one if you want to add those. Plus a stereotypes list from hell. I think one bonus from the old system was that you could give a brief overview of every Kith just by writing about a Seeming. Not so now. So let's see what we can do about that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just a thought: what if instead of having lots of fixed Kiths we got the option to actually build one out of a big list of abilities/characteristics - similar to the way we create Demonic Forms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T18:12:24-08:00","id":379705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoktorNiemand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=379701#post379701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just a thought: what if instead of having lots of fixed Kiths we got the option to actually build one out of a big list of abilities/characteristics - similar to the way we create Demonic Forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer: No.<br /> <br /> Long answer: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/217778-inspiration-from-demon?p=218544#post218544\">Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo</a>[\u2026]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T08:13:00-08:00","id":380116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=287316#post287316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't mean Dual-Kiths are out of the question or shouldn't exist. It just means that Dual-Kith can focus on its name and mean having two Kiths mechanically, instead of being a stop gap for concepts where the best fitting Kith doesn't match the best fitting Seeming and there isn't a printed Kith that removes that issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I will finally be able to make my Bright One/Swimmer-skin Anglerfish-man Darkling!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T08:25:10-08:00","id":380124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=379705#post379705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Short answer: No.<br /> <br /> Long answer: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/217778-inspiration-from-demon?p=218544#post218544\">Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo</a>[\u2026]</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, is that why I got two more likes for that?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T04:02:49-08:00","id":380893,"title":"","content":"Just my opinion, it seems like many, but not all, Kiths will have Seemings which &quot;fit&quot; them well. Coyote &quot;fits&quot; Beast, but you could imagine a Coyote Fairest as well. A Bright One &quot;fits&quot; Fairest, but you could see that as an Elemental fairly easily as well. But a Coyote Elemental doesn't make *as much* sense, nor does a Bright One Darkling make *as much* sense. This is all grey-area, and yes you could come up with examples, but it seems that certain Kiths fit more easily with certain Seemings. Do you agree with this observation?<br /> <br /> If so, are you going to limit the final kith selection available to only to those that can be generalized to all Seemings with ease? Otherwise, will there be any mechanical or RP advantage for having a kith which &quot;fits&quot; the seeming you choose? Will that be officially addressed/quantified somehow within the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T04:45:45-08:00","id":380912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjspra2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=380893#post380893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just my opinion, it seems like many, but not all, Kiths will have Seemings which &quot;fit&quot; them well. Coyote &quot;fits&quot; Beast, but you could imagine a Coyote Fairest as well. A Bright One &quot;fits&quot; Fairest, but you could see that as an Elemental fairly easily as well. But a Coyote Elemental doesn't make *as much* sense, nor does a Bright One Darkling make *as much* sense. This is all grey-area, and yes you could come up with examples, but it seems that certain Kiths fit more easily with certain Seemings. Do you agree with this observation?<br /> <br /> If so, are you going to limit the final kith selection available to only to those that can be generalized to all Seemings with ease? Otherwise, will there be any mechanical or RP advantage for having a kith which &quot;fits&quot; the seeming you choose? Will that be officially addressed/quantified somehow within the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it. While I totally get the virtue of doing so, I think it'll upset a lot of people. It's not the hill I'd want to die on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T05:37:10-08:00","id":380918,"title":"","content":"Is not the talk of 3 suitable Seemings per Kith in book? Like in Coyote's example, under it's description we would get idea for Beast, Fairest and Darkling one. It would be implied that other combinations are possible if ST agrees, but those mentioned will be in corebook. Am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T05:59:58-08:00","id":380921,"title":"","content":"They've already said we can combine all kiths with all seemings. There's no implication, it's fact. There's just not enough room to list <i>an example of each</i> so obviously we're getting limited descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-25-2015, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T06:42:53-08:00","id":380932,"title":"","content":"Seemings represent the manner in which one escaped from the Durance (generalizing now), so any Kith could develop any Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T16:47:11-08:00","id":381432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=380918#post380918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is not the talk of 3 suitable Seemings per Kith in book? Like in Coyote's example, under it's description we would get idea for Beast, Fairest and Darkling one. It would be implied that other combinations are possible if ST agrees, but those mentioned will be in corebook. Am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I just have to keep examples to a limited number, because of space reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T17:37:11-08:00","id":381458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=380912#post380912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt it. While I totally get the virtue of doing so, I think it'll upset a lot of people. It's not the hill I'd want to die on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool. The main question is whether or not we'd have to limit the kiths so that they are all highly generalized. I would highly prefer ST discretion to limiting the kith selection. X) Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:21:30-08:00","id":382094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjspra2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=381458#post381458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. The main question is whether or not we'd have to limit the kiths so that they are all highly generalized. I would highly prefer ST discretion to limiting the kith selection. X) Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do note that Seeming no longer means exactly what it did in 1e; in 2e, it's going to signify the manner in which a Changeling took back his life and agency. I don't see value in denying certain Kiths the full range self-determination, much as I'll grant the particular execution of the idea may change my mind. By the same token, you may want to consider reevaluating your preference under the new context for Seeming, when we have more examples and details.<br /> <br /> I also get the sense you're assuming all Kiths will be just as they were in 1e. If the system assumption is that all Kiths can potentially fall under all Seemings, that may give the writers some incentive to write the Kiths such that the sort of dissonance you worry about doesn't arise.<br /> <br /> There was a <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd6df.html?g=posts&amp;t=45674\" target=\"_blank\">fun thread</a> on the old forums in which one poster would put forth a combination of two Kiths, while the next would write up a Changeling concept based on that as well as a new pair of Kiths. Not exactly Seeming, but the principle is undeniably there. The thread convinced me that not seeing how a particular combination would work is simply a failure of imagination, not something to be denied or disincentivized by the system (mechanical reasons aside, natch). <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultec81.html?g=posts&amp;t=2413\" target=\"_blank\">This one</a> also gave some nice example combos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T09:56:39-08:00","id":385215,"title":"","content":"Thanks Gaius! I'm asking these questions because it was not obvious to me whether we'd be losing, gaining, or maintaining status quo on the level of variety available in character concepts. I want to be able to go out there and tell people with certainty how awesome the new stuff's going to be. Without asking the questions, I *would* be making assumptions, and I want to avoid that. X)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:35:08-08:00","id":385271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjspra2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=385215#post385215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Gaius! I'm asking these questions because it was not obvious to me whether we'd be losing, gaining, or maintaining status quo on the level of variety available in character concepts. I want to be able to go out there and tell people with certainty how awesome the new stuff's going to be. Without asking the questions, I *would* be making assumptions, and I want to avoid that. X)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome, and thank you for taking my statements in the best light. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> On a reread, I was concerned I might have come off as a touch arrogant or snippy in there. Particularly as it's now obvious to me I completely misread your last post: I thought you were hoping there would be some hard limitations more-or-less &quot;because&quot; (and there'd be nothing wrong with expressing personal preferences, anyway). It's now now much clearer to me you were wondering if the changes meant Kiths might become more generic so they could work for any Seeming and kinda hoping they wouldn't.* So, you have my apologies for missing the mark, and I'm glad my response was helpful in spite of that! ^_^o<br /> <br /> * Unless I've missed the point again, in which case, sorry about that!<br /> <br /> Specifically on the point of making Kiths generic, I have a pretty good feeling they'll stay distinct. I caught a look at the preliminary outline and, while things are obviously subject to change, it set aside enough wordcount for 100 Kiths or so, with a note that 1e had around 91 Kiths altogether. Even if they don't use exactly the same Kiths as last time, I get the sense they can afford to go in some relatively specific directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T19:46:23-08:00","id":395774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=385271#post385271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically on the point of making Kiths generic, I have a pretty good feeling they'll stay distinct. I caught a look at the preliminary outline and, while things are obviously subject to change, it set aside enough wordcount for 100 Kiths or so, with a note that 1e had around 91 Kiths altogether. Even if they don't use exactly the same Kiths as last time, I get the sense they can afford to go in some relatively specific directions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, and yeah that was the point of the question haha. And, yeah, more than once I've played the game of &quot;give me a dual kith I'll give you a durance.&quot; X)<br /> <br /> Also, you're fine, no worries lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:12:15-08:00","id":396309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=385271#post385271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Specifically on the point of making Kiths generic, I have a pretty good feeling they'll stay distinct. I caught a look at the preliminary outline and, while things are obviously subject to change, it set aside enough wordcount for 100 Kiths or so, with a note that 1e had around 91 Kiths altogether. Even if they don't use exactly the same Kiths as last time, I get the sense they can afford to go in some relatively specific directions.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, we're revising almost all those 90+. There are a few that are getting wrapped together due to overlapping. But, we'll have all the classics represented, then some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T15:49:19-08:00","id":396867,"title":"","content":"I wonder which ones will get combined? Maybe some of the water based ones, and the gliding ones like mothman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:35:39-08:00","id":396910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=396867#post396867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder which ones will get combined? Maybe some of the water based ones, and the gliding ones like mothman.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Windwing/Lurkglider</span></span> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Stonebones/Earthbones</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Cleareyes/Cyclopean </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hunterheart/</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Razorhand</span></span> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Palewraith/Shadowsoul</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Waterborn/Swimmerskin</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Succubus/Romancer</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">I think there are maybe some others; these were just from the first list brought up. But, these might be cases where you get one as the main kith, and one is just an example Seeming variant on it. Or something. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:38:00-08:00","id":396914,"title":"","content":"So, just like Contracts, some Kiths have Seeming-based variants? Nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T19:28:16-08:00","id":397078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=396914#post396914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just like Contracts, some Kiths have Seeming-based variants? Nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Not mechanically different. But we offer examples of what Kiths look like with different Seemings. Most will get 3-4 examples, depending on word count. Some will have names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:02:06-08:00","id":399271,"title":"","content":"So Succubus might be the Darkling Variant of Romancer for example?<br /> <br /> This will likely leave alot of room for new Kiths as well, I mean say this shortens the amount of Kiths to 80 old ones, with Seeming variants representing some old kiths, and if you have space for around a 100 Kiths, that gives you some space for new Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:15:02-08:00","id":399316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=399271#post399271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Succubus might be the Darkling Variant of Romancer for example?<br /> <br /> This will likely leave alot of room for new Kiths as well, I mean say this shortens the amount of Kiths to 80 old ones, with Seeming variants representing some old kiths, and if you have space for around a 100 Kiths, that gives you some space for new Kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct on both counts. <br /> <br /> If the numbers shake out the way it's looking, we will have at least a handful. So far though, draft versions of Kiths are a LITTLE longer than expected. Not much. So we might not have quite as much room as I expected. But close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:16:58-08:00","id":399318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=396309#post396309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FWIW, we're revising almost all those 90+. There are a few that are getting wrapped together due to overlapping. But, we'll have all the classics represented, then some.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what one would hope for from a second edition and then some. Still kind of reeling (in a good way!) about the fact that you've pulled ALL the kiths in from the various books. This'll really help some of the ones from Winter Masques, which I felt had great flavor but not much in the mechanics department.<br /> <br /> It was a weird day when I realized the kith blessing for the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Ask-wee-da-eed/Will-o'-the-Wisp didn't exactly work as written. And I had spent three dots to get it as a duel kith out of seeming too!<br /> <br /> Hmm, I wonder then if there may be a Merit to give you duel seeming as well as dual kith (that may have been addressed earlier, sorry).</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T20:29:33-08:00","id":399900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=399318#post399318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what one would hope for from a second edition and then some. Still kind of reeling (in a good way!) about the fact that you've pulled ALL the kiths in from the various books. This'll really help some of the ones from Winter Masques, which I felt had great flavor but not much in the mechanics department.<br /> <br /> It was a weird day when I realized the kith blessing for the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Ask-wee-da-eed/Will-o'-the-Wisp didn't exactly work as written. And I had spent three dots to get it as a duel kith out of seeming too!<br /> <br /> Hmm, I wonder then if there may be a Merit to give you duel seeming as well as dual kith (that may have been addressed earlier, sorry).</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>We'll chat on dual kith/seeming soon. Not sure if we want to do anything with that, or if it's that feasible. But we'll look at the possibility. That'll probably occur between first and second draft passes if possible, because I want to look at how the kits work alone before we start talking about doubling up on them. The kiths so far are significantly beefier than the old ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T22:12:44-08:00","id":399978,"title":"","content":"Pleased to hear it. ^_^ I continue to like the idea of having the Kith as the focal point instead of Seeming.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Seemings, I had a couple of questions on the topic. I can understand if you'd prefer to hold off (or just aren't capable of) answering either at the moment, but I'm curious: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>We know a Seeming reflects the way a Changeling took back his or her life, gives a certain &quot;flavor&quot; to the Kith, and gives an additional option on some Contracts. What else can the Seeming give to a Changeling?</li> <li>There was some lively debate around what Beast and Elemental Seemings would mean under the new paradigm. Some argued they had strong similarities and theorized about a sort of &quot;Primal&quot; Seeming or something for both. Ultimately, you decided on keeping them, which I'm kind of glad about, but still curious. More than the other 4, those two seemed to have the broadest range (a mouse is very different from a crocodile, and fire is very different from water). Were there any particular challenges you had in tackling those two? What modes of self-determination do they reflect in Changelings?</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T22:40:39-08:00","id":400007,"title":"","content":"I thought Succubi would be the Darkling variant of Romancer, because while Succubi have beast like elements, tails, horns, bat wings, its meant to be symbolic of demons not animals. Also the previous fluff of using sex as a weapon fits the new verison of Darklings who sacrificed a piece of thier light for freedom.<br /> <br /> I too am curious as to what kind of mechnics Seemings will have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T03:28:31-08:00","id":400148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=399978#post399978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pleased to hear it. ^_^ I continue to like the idea of having the Kith as the focal point instead of Seeming.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Seemings, I had a couple of questions on the topic. I can understand if you'd prefer to hold off (or just aren't capable of) answering either at the moment, but I'm curious:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>We know a Seeming reflects the way a Changeling took back his or her life, gives a certain &quot;flavor&quot; to the Kith, and gives an additional option on some Contracts. What else can the Seeming give to a Changeling?</li> <li>There was some lively debate around what Beast and Elemental Seemings would mean under the new paradigm. Some argued they had strong similarities and theorized about a sort of &quot;Primal&quot; Seeming or something for both. Ultimately, you decided on keeping them, which I'm kind of glad about, but still curious. More than the other 4, those two seemed to have the broadest range (a mouse is very different from a crocodile, and fire is very different from water). Were there any particular challenges you had in tackling those two? What modes of self-determination do they reflect in Changelings?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>They haven't been tackled yet. I've got Filamena Young handling them now. She's busy writing some stuff for Feng Shui, and then Hurt Locker. THEN, she'll get to Seemings.<br /> <br /> They're a thing I will probably post when the draft comes in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:27:11-08:00","id":402545,"title":"","content":"This might be way too early to ask, but will &quot;Elements&quot; be more narrowly defined in the new system? What is your hope with this, how do you feel about them? <br /> <br /> This is a big questions because if you limit too much you lose a lot of harmless and fun flavor, if you limit too little you get stuff like Contract of Elements: Avocado. X) So I'm wondering what your feeling is on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T16:39:18-08:00","id":402600,"title":"","content":"Did anyone ever actually play Avocado?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:09:05-08:00","id":402613,"title":"","content":"No; but I was tempted to try a game of GURPS Asparagus once\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:17:22-08:00","id":402644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=400148#post400148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They haven't been tackled yet. I've got Filamena Young handling them now. She's busy writing some stuff for Feng Shui, and then Hurt Locker. THEN, she'll get to Seemings.<br /> <br /> They're a thing I will probably post when the draft comes in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I will look forward to hearing more on that front. Also many other fronts, but that one's a particular biggie.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the clarification and update. Actually, thank you for all the answers in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:54:14-08:00","id":402671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjspra2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=402545#post402545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be way too early to ask, but will &quot;Elements&quot; be more narrowly defined in the new system? What is your hope with this, how do you feel about them?<br /> <br /> This is a big questions because if you limit too much you lose a lot of harmless and fun flavor, if you limit too little you get stuff like Contract of Elements: Avocado. X) So I'm wondering what your feeling is on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another place where I want to feel out what my writers say. If it sounds compelling, then I support that. Otherwise, I tell them to edit it. But I try not to put too many assumptions onto my writers up front; I hire them because of what they bring to the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T20:16:09-08:00","id":402861,"title":"","content":"So I noticed you\u2019ve got five different writers handling the Kiths and Seemings; if I\u2019m reading the outline right, Filamena is responsible for the Seemings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T20:24:58-08:00","id":402869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=402861#post402861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I noticed you\u2019ve got five different writers handling the Kiths and Seemings; if I\u2019m reading the outline right, Filamena is responsible for the Seemings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. She's writing Seemings. The other writers are doing Kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T21:05:59-08:00","id":402936,"title":"","content":"Hmm, hadn't really mathed out the wordcount distribution for that section of <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g225t9mnjcwfsxd/Huntsmen%20Chronicle%20Outline.docx?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">the outline</a> before, but the ~100 Kith estimate may have been a little optimistic. Unless I've goofed in my calculations or assumptions.<br /> <br /> With ~7K words of the Seeming-and-Kith Chapter's ~30K going to Seemings, that leaves ~23K for Kiths. If each Kith is ~250 words, that would mean ~92 if they all went to Kith write-ups. We know they aren't, though, since some of those ~23K need to go toward describing what Kiths are. Still, covering all the (est. 91) 1e Kiths should be doable, as some are getting condensed into mechanics-free Seeming variants for &quot;prevailing&quot; Kiths. At least 7 have been planned to be condensed, so that'd be at most 84 distinct entries to cover the 1e Kiths, eating up ~21K words. That leaves ~2K of the ~23K to split between the description of Kiths, newly introduced Kiths, and surplus for Kith write-ups that run over (David had mentioned some were coming in a bit heftier than planned).<br /> <br /> Does that seem about right, or has the aforementioned goofing come into it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T21:24:32-08:00","id":402964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=402936#post402936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, hadn't really mathed out the wordcount distribution for that section of <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g225t9mnjcwfsxd/Huntsmen%20Chronicle%20Outline.docx?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">the outline</a> before, but the ~100 Kith estimate may have been a little optimistic. Unless I've goofed in my calculations or assumptions.<br /> <br /> With ~7K words of the Seeming-and-Kith Chapter's ~30K going to Seemings, that leaves ~23K for Kiths. If each Kith is ~250 words, that would mean ~92 if they all went to Kith write-ups. We know they aren't, though, since some of those ~23K need to go toward describing what Kiths are. Still, covering all the (est. 91) 1e Kiths should be doable, as some are getting condensed into mechanics-free Seeming variants for &quot;prevailing&quot; Kiths. At least 7 have been planned to be condensed, so that'd be at most 84 distinct entries to cover the 1e Kiths, eating up ~21K words. That leaves ~2K of the ~23K to split between the description of Kiths, newly introduced Kiths, and surplus for Kith write-ups that run over (David had mentioned some were coming in a bit heftier than planned).<br /> <br /> Does that seem about right, or has the aforementioned goofing come into it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about right. <br /> <br /> I don't expect a LOT of new Kiths. But a few. Most are right around 250 words. Some a little above. Some a little below. So, I think it'll balance out, but it's a little early to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:11:18-08:00","id":403019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=402869#post402869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. She's writing Seemings. The other writers are doing Kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I\u2019m definitely looking forward to seeing what she has to say about Elementals and Beasts. <br /> <br /> That said, it seems to me that many of the concerns about Elementals, Beasts, and Kiths will be addressed by the \u201cthree sample Seemings per Kith\u201d bit: <i>every</i> Kith that used to be tailored specifically for Beasts or Elementals will now include examples of how to associate them with other Seemings, and many Kiths that previously had nothing to do with Beasts or Elementals will now have examples of how to associate them with Beasts and/or Elementals. So I\u2019m <i>also</i> interested in seeing some of th sample Kiths. <br /> <br /> Strike that: I\u2019m interested in seeing everything in CtL2e. Publish it tomorrow! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=