ass=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:37:43-08:00","id":403044,"title":"","content":"Only if it was a dark and stormy night.<br /> <br /> Or Future Immemorial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:42:24-08:00","id":403046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=402600#post402600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone ever actually play Avocado?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably haha. I am reluctant to cite particular problematic ones I have seen because I do not want to indirectly point the finger at characters currently in play. But, I have run into certain versions of Elements which make for very challenging calls on the part of the ST. You want fair play and consistent expectations, and some element choices don't really guarantee that. You also want versatility and creativity, so limiting it severely is also problematic. This is a case where I do not come with the answers, only the concerns and the hopes for a better tomorrow. X)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:55:44-08:00","id":403060,"title":"","content":"Right, side stepping asides...<br /> <br /> I don't want to waste a lot of time on this, I'm writing fantasy right now, so I do want to just say this: I know the works of the writers David Hill has compiled for this projects, and I can uniformly say that they all have been awesome. I think they'll keep the versatility and awesomeness of the the splat and it's many branches that we know while sharpening the gameplay and setting details-in short, I have no reason to expect less than superb results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T23:02:40-08:00","id":403064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=403060#post403060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, side stepping asides...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm, was that side stepping? I apologize. :/ I have no reason to expect less that superb results either, I'm just asking questions about stuff that's important to me while trying not to offend anyone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T23:05:27-08:00","id":403066,"title":"","content":"Well, it was and it wasn't. I figure with Kiths coming up for discussion soon, fretting about Elemental/Kith relations is a little silly for now,and at the same time, while I'm amused by the drop of plush in a teddy bear ocean or an Avocado Elemental, I've never met anyone who's done something like that and had to ask if we wanted flexibility for flexibility's sake rather than practical application.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T23:18:26-08:00","id":403077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=403066#post403066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it was and it wasn't. I figure with Kiths coming up for discussion soon, fretting about Elemental/Kith relations is a little silly for now,and at the same time, while I'm amused by the drop of plush in a teddy bear ocean or an Avocado Elemental, I've never met anyone who's done something like that and had to ask if we wanted flexibility for flexibility's sake rather than practical application.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay! The authors can only provide general thoughts on where they hope to go with the book, so I'm giving general concerns rather than fingering particular characters--even if indirectly. I think we can talk about the general issue without doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T16:23:00-08:00","id":407120,"title":"","content":"I think you could merge a lot of kits together, woodbloods/flowering, Tellars/Greys for an alien Kith, Nightsingers/Minstrels, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T16:20:43-08:00","id":414573,"title":"","content":"Well, OK, I know I'm a bit late to the party, here, and I haven't read all 27 pages of this, (did read the last five pages, at least...) but no point holding back...<br /> <br /> There were two general disappointments I had in kiths from the first edition.<br /> <br /> The first was the general lack of relevance the kith had to the game relative to its core defining characteristic of what makes your character unique and different. Contracts are also important, but anyone can buy them, and skills and other stats are anything any human can get. But kiths really only gave some minor gimmick or skill boost, but for a few rare powerful ones with broad usage. (Hello, Mirrorskin!)<br /> <br /> The second was the rather ham-handed cramming of too-widely divergent mythological creatures into a handful of labels. The core book lists Japanese kitsune as just another Hunterheart. This makes them no different from any other random changeling that just is a jaguar-man, when they have far different powers more in line with a Fairest than a Beast. Kitsune weren't known for their simply BEING a fox and having claws or speaking to other foxes, they're known for their shapeshifting, cunning, illusions, capacity to conjure fire from nothing, and manipulation of men through their sexuality towards accomplishing their goals. They were everything from evil seductresses, to mystic sages, to trickster punishers of human immorality, to ideal fae-touched lovers. It's even worse for their counterpart/rival mythological creature, the tanuki. Honestly, the best way to play them would be a Darkling Mirrorskin, since their trickery and shapeshifting were their most noted aspects.(Oh how useful you are, Mirrorskin!) (Well, that and the giant ballsacks, but I doubt anyone wants to play with someone who wants magic ballsack powers...) If I wanted to play a tsukumogami, (physical tools that gained anthropomorphization through age and gathering a sentient soul, which may be more in line with spirits, but in many stories act more like a changeling's humanized thought process,) which is a very broad category of creature, they pretty much all had to be an Elemental Mannikin... which gives you nothing more than a coupon for Wizened contracts. Woo. (That, or Treasured One, which was better, but focused upon fortitude rather than actively acting upon the world.)<br /> <br /> That is to say, I think it would be best to focus upon function more than form, as was the norm in the first edition. Looks are largely fluff, and don't need mechanical rules to balance them, so you might want to play down how kiths look in favor of what they can do, or have multiple examples of looks. And again, it really needs to be something that sets a character apart. Picking a Chirugeon means basically declaring your intent to be the healer of the group, but its exact utility was somewhat marginal, as it only helped in slow, non-magical healing, which the player would generally be able to avoid having to rely upon so long as they didn't need to worry about the covertness of their actions. (You can take a merit that lets you just throw goblin fruits at people for faster healing than normal medicine provides, and there are a handful of more interesting contracts that provide more immediate and/or powerful healing.)<br /> <br /> I rather liked the Equinox Road idea of having additional seeming bonuses as you progressed in wyrd. That kept those early-game choices feeling unique and powerful, as they came to continue to loom over your character with greater frailties/penalties. I'd like to see something like that for kiths, as well; Having some evolving power as your wyrd increases makes the choice relevant, even at later-game stages. I.E. a Muse is forever just giving a +2 bonus to someone else's expression skills in 1e, but the effects might be expanded like a contract has clauses at a few different wyrd levels, starting with a free +1 bonus to anyone you have a relationship with at 1 wyrd, to a contract-like paying a couple glamour and a willpower to gain a Leanan Sidhe's power of driving someone to superhuman heights (a +5 to something, or a glamour-infused power), with a self-destructive burnout (subject burns 1 willpower dot) when you hit some point of, say, 7 wyrd. Something in-between at 4 wyrd.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I doubt there will be a way to make enough kiths to make everyone happy, so I think the best way to go would be to focus more on a make-a-kith section that gives general guidelines for how to slap together appropriate advantages and disadvantages to meet anyone's concept's needs, and still have some agreed-upon balance. Maybe not a full-on pick-a-power catalogue like Demon, but at least some guidelines for having a player-storyteller discussion of what sort of thing you want your character to be. I mean, some kiths were more-or-less just a &quot;you get a bonus to a skill&quot; and it wouldn't be hard to just say you can extrapolate that across every skill. (The gladiator kith gets +1 to weaponry, the grappler kith gets +1 to brawl, the huntsbeast kith gets +1 to survival.) Granted, if we're adding more power into the kiths, that'll be harder, but you can write out guidelines for these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T16:44:57-08:00","id":414607,"title":"","content":"Well its been said that Kith benefits are beefier and more powerful now, and the goal is to make them more generally useful. I guess we'll see how powerful they are. It should be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T17:03:05-08:00","id":414618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=414607#post414607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well its been said that Kith benefits are beefier and more powerful now, and the goal is to make them more generally useful. I guess we'll see how powerful they are. It should be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they also seem to be more-or-less keeping the old, just changing the mechanical effects. Hence, I think the problems I had with the old kiths are relevant.<br /> <br /> That said, it depends upon why a player is picking a kith. If they say &quot;I want to be a Rusalka&quot;, it's different from &quot;I want to be an anthropomorphized cat&quot;, and different still from &quot;I want to have really cool powers of manipulation and be some shadowy string-puller.&quot; That is, again, a difference between what they are like in terms of inspirational source material, aesthetics, and function. The problem I always had was that aesthetics seemed to be favored over inspiration (since there was no way to have enough kiths to cover every possible folk creature), and their function was largely secondary.<br /> <br /> I mean, the character I last baked up and am waiting to play, I wanted to make an Irish myth phooka-like character, so I took Darkling Mirrorskin dual kithed with Oracle. If I get around to it, I might add in some Fang and Talon to transform into a Black Dog or a black horse or something as well, but it's the shapeshifting fortune-telling I'm most keying into. The way Changeling has tended to treat it, you're an animal first, and the rest of that stuff about what they do is secondary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":".  Undoing previous edit - making another post 02-21-2015, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T20:00:43-08:00","id":414794,"title":"","content":"I kinda get the sense that they <i>are</i> doing it function-first for 2e. You pick the Kith you want, and then pick which of the 6 Seemings to apply to that, with the intent that all 6 can fit it just fine. I have trouble seeing how they could make that work without making the Kiths relatively flexible and amenable to different interpretations. To this end, David's mentioned that some Kiths will be merged, and that some of the old names may pop up on a particular Seeming's variant suggestion -- no different mechanics, just an additional idea for where that bonus could be coming from.<br /> <br /> In 1e, all the Kiths were written under the assumption that if you were taking it, you had already taken its associated Seeming. In that context, it made sense for all the Beast-associated Kiths to assume the character's an animal, because that was the story the Beast Seeming was trying to tell. The minor bonus from the Kith just helped tell a slightly different version of that story. Like you, I also kinda found this constricting. Nor are we alone; disassociating Seeming and Kith or making more allowances for fluff explanations on the mechanics seems to me to be one of the most common house rules around. It's also another benefit I see to giving the 2e Kiths more potent powers than they've had. It makes the Kith the key factor in the sort of story being told, while the six Seemings offer different ways to help tell it. Or, per the sense I'm getting, the two may wind up being more equal partners in helping to tell a Changeling's story.<br /> <br /> I do kinda wish 1e had gone more into the sort of looseness that lots of fans ultimately went for themselves. Like, taking your Kitsune example. There's nothing wrong with someone taking Beast-Hunterheart for that, if playing up the animal side, and the claws and fangs, is the story the player wants to tell. If the player is more keen on going for the illusion and trickery side of things like you (and, frankly, me), then Darkling-Mirrorskin should be just as valid.<br /> <br /> As a side-note, there may be good news for your phooka-themed character, regarding animal shapeshifting. They're moving away from the 5-dot progression, so a &quot;turn into an animal&quot; Contract would be a single purchase. I can only speak for myself, but I much prefer that to first needing 4 steps that may or may not be very useful and certainly aren't as central in order to get to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T20:39:59-08:00","id":414808,"title":"","content":"Ah, well, I was editing my previous post to tack this on, but since you responded in the intervening time, Gaius, I might as well make it a full post...<br /> <br /> I guess I should be a bit clearer about what I mean... A lot of kiths, especially beast and elemental kiths, seemed to be more about just looking like something than about what players actually want to do with them. Elemental kiths had basically no bearing on the actual powers you could focus upon, so you could be a Fireheart and enjoy buying cheaper water-related powers. For that matter, it had little to particularly say about who your character really tried to do with their lives. In that Fear Maker's Promise supplement, you had a Winter Court Fireheart who enjoyed causing heartbreak for the giggles. There's no link there between kith and character concept. That Fireheart power is to give a boost to wits rolls, of all things.<br /> <br /> An Antiquaraian, meanwhile, says &quot;I'm playing a character who is valued for being very knowledgable.&quot; A Gravewight says, &quot;I want to have a game that involves ghosts, and not just living characters.&quot; An Oracle says, &quot;I want to be a the voice of wisdom in the motley, always cautious, strategic, and sniffing out the traps ahead.&quot; A Gameplayer says, &quot;I want to play some crafty gambler or chessmaster strategist.&quot; A Flowerling says, &quot;I want to wield social influences like a spider weaves its webs.&quot; A Mirrorskin says, &quot;I want to go doppelganger and make my enemies fight each other for me while I laugh from the shadows.&quot; A Gargantuan says, &quot;HULK WANNA SMASH!&quot;<br /> <br /> Kiths are so fascinating because they're the single biggest tip-off of what it is the player wants their character to be. It's the most defining and unique choice they make, and it plays as directly into where they want to take a character as the choice of virtue and vice. That's why I'm saying that there needs to be less focus upon the aesthetics, which you could free up to change as you will, and more upon the paths of what they make the player's characters actually capable of doing that others not of that kith could do.<br /> <br /> This is why there can never be enough kiths, and flexibility is a better way to go. It's both the core character concept and that one thing the player really wants to feel when they play the game. Players pick stealthy or manipulative character types because they enjoy that feeling of cleverness and skill when they manage to pull something off, while players might pick the hulking ogre types when they just enjoy a good beat-down on their enemies. Bring up all those discussions about different player types in RPGs, and you could probably pin kiths to each archetype as being custom-fitted for those player stereotypes. (Although there might be a dearth of &quot;wacky&quot; kiths in CtL...)<br /> <br /> Hence, I'm a bit uneasy about seeing Fireheart just recycled one more time. Fireheart really only said, &quot;I am going to buy contracts relating to fire at some later point,&quot; but anyone could do that. It was a kith that existed largely just for the aesthetics of being a guy with fire hair, not for what they said about the player, or let the player do. Now, maybe that's changing, maybe it's some full-on set of fire-related contracts you can't get somewhere else, but I'm not sure that's the case, and even if it were, what's the theme? What's that thing a fire kith does that makes it blatantly obvious what the player wants to do? (I mean, barring wanting to be a Fire Bender and Kung Fu fighting with an Airtouched...) The only reason they'd recycle the kith is if they want to maintain continuity with the old line, so it wouldn't make sense to warp its intent TOO heavily, but without really restructuring it, they aren't going to make it a signal of the player's intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 02-21-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T06:09:05-08:00","id":415078,"title":"","content":"To again give an example of what I mean, I saw somewhere in this thread a correlation between Flowerling and Woodblood, because &quot;plants&quot;. But, again, the reason why someone would want a Flowerling, whose main purpose is seduction, (with a dryad/nymph-like aesthetic,) is drastically different from why someone would want a Woodblood, whose main purpose is toughness and a rather direct, literal connection to nature. <br /> <br /> If the name of the game, however, is to divine where the kiths are going from what's been said, the previous MachineIV post on what's being merged because of &quot;similarities&quot;, provides the more obvious route of long-distance psychoanalysis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=396910#post396910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Windwing/Lurkglider</span></span> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Stonebones/Earthbones</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Cleareyes/Cyclopean </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hunterheart/</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Razorhand</span></span> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Palewraith/Shadowsoul</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Waterborn/Swimmerskin</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Succubus/Romancer</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">I think there are maybe some others; these were just from the first list brought up. But, these might be cases where you get one as the main kith, and one is just an example Seeming variant on it. Or something. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Now, as MachineIV says, these are more rough-draft than final product, but the very fact that it's what they first bring up indicates that it's their innate reaction, the one that most indicates the governing philosophy they are using to make these decisions.<br /> <br /> Windwing/Lurkglider seem pretty obvious and harmless, since Lurkglider was originally sold pretty much as a Windwing for Darklings. <br /> <br /> Razorhand/Hunterheat shows an even more powerful correlation of use rather than aesthetics, because Razorhand had the aesthetics of Freddy Kreuger versus just any random predatory animal, although on a subtle level, they were different. (You always have a lethal weapon at hand versus your brawl being lethal.) However, where's the Draconic? Draconic was just a Hunterheart in Fairest clothing by mechanics...<br /> <br /> That said, some are a bit problematic. Stonebones is about being strong (strength buff), while Earthbones is about being tough (armor bonus). It seems these are bundled more by being &quot;earth-based&quot;, since there's a big difference in a player's role in the motley when they say they want to go on offense and when they want to tank, even if both have to do with combat. Even if both are combat-focused, it's the difference between the berserker and the paladin.<br /> <br /> Palewraith and Shadowsoul is even stranger, as they have little but &quot;darkness&quot; in common. Shadowsoul is about intimidation in use, but the cross between shadow and beauty in aesthetics. Palewraith is about reinforcing the keep-to-the-shadows nature of Darklings in use, and about being the forgotten even among Darklings in aesthetics. I don't know where those cross over at all. It seems the idea was that Shadowsoul needed to be merged into something that was a &quot;generic darkling&quot; because the Seeming-blending purpose of the kith was gone, and they just grabbed Palewraith because it was one they didn't feel like keeping, rather than because it, specifically had anything in common with Shadowsoul.<br /> <br /> Combining Succubus and Romancer under the name of just differentiating kiths by seeming is a little strange, as well, being as they come from the same seeming to begin with! I get the sense Succubus needs to get the axe since vices don't work the same way, while Romancer's actual utility was completely different from its stated aesthetics. (That is, it makes you harder to identify to other people, rather than having anything to do with seduction.) In terms of function, Romancer has more to do with Mirrorskin...<br /> <br /> Also notable is that a lot of these are Beasts and Fairest. Someone else mentioned earlier in the thread how Wizened were basically all aesthetically the same, but their kiths were just different specialties, the jobs that you were going to dedicate yourself to, which makes them already solidly molded to the notion of being that signifier of intent. There aren't any Wizened on that list. Meanwhile, as I said before, Beasts and Elementals are the vaguest of the seemings, with kiths more focused upon just giving you the aesthetics of a general family of animals or elemental appearance, rather than actually giving you gameplay mechanics related to being one. <br /> <br /> If you look at a kith like Airtouched and Runnerswift, however, those are basically similar in effect, but wildly divergent in aesthetics, and they're not being merged, at least in this list. I again have to question whether or not it would be better to just wipe the list of elementals, almost entirely, and make them just the elemental aspects of a different kind of kith. A kith that focuses upon anger, like Hunterheart, and has an elemental seeming could be the equivalent of a Fireheart whose aesthetic is based around fire = passion/anger. Rather than being predatory claws and fangs, they may simply have a searing hot grasp. If you wanted to have more the &quot;mind that is powerful and flowing like a fire&quot;, like the original effect was, you would take something like Riddleseeker with an elemental seeming. If you wanted a more stand-back-and-hurl-fireballs-like-a-wizard type of Fireheart, then you take... well, there's no kith that's really like that, at least not directly. If you want a boost to your fire contracts, you're better off just going for more Manipulation or Wits, since those are the stats you use for the contracts. (Although Troll and Chateline have Manipulation buffs, amusingly enough...) Which is kind of the problem I had with the old elemental kiths, as they had only to do with aesthetics, and not with the actual driving playstyle a player would enjoy playing. <br /> <br /> The Snowskin ironically has more in common with the Shadowsoul than Shadowsoul has with Palewraith, since it's bonuses to intimidation and subterfuge that are their main kith powers. <br /> <br /> Finally, the Winter Masks direct references to different cultural mythological creatures, like the Illes or Oni, are great as a way of telling people how to make additional kiths to suit a specific desired inspiration, but they open up a completely new can of worms when it comes to effects. For one, there are far more than one way of interpreting an Oni, from the punishers of sin on one hand to just plain demons on another to just wild, barbaric drunkards with comically huge strength on yet another, still. For another, they're rather specific takes on legends, so they wouldn't play well with the different flavors of seemings. They are pretty prime candidates for trying to strip down into what people would want to do with those kiths, and generalizing, rather than keeping as a specific take on a legend. If you focus on the &quot;what they push players towards doing&quot; parts, you can make an Illes or, for that matter, a Rusalka if you focus upon either the water-dwelling or temporary beauty parts. In fact, you could reproduce some legends of the Jurogumo, a giant spider monster, or the skin-stealing Hags by expanding that base glamour of a pretty face thrown over a hideous monster part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:33:47-08:00","id":415786,"title":"","content":"Actually Succubus being a Darkling of Romancer makes sense given that Darklings are as I understand it Changelings who sacrificed the light within themselves, to escape and reclaim thier identity, either literally or figuratively.<br /> <br /> So a Succubus would be a Romancer who used her or his ability to seduce to hurt someone in their attempt to escape or preformed some sex act that they cost them deeply, either a betrayal or so taboo/profane that it took something within them, perhaps a moral compass, the ability to love or truth, their religious faith.<br /> <br /> So a Nun who because a Romancer, who betrayed her faith to seduce the guards to escape might feel that it was a betrayal of Jesus, they her spiritual connection is now gone, and so she becames a Darkling, a Succubus subset of the Romancer Kith, her sacrificing her faith/oath to Jesus twisting her into a Succubus.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps an Incubus seduced a fellow changeling who wished to escape and stole thier chance a betrayal so profound it took something from them that they can never get back, and twisted thier appearance.<br /> <br /> I'll add that they've changed many if not all Kith blessings, making them beefier, so I doubt Romancer and Shadowsoul will have the same Kith blessings. I'm curious as to what Kith blessings they get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T16:05:34-08:00","id":415807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=415786#post415786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Succubus would be a Romancer who used her or his ability to seduce to hurt someone in their attempt to escape or preformed some sex act that they cost them deeply, either a betrayal or so taboo/profane that it took something within them, perhaps a moral compass, the ability to love or truth, their religious faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense if Succubi (or Fooccubi, since gender-neutral,) were listed as a Darkling to begin with, but they're Fairest in 1e, as a specifically Jewish &quot;cultural&quot; kith. <br /> <br /> In the midst of things like waterborn being combined with swimmerskin, which are both just different seeming versions of a similar &quot;under the sea&quot; theme, where the point is that when two things are basically the same kith from different seemings, they can be merged, when there's two kiths from the SAME seeming, it means it sticks out as different. <br /> <br /> Basically, they're just using the <i>name</i> &quot;succubus&quot; again, and not as a kith, which is effectively the same as just deleting it outright. It's not there to have the same purpose it once had as a way of being a culture-specific flavor of mythical creature. That said, it may not be much of a loss, since I'm not sure how many people really wanted to go for an &quot;exotic foreign culture's kith&quot; and go for Judeo-Christian town. The same goes for Romancer, since, if it's going to be like what a Succubus was <i>supposed</i> to be, then all its actual functions are also going to be erased. <br /> <br /> Or in even simpler terms still, these are two kiths that are just plain being deleted because their name's connotations were not at all what they actually delivered players, and nobody played them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:03:01-08:00","id":415939,"title":"","content":"The mechanics change, but the basic fluff would like remain, Romancers are likely to be about well romance as seen by the Gentry, and Succubus are still fallen in a sense, via using thier sexual it as a weapon or moral violation still, a bit fallen Romancers instead of fallen Fairest, but I have a feeling that Romancers will likely inherit much of the 1e Fairest Mantle anyways. Just a guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:57:18-08:00","id":416233,"title":"","content":"With such myths of the Dullahan and other such faerie creatures like the Bull Beggars, who are able to remove their own heads (and possibly other body parts) were you thinking about a correlating kith which could perform such bizarre physical feats?<br /> <br /> Also, fairy tales are full of faeries transforming humans into various shapes--shrinking them, turning them into animals (which could be reversed with strong emotional displays, such as a kiss), turning people to stone, etc. Would you have any contract ideas or powers for these kinds of things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 02-23-2015, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:48:33-08:00","id":416521,"title":"","content":"Hellovg that would be cool and interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:42:58-08:00","id":416935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=415939#post415939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics change, but the basic fluff would like remain, Romancers are likely to be about well romance as seen by the Gentry, and Succubus are still fallen in a sense, via using thier sexual it as a weapon or moral violation still, a bit fallen Romancers instead of fallen Fairest, but I have a feeling that Romancers will likely inherit much of the 1e Fairest Mantle anyways. Just a guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you're getting your idea of what a Romancer is about is from, but it only appears in Night Horrors as the kith of a sample psychotic Cotton Mather-style fundamentalist preacher Bridge Burner, and the kith's description is that of being like a mirror to whoever looks at them because Gentry are narcissist, so the Romancer looks however a Gentry wants them to look (which, to a Gentry, is like the Gentry in question.)<br /> <br /> Again, it's a misleading name to start with. In spite of the name, there's NOTHING about romance in the Romancer's kith description. <br /> <br /> Hence, again, it honestly has more in common with Mirrorskin than Succubus, which was about the older Jewish concept of an evil woman who dares to exert power outside of serving her husband, and it seems that people are just latching onto names without actually paying attention to what they were actually implemented in the game in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T18:55:33-08:00","id":417051,"title":"","content":"I don't think kiths are all going to be mirror images of thier origin, there will be commonalities, but some differences too. I do think your right in the sense that Romancer will likely shift away more from its origins, but Succubi I think will be a bit closer or as close as it can be with vices working different.<br /> <br /> Until we see some fleshed out examples, such as the Romancer Kith itself we just don't know and all of this is just guess work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T12:43:35-08:00","id":420545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=417051#post417051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think kiths are all going to be mirror images of thier origin, there will be commonalities, but some differences too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think the problem is that people saw different things in these kiths in the first place. Especially those that a given person didn't play. Hence, the argument that the focus should be on &quot;what kind of character does this enable/encourage/enpower&quot; rather than &quot;what does this look like&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically, the problem I have is that they're promising us that, &quot;don't worry, none of your favorite kiths will really go away!&quot; but I'm not sure that's really what the game needs. We weren't really all that attached to specific kiths in the first place - why else would we want to dual kith so much? - but rather, what they allowed our characters to symbolize. It seems like we're getting too attached to a name, and not the concepts they represented, and if the new kiths are built around just preserving a name, rather than the concepts they let us play, it will limit what the new kiths can be, in a way.<br /> <br /> Another problem is that it's just plain vague how powerful kiths are going to be. They say &quot;more powerful&quot; but give no real sense of how much more powerful. Is this taking away the 9-agains in favor of a +2 and 9-again, or is it full-on innate contracts?<br /> <br /> Again, I'd think it best to have a minor contract line in power based upon unlocking powers with new wyrd levels, along with possibly kith-specific drawbacks. (From a story perspective, the wyrd that permeates the changeling manifests more strongly pulls them away from humanity, letting certain wondrous tricks become effortless. From a play perspective, one of the reasons kiths were weak was because they were the same power with new characters as late-game characters that sneezed more glamour than a new character could wield.) For example, that water breathing kith might take a glamour to breathe underwater or only hold their breath at wyrd 1, but at wyrd 3 graduate to full water breathing for free, and could have outright underwater houses. The windwing kiths were lame, but flight is such a major advantage that it's understandable why it was left out. Maybe make it a wyrd 7 power-up, and even then, still cost glamour.<br /> <br /> Another route might be merits that are restricted to certain types of kiths, so that you can customize a kith mid-gameplay de facto without it being de jure. I remember the Gravewight kith and the 1 dot Shade and Spirit merged in function so much that having both combined into just letting you activate it for free at will. Merits that make kiths with high affinity for specific contracts either cheaper or innate free powers would be great. Alternately, you might make &quot;merit trees&quot; that branch a kith out in different powers. For example, Venombites might share a claw or fang merit chain with Hunterhearts and Gristlegrinders, letting them produce more fearsome bites that combine with their poison-delivery, or might take a merit that upgrades a weak venom into having more diverse effects, like a sleep poison or a hallucinogenic.<br /> <br /> In fact, again, I think it might be better to have a more generic set of kiths in general. Gristlegrinders, Hunterhearts, Draconics, Soldiers, and Razorhands might all be boiled down to a combat kith, and then given a minor option of differentiation by a couple free specialized kith merits over what precise specialization they gain. A lot of the Wizened can be made into a &quot;dwarf&quot; or &quot;gnome&quot; kith (differentiated by seeming) with a minor differentiation merit to determine their specific craft.<br /> <br /> Making them merits also means you could hypothetically go back to them and diversify or rank up a merit to specialize. If preventing people from just buying everything is a problem, you might set a limit to kith specializations to wyrd level or make a compounding cost formula (each kith specialization takes two more experience, no matter what tier it is from).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 02-26-2015, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T00:53:26-08:00","id":421456,"title":"","content":"So, right up front, I'm curious where this kith power adjustment leaves the flyers. Recent releases seem to have gotten past WoD's fear of flying, but a kith doesn't come with the same drawbacks as a demon form or investment as protean 4. So do we get a very good glider? A glider with another bonus? Or a real flyer?<br /> <br /> I'm also interested in how exactly the definitions and sorting of kith v. seeming v. court shake out - with the new lineup there's even more room to explore asymmetry and conflict in building the character. Like, consider all the tropes you get out of a princess-type myth figure rebelling against her role. That's probably a gamespace relevant to a lot of people. I've played around with this in the past as a Fairest who tried to become a gritty Summer after their escape, but now there seems to be room to explore the clash earlier.<br /> <br /> Take the Romancer/Succubus kith as the role. They were cast by their Keeper that way. But rebellion and seeming starts right there in Arcadia. So maybe she gets out with slow stubborn Shawshank-style scheming, and she ends up a Wizened. Or she turns to great impersonal forces beyond her and seduces the stars, and she becomes an Elemental (and kind of a new way to Telluric, in a way). Or take the closest route to my action-heroine summer thing, and have her fight and mash and kill her way out as an Ogre.<br /> <br /> Then with courts you could set up a third point of contrast. Maybe she doesn't want to totally embrace her ogre violence either once she escapes, so she joins something along the lines of the Day Court to sublimate her violent drives and social wiles into an enlightened cause. Or her choice of court lines up with kith or seeming - she joins something more Spring-like and revels in being the Romancer as long as it's on her own terms (and gets violent when it isn't).<br /> <br /> The details of making that work, what paths the game pushes me towards, and general playing with the dials and gears will be clearer as we see more, so I'm (intensely) curious. It seems more (and more interesting) to play with then the original Summer Fairest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T01:16:00-08:00","id":421465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=421456#post421456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also interested in how exactly the definitions and sorting of kith v. seeming v. court shake out - with the new lineup there's even more room to explore asymmetry and conflict in building the character. Like, consider all the tropes you get out of a princess-type myth figure rebelling against her role. That's probably a gamespace relevant to a lot of people. I've played around with this in the past as a Fairest who tried to become a gritty Summer after their escape, but now there seems to be room to explore the clash earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's quite the conflict you seem to think it is. I mean, Draconic Fairest were already &quot;pretty but deadly in physical contests&quot;, and a Summer Fairest would be the &quot;charismatic leader&quot; type. (Or at least, assume they were the leader...) The Lily, Saber, and Thorn chapter even has its bombastic Breton leader as a Summer Draconic Fairest.<br /> <br /> Summer, if anything, is just the reaction to what you fear with anger, as well as a love for direct competition. There's plenty of room in that for Fairest of athletic talent or an interest in organizing people towards direct conflict with one's opponents. <br /> <br /> If you're talking about what kiths mean in the next game to a character, then it's more what was done TO you, what you didn't have a choice over. Seeming now seems to be the regaining of that choice. Hence, there's not necessarily a conflict, there. Courts, however, have been about the psychological scars left upon the character. The specific manifestation of PTSD they bear, if you will. It was much more a declaration of where a character is going than the Seeming was. I'm not sure what they're really doing with that aspect, but I'm wondering if they will have as much symbolism when they're more generic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T20:41:44-08:00","id":422567,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think there's any reason to doubt that you could readily be pretty, deadly, and fairest all at the same time. Or that fairest could join the summer court. What I'm talking about is setting up contrasts between what the character has been made to be and what they want to be - not the draconic fairest as the military leader, but the succubus or flowering or playmate who tries to reinvent themselves as a lithe Rambo. Like making a Wizened Soldier who joins up with Spring and tries to fight as little as possible, or the Ogre Gristlegrinder who tries to break their cannibal addiction and work as a healer.<br /> <br /> Again, all to some degree things you could already do, but that the new setup gives more space and tools to explore them. In the case of the Gristlegrinder, for example, you could now have them breaking out as a Wizened or even a Fairest, and there'd be a part of their core powers they didn't want to turn their back on. Or you could double down on the gruesome template elements by sticking with Ogre, or make them a Darkling, and play with that.<br /> <br /> Before, the &quot;what you were made into&quot; encompassed both Seeming and Kith. Narrowing that to just Kith opens up new possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T08:54:41-08:00","id":422981,"title":"","content":"Well, I have to wonder how many people really want to make a character who has a power just to not use it? That fairest gristlegrinder idea doesn't really make much sense unless you're playing them to be something like an ogre by nature who pretends to be pretty and sedate, <a href=\"http://bambooblade.wikia.com/wiki/Miyako_Miyazaki\" target=\"_blank\">but breaks the facade on frequent occasion</a>. (In fact, going by the above logic, you might just have a &quot;brawler&quot; kith, and the ogre version is the Gristlegrinder, while the fairest version is the Draconic.)<br /> <br /> Kiths are your most significant, unique, and defining power. Very, very few people would waste them on something they would actively go out of their way to not use. You can throw away some skill points into brawl and streetwise or something to say you were a ruffian in your youth, then the durance turned you around, because you can always get more skill points. <br /> <br /> In fact, I still think that, if we're to separate out a &quot;what you were made into&quot; and &quot;what you chose to become&quot;, that kith should be the choice, and seeming should be what was forced. Seeming, at least in 1e, comes from the environment you were in during the durance, while kith comes from what you did. Darklings were the changelings in darkness, spawned of chthonic Keepers. Ogres were the ones that had to be hard for brutality was the only way to survive. I mean, who gets out of their durance, and then chooses to have the power to be a tree? Rather, you were forced to be a tree, but you chose what being a tree meant as your kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:59:34-08:00","id":423067,"title":"","content":"It really isn't always super exciting to take a power and then never use it! Which is why the new breakdown makes such a character more viable for more people. Though one of the interesting things about such characters is figuring out how to use it anyway.<br /> <br /> What doesn't make sense about a fairest gristlegrinder? They'd be someone with an irremovable core of violence who hides it behind charm, which is something that shows up all over. Someone in almost every spy story or thriller has something like that in their character. It could be a charming serial killer, or someone trying to go clean, or something in between.<br /> <br /> It's more interesting to take what's been described and try to make it work then to try and fit old ideas into it squarely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:08:16-08:00","id":423237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423067#post423067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What doesn't make sense about a fairest gristlegrinder? They'd be someone with an irremovable core of violence who hides it behind charm, which is something that shows up all over. Someone in almost every spy story or thriller has something like that in their character. It could be a charming serial killer, or someone trying to go clean, or something in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe it's me, but doesn't that just describe what a Draconic always was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:17:48-08:00","id":423487,"title":"","content":"A 1e draconic fairest was made to be martial and social. A 2e gristlegrinder fairest was made to be martial and chose to be social.<br /> <br /> Seeming now means that the power you wield is defined by how you took it more than what you were made. That's a telling change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:45:18-08:00","id":423510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423487#post423487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeming now means that the power you wield is defined by how you took it more than what you were made. That's a telling change.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that, but I still feel it's backwards. <br /> <br /> I mean, I just have trouble seeing how someone CHOOSES to be the ogre, or CHOOSES to be the creature cursed to darkness. It makes far more sense to me that they were cast into darkness, and then their kith was what they used to get out of it. They were cast into the bloody brawl, and their kith is how they kicked and fought their way out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T16:23:36-08:00","id":423538,"title":"","content":"You don't choose to be an Ogre or a Darkling. You choose to escape. Your method of escape dictates your Seeming in the new paradigm.<br /> <br /> In many ways, this means that before escaping a changeling is just their Kith. One living in darkness is just a being that lives in darkness. It isn't until they choose to make the effort to escape that they refine themselves into a more specific expression of that. A fighter in the bloody pits is a violent brawler. It isn't until they escape, and the agency they get from it, shapes that into a more specific form via their Seeming.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T16:33:54-08:00","id":423543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423538#post423538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't choose to be an Ogre or a Darkling. You choose to escape. Your method of escape dictates your Seeming in the new paradigm.<br /> <br /> In many ways, this means that before escaping a changeling is just their Kith. One living in darkness is just a being that lives in darkness. It isn't until they choose to make the effort to escape that they refine themselves into a more specific expression of that. A fighter in the bloody pits is a violent brawler. It isn't until they escape, and the agency they get from it, shapes that into a more specific form via their Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the way that Seemings work, they're mostly the &quot;color&quot; of your wyrd. They're not related to what you do, but to what your power source is in terms of glamour. Hence, it seems like the thing most akin to what you pick up in the environment, rather than what you chose to do, how you chose to form yourself or mount your escape or actually escaped. <br /> <br /> That is, the bloody pit made you an ogre, but you hid on your path back, learned the hedge, and patiently found the trods back while surviving on experimentation and knowledge, making you a Farwalker. The faerie magic within you is that of brute force, but your honed skill and choice define what specializes and refines the raw energy into your kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:32:59-08:00","id":423615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423543#post423543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the way that Seemings work, they're mostly the &quot;color&quot; of your wyrd. They're not related to what you do, but to what your power source is in terms of glamour. Hence, it seems like the thing most akin to what you pick up in the environment, rather than what you chose to do, how you chose to form yourself or mount your escape or actually escaped.<br /> <br /> That is, the bloody pit made you an ogre, but you hid on your path back, learned the hedge, and patiently found the trods back while surviving on experimentation and knowledge, making you a Farwalker. The faerie magic within you is that of brute force, but your honed skill and choice define what specializes and refines the raw energy into your kith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think we might be talking past each other because this is the opposite of what the developer said towards the beginning of the thread! To wit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233377#post233377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a thing to consider.<br /> <br /> We're discussing Seemings as coming out of your escape. The method of escape stains what you were, what role you played in your Durance. That's mostly just to add a little more flavor on the splat intersection, since we're going to front-load the Durance a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233469#post233469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Kith is what they did to you, and Seeming is how you escaped?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=233486#post233486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, yeah. Kith is the role you played in their myth. Seeming is how you broke it. Kith is your Arcadian side. Your flesh is your Earthly side. Seeming is the bridge between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:15:11-08:00","id":423649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423510#post423510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say that, but I still feel it's backwards.<br /> <br /> I mean, I just have trouble seeing how someone CHOOSES to be the ogre, or CHOOSES to be the creature cursed to darkness. It makes far more sense to me that they were cast into darkness, and then their kith was what they used to get out of it. They were cast into the bloody brawl, and their kith is how they kicked and fought their way out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree, it kinda makes more sense that Seeming is &quot;why they were taken&quot; rather than &quot;how they got out&quot;, to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:23:55-08:00","id":423655,"title":"","content":"Really? Becuase it seems pretty clear to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:29:48-08:00","id":423660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423655#post423655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Becuase it seems pretty clear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having just reread the first two chapters of Winter Masques in the last week, I must quite firmly agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:13:12-08:00","id":423682,"title":"","content":"Me too. <br /> <br /> I see 2e Seemings as a refinement of ones Kith, the act of escaping refines your Kith and reconnects it too Earth.<br /> <br /> So maybe Draconic Kith, the role you played was one of a dragon in the Gentry's story, but when you escaped you made a deal with darkness, a piece of your inner light and it would cloak your escape from the Gentry, and it tainted your mein nature, you took on a darker look, you became not just a dragon, but a black dragon or a Dracolich In Appearance (Admittedly a humaniod one). <br /> <br /> On the other hand another Dragonic used his primal instincts to flee, and is more like a Grey Dragon, of the Beast Seeming, another went the opposite way, rejecting his instincts and relied on pure logic to escape, becoming an elemental white dragon, another might have seduced or convinced someone to let you go and so his Dragonic nature shifted into something more like a Gold Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:29:48-08:00","id":423711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423660#post423660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having just reread the first two chapters of Winter Masques in the last week, I must quite firmly agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe I'm just thinking back to the base book, then. In it, the Seemings are not only directly tied to the type of Fae that took you, but also <i>why</i> they took you. Basically, &quot;Darklings are those that transgressed.&quot; Or, &quot;Fairest were selected because they were or did something a Keeper found pretty.&quot; This is also why, when they give out example keepers, they specify which seemings you might get from them, but leave the kiths more-or-less open.<br /> <br /> Kiths are what you DID, and seemings are where you were TAKEN.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423682#post423682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me too.<br /> <br /> I see 2e Seemings as a refinement of ones Kith, the act of escaping refines your Kith and reconnects it too Earth.<br /> <br /> So maybe Draconic Kith, the role you played was one of a dragon in the Gentry's story, but when you escaped you made a deal with darkness, a piece of your inner light and it would cloak your escape from the Gentry, and it tainted your mein nature, you took on a darker look, you became not just a dragon, but a black dragon or a Dracolich In Appearance (Admittedly a humaniod one).<br /> <br /> On the other hand another Dragonic used his primal instincts to flee, and is more like a Grey Dragon, of the Beast Seeming, another went the opposite way, rejecting his instincts and relied on pure logic to escape, becoming an elemental white dragon, another might have seduced or convinced someone to let you go and so his Dragonic nature shifted into something more like a Gold Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but that's only because you're forcing the narrative to comport with the &quot;Seemings come after kiths&quot; that is being thrown out.<br /> <br /> I just said how you could just as easily do this in reverse. In fact, I'll do it again:<br /> <br /> You were taken by a dark shadow power for breaking a rule you never thought existed. You were left in the darkness until it consumed you, and you melded with it. In that state, however, you returned to your senses, and learned how to fight. Fight not as a man, but a beast. You bit and clawed your way out, and for it, your scars, your trophy, is the countenance of a fantastic beast. Your claws are the claws built by rending your way out of the darkness, but even so, the darkness emanates from you, and the deathly pallor of the shadow clings to you, giving you more the semblance of a dracolich than a glistening dragon. (Granted, I still don't see why Draconic isn't just the fairest version of a Hunterheart...)<br /> <br /> Why are we doing it this way, and not the other way around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 02-28-2015, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:41:42-08:00","id":423717,"title":"","content":"I can definitely see how Seeming can be presented as \u201chow I reclaimed my soul\u201d, or some variant thereof, rather than \u201ca broad category of Kiths\u201d \u2014 though the Seeming names still imply the latter. It\u2019s also reminiscent of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>\u2019s approach to Kiths and Seemings (though in <b>Dreaming</b>, your Seeming referred more to your mental age). <br /> <br /> Conceptually, it\u2019s a <i>very</i> nice idea; but mechanically, it raises some concerns: if your Kith is \u201cwhat the Gentry did to you\u201d and your Seeming is \u201chow you took your life back\u201d, then doesn\u2019t that imply that your Curse/Frailty/whatever CtL calls it should be tied to your Kith rather than your Seeming? That is, shouldn\u2019t the Kith be a mixed bag of good and bad stuff while the Seeming is essentially positive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:46:47-08:00","id":423722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423711#post423711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are we doing it this way, and not the other way around?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, it\u2019s because David Hill wants it this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:56:59-08:00","id":423727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423717#post423717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conceptually, it\u2019s a <i>very</i> nice idea; but mechanically, it raises some concerns: if your Kith is \u201cwhat the Gentry did to you\u201d and your Seeming is \u201chow you took your life back\u201d, then doesn\u2019t that imply that your Curse/Frailty/whatever CtL calls it should be tied to your Kith rather than your Seeming? That is, shouldn\u2019t the Kith be a mixed bag of good and bad stuff while the Seeming is essentially positive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that this is only a concern if you ignore the statement that is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232380#post232380\"><i>literally on the first page of this thread</i></a> that indicates seeming curses aren't likely to remain a thing in this paradigm.<br /> <br /> I mean, back in 1e I was toying with the idea of offering an incentive for kithlessness by tying frailties to kiths, but &quot;we're changing the arrangement of fixed-inborn and mutable-inborn splat types around&quot; doesn't seem likely to mean &quot;the thing that is [now] a refinement of [what is now] the core concept of the character's supernatural state is going to be the thing that houses any drawback that that state may possess.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T23:04:52-08:00","id":423862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423727#post423727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should note that this is only a concern if you ignore the statement that is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=232380#post232380\"><i>literally on the first page of this thread</i></a> that indicates seeming curses aren't likely to remain a thing in this paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026or if you take him at his word that it was \u201cnot settled yet\u201d as of the time of the post in question. <i>If</i> Dave has decided to jettison Seeming blessings and curses entirely, then yeah, it\u2019s a non-issue; if he has since decided that there\u2019s merit to keeping either or both around, that\u2019s a different story. The former does seem likely; but it\u2019s not yet verified. <br /> <br /> And yeah, we seem to be in agreement that if splat-based curses are still a thing, Kith Curses make more sense than Seeming Curses \u2014 though we appear to have come to that conclusion through rather different lines of reasoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:04:04-08:00","id":424269,"title":"","content":"No, because part of gaining you Seeming is what you had to do or sacrifice to gain your freedom, which means a Seemings curse is the price for freedom, seeming blessing is the refinement of your Kith that helped gain you your freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:07:04-08:00","id":424272,"title":"","content":"You could do that, that way, but it's not the angle David plans to go with as he wants to &quot;Front Load&quot; Kiths as he put it. Your free to house rule it so that seeming comes from you kidnapping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:08:33-08:00","id":424412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=424272#post424272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do that, that way, but it's not the angle David plans to go with as he wants to &quot;Front Load&quot; Kiths as he put it. Your free to house rule it so that seeming comes from you kidnapping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, again, so far as the themes are concerned, it seems backwards to what the stated goals are.<br /> <br /> If the point is to focus more upon how Changeling took their life back, and the focus is now more upon kiths than seemings, why isn't it the kith, the thing that actively empowers what you DO as a Changeling, the one that is the character's own deliberate choice?<br /> <br /> Seemings deal more with the tone of the magic that pervades you, but not your overall character direction, especially if they are receding in importance. Hence, making seemings the &quot;Abuse Victim&quot; part of the character, which is a legacy of violence that taints your soul and every act or the drip of the inky darkness or the feral mindset of the Keeper, while kiths, the bigger active choice, the specialization, the thing that makes your character unique and gives them that little power edge is the &quot;Abuse Survivor&quot; part. I mean, players build their character's talents around their kith, story-wise. Who picks a kith as a flowerling, and then focuses upon mental skills to the exclusion of social skills? It contradicts the story that characters are reclaiming their own lives if they always play to the life that their Keepers forced upon them, but just pretend it was all their own idea, now. (Because, after all, it IS all the player's idea...)<br /> <br /> Kiths-as-past also means that the things done against your will loom larger as a part of your character's unique flavor, and come in infinite varieties, while your character's active choice is restricted to just 6 choices you are allowed to make. (Or 5 if there's a consolidation...) If you want to play up the character determination to reclaim their lives part, isn't this backwards? Wouldn't making the &quot;enh, there's only a half dozen different types of you, anyway&quot; thing be more in line with the callous indifference of the Keepers? <br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, I get that it's something that's been thrown down to us from on high, but I sort of suspect this wasn't just some utterly random, arbitrary decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:08:52-08:00","id":424413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423862#post423862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026or if you take him at his word that it was \u201cnot settled yet\u201d as of the time of the post in question. <i>If</i> Dave has decided to jettison Seeming blessings and curses entirely, then yeah, it\u2019s a non-issue; if he has since decided that there\u2019s merit to keeping either or both around, that\u2019s a different story. The former does seem likely; but it\u2019s not yet verified.<br /> <br /> And yeah, we seem to be in agreement that if splat-based curses are still a thing, Kith Curses make more sense than Seeming Curses \u2014 though we appear to have come to that conclusion through rather different lines of reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could honestly dig Curses and Blessings to both. I don't especially think it likely, of course, particularly with how much they're trying to fit into that chapter, and wouldn't be surprised if there were indeed no Curses at all. If down to one or the other, though, I agree I'd prefer a Kith Curse; that feels like it would help create a more focused play experience for each Kith. That said, Seeming Curses also have a certain logic: Seeming Blessings (including favored access to parts of particular Contracts) demand their own tolls for seizing control of a personal narrative in such a way. As tightly written as Kiths are, I suspect that Seeming Blessings are the more likely of the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:15:54-08:00","id":424632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=423862#post423862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026or if you take him at his word that it was \u201cnot settled yet\u201d as of the time of the post in question. <i>If</i> Dave has decided to jettison Seeming blessings and curses entirely, then yeah, it\u2019s a non-issue; if he has since decided that there\u2019s merit to keeping either or both around, that\u2019s a different story. The former does seem likely; but it\u2019s not yet verified.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it looks, first drafts won't have curses. I'll feel it out. Kith curses would be kind of difficult, because there's just so many of them to add. We might do seeming. But so far, I don't know that we need them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:08:15-08:00","id":424688,"title":"","content":"For the record, I won\u2019t miss them if they\u2019re gone. I\u2019m assuming that 2e Clarity will have something like VtR2e\u2019s Humanity in the sense of \u201cthat breaking point you just got walloped by? Take some sort of supernatural flaw right w in exchange for never having to mess with it again.\u201d If so, <i>that</i> will nicely handle what few cases I can think of where Seeming Curses have value \u2014 but as an <i>individual</i> curse/frailty/flaw, rather than somethng you\u2019re stuck with because of your splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:29:06-08:00","id":424694,"title":"","content":"Frailties are always a treat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:02:47-08:00","id":424718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=424632#post424632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way it looks, first drafts won't have curses. I'll feel it out. Kith curses would be kind of difficult, because there's just so many of them to add. We might do seeming. But so far, I don't know that we need them.</div> </div> </div> </div> what do Seemings have in the first draft then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:52:53-08:00","id":424741,"title":"","content":"One of the biggest impacts of Seeming that's been discussed is that they'll impact a significant group of Contracts. So in a certain sense the Seeming bonus/curse is going to be in having some Contracts being cheaper and others more expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:32:58-08:00","id":424761,"title":"","content":"Over in the Contracts brainspew, David mentioned that he\u2019s not big on price-based incentives; rather, he\u2019d prefer it if various Seemings gave little tweaks to how a Contract works. I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s still in play (one advantage of price-based awards is that they\u2019re not particularly word-intensive); but I think it is \u2014 if so, your choice of Seeming determines which \u201cbonus effects\u201d you get from your Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T20:31:38-08:00","id":424830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=424761#post424761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over in the Contracts brainspew, David mentioned that he\u2019s not big on price-based incentives; rather, he\u2019d prefer it if various Seemings gave little tweaks to how a Contract works. I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s still in play (one advantage of price-based awards is that they\u2019re not particularly word-intensive); but I think it is \u2014 if so, your choice of Seeming determines which \u201cbonus effects\u201d you get from your Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'll be the case. But I think the way we're doing it, you can buy another Seeming's effects for a Contract as secondary effects. But your Seeming determines the default version of those powers that you get when you acquire the Contract.<br /> <br /> So if you're Fairest, and like the Troll version of a Contract, that's cool. You buy it, and get the Fairest version. But, you can learn the Troll version as an expanded bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T20:35:47-08:00","id":424833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=424830#post424830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you're Fairest, and like the <b>Troll</b> version of a Contract, that's cool. You buy it, and get the Fairest version. But, you can learn the <b>Troll</b> version as an expanded bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, with all respect, izzat a typo (Ogre?), or will we be seeing more than the original six Seemings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T21:10:02-08:00","id":424844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=424833#post424833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er, with all respect, izzat a typo (Ogre?), or will we be seeing more than the original six Seemings?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a typo. I'm going off little sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T21:19:24-08:00","id":424873,"title":"","content":"Ahhah. Not surprising, given how many irons you've got in the fire, but sorry to hear it all the same. Here's hoping you're able to catch up on some sleep soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T21:32:40-08:00","id":424879,"title":"","content":"So: each Kith gives you a neat power; each Seeming gives you free access to appropriate enhancements of various Contracts. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve gotta say, though, that while I\u2019m not going to miss Seeming Curses, I <i>am</i> going to miss Seeming Blessings. I kind of <i>like</i> the fact that, say, being a Fairest gives you an edge in social situations \u2014 and not just when invoking suitable Contracts. If you could keep something like that in 2e, I\u2019d appreciate that. Nothing big or fancy, mind you; 1e\u2019s Seeming Blessings were <i>mostly</i> OK in this regard (though I\u2019d want some tweaking done to a few of them; e.g., if it costs Glamour, it should probably be a Contract).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T22:04:34-08:00","id":424896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=424879#post424879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: each Kith gives you a neat power; each Seeming gives you free access to appropriate enhancements of various Contracts.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve gotta say, though, that while I\u2019m not going to miss Seeming Curses, I <i>am</i> going to miss Seeming Blessings. I kind of <i>like</i> the fact that, say, being a Fairest gives you an edge in social situations \u2014 and not just when invoking suitable Contracts. If you could keep something like that in 2e, I\u2019d appreciate that. Nothing big or fancy, mind you; 1e\u2019s Seeming Blessings were <i>mostly</i> OK in this regard (though I\u2019d want some tweaking done to a few of them; e.g., if it costs Glamour, it should probably be a Contract).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think David actually said Seeming Blessings are no longer a thing. Simply that free access to affiliated enhancements to various Contracts is something Seemings give a character. In the original version of the Outline, I remember spying some baseline benefits that would be part of each Seeming before Contracts even came into it. I have no idea if the plan is to stick with those, switch to another model, or nix the idea in favor of the Contract-only benefits, but I do feel that the former two are more likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T22:23:58-08:00","id":424902,"title":"","content":"I hope you\u2019re right; but reviewing the Outline, I\u2019m not finding anything about Seeming Blessings. The only mechanics I see referenced for Seemings are their effects on Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T23:27:46-08:00","id":424913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=424902#post424902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope you\u2019re right; but reviewing the Outline, I\u2019m not finding anything about Seeming Blessings. The only mechanics I see referenced for Seemings are their effects on Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeming Blessings will still be a thing; they're not in the outline because the Seemings are being done closely with Filamena, who talked to me extensively about them. So I didn't feel like reiterating our conversation for her consumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T07:35:33-08:00","id":426565,"title":"","content":"Good, I'm glad that Dealings still really matter. The choice of 6 seemings x 100+ kiths x I don't know how many courts should make for a lot of interesting combos. That doesn't even include Eldrich/Noble entitlements which may or may not end up in 2.0 changeling core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T10:41:59-08:00","id":427830,"title":"","content":"Well, if we're doing Seemings as a metaphor for how you regained control of your life, I'd honestly prefer it if you broke Seemings completely.<br /> <br /> That is, rather than trying to force every possible way characters could have decided to retake control of their lives into 6 pre-established molds that weren't constructed with this narrative in mind, make up a new batch of Seemings from scratch, such that Seemings fit the narrative, rather than square-pegging everything. The fact that there are about 15 pages of people trying to talk themselves into believing how this could actually work is actually a sort of proof in and of itself how difficult it is to really square that circle. It's better to have a clean break in that case and vaporize old Seemings, like the way that virtues and vices just plain get vaporized in the new edition. <br /> <br /> Again, I think that kiths are the most defining thing about how you choose for your character to live, and as such, making that the thing that someone else supposedly chose for your goes contrary to any notion that the character is in definite control of their life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:54:37-08:00","id":430522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, again, so far as the themes are concerned, it seems backwards to what the stated goals are.<br /> <br /> If the point is to focus more upon how Changeling took their life back, and the focus is now more upon kiths than seemings, why isn't it the kith, the thing that actively empowers what you DO as a Changeling, the one that is the character's own deliberate choice?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=427830#post427830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I think that kiths are the most defining thing about how you choose for your character to live, and as such, making that the thing that someone else supposedly chose for your goes contrary to any notion that the character is in definite control of their life.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I disagree with this. This is a horror game and the focus of the game is on how the Changeling is TAKING their life back, present and ongoing not past tense . It's an ongoing process, making the Changeling struggle to be in control of their lives is the point.<br /> <br /> I see it like this:<br /> <br /> Kith is what the Fae made me and defines what I am. (The is backstory)<br /> Seeming is the beginning of me regaining my agency that allows the escape from the total control of the Fae. (So is this)<br /> Now I have to work to decide if what I am can be more than what the Fae made me. (This is actually playing the game)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T17:01:11-08:00","id":430841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=430522#post430522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> See, I disagree with this. This is a horror game and the focus of the game is on how the Changeling is TAKING their life back, present and ongoing not past tense . It's an ongoing process, making the Changeling struggle to be in control of their lives is the point.<br /> <br /> I see it like this:<br /> <br /> Kith is what the Fae made me and defines what I am. (The is backstory)<br /> Seeming is the beginning of me regaining my agency that allows the escape from the total control of the Fae. (So is this)<br /> Now I have to work to decide if what I am can be more than what the Fae made me. (This is actually playing the game)<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much in line with my thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:46:36-07:00","id":437845,"title":"","content":"I honestly liked Kith and Seeming both as facets of &quot;What you became&quot;, but I'm open to seeing what you come up with.<br /> <br /> I did want to ask, re: Seeming blessings, whether there'll be an &quot;evening out&quot; in that regard. Beasts and Elementals kind of got shafted in the previous edition over that. Fairest, especially as they grow in power, can wield tremendous social influence; Ogres grow increasingly mighty; Darklings just get stealthier and sneakier. Elementals get to be slightly more resilient, and Beasts get a more medial version of the above bonuses. It'd be nice if everyone got to have moments where they really feel like they can pour into that fae role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T17:36:26-07:00","id":457507,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm really interested to see how this turns out, although I'm scared how the Wizened seeming will be translated into the new paradigm. I've never seen them as just crafty and intelligent. In 1e out of all the Seemings, the Wizened were the definition of abuse, torment and pain amd pointless torture, which goes beyond the capability of the human mind or body to comprehend. And then if you're lucky, the Keeper forces you to do something, to learn and execute a specific task/craft/art and learn it well. And then comes the moment you are able to escape on your own accord with all the knowledge and skills and spite your earned from your Keeper. They symbolized triumph through persistence, cunning and being able to sacrifice in order to be free.This is what really grabbed me initially to the Wizened, and I feel like much of it will be stripped away in order to turn it into &quot;agency&quot;.<br /> <br /> The other seemings I can easily imagine and I think they would work great in 2E, I'm acually excited to see how they &quot;translate&quot;. But I only cringe when I think about the Wizened as agency. Will I be able to recreate my Wizened Chirurgeon, abducted by Grey Alien Keepers, who has spent 7 years in intense and pointless torture, and then 7 years of service (vivisecting other changelings, messing up their bodies and torturing them) and then escaped after 7 failed attempts? If I can replicate that in 2E I would be super happy, as this is one of my first concepts to hook me into the game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3567,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3567-dobyk","user":"Dobyk","date":". 03-26-2015, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3567-dobyk","name":"Dobyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3567_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T05:31:11-07:00","id":464598,"title":"","content":"I think it's really cool the switch of paradigma, it has even more sense. <br /> Kith are the role that a Changeling has in Arcadia &quot;society&quot;, that is forced by a Keeper, it's not a choice (at least not a choice of a character). When a Changeling gains the will to rebel and affirm himself accepting and using Wyrd it change, inside and outside.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=415807#post415807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would make sense if Succubi (or Fooccubi, since gender-neutral,) were listed as a Darkling to begin with, but they're Fairest in 1e, as a specifically Jewish &quot;cultural&quot; kith.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Please no, everything but not &quot;Fooccubi&quot;. I can't even think how someone can even think a neologism like that... &quot;Succubi&quot; is already a male/neutral form invented by German priest at the end of XV century to indicate a &quot;demon&quot; of Roman tradition (never recognized by the Church as &quot;true&quot; demon, at least as i know, it doesn't even exist in Latin's dictionaries as a term, you can only find succuba/ae and it is not referred to a demon, it just means &quot;female who lies under&quot;; in the form &quot;Succubus&quot; it means &quot;something who lies under&quot;). <br /> <br /> To creators:<br /> I never read Winter Mask and i discovered now that kith (i searched in ww wiki to be sure of that):<br /> Lilith was never recognized by the Church too, if you are ispired to semitic mithology I suggest to don't use latin term to identify their entities, you know, jews are really gelous of their stuff. Use a jewish/arab/aramaic term, it is even more exotic. <br /> <br /> I don't know were to put another suggestion (not pertinent in this thread) so i put it here:<br /> I think that Changeling: the Lost is one of the best book made of nwod (even if the Italian version had many mistakes), it just let feel the mood since beginning, was maybe even better than lots of novels I read (even the little stories are wonderful) but i had a problem with it; the game is huuuuuge and the rules for every situation/power/particular contract (with dreams, tokiens, fetch ecc ecc) were organized a bit chaotically. During narration i prefered ignore lot of rules because I needed too much time to search in the manual.<br /> Will you put a recap at the end of chapters (or in the appendix)? Or just a more user friendly layout?<br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> (I know my english is bad, even if i read lot of stuff in english I'm not used to write/talk)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5535-priapo","name":"Priapo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T10:30:38-07:00","id":464842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Priapo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=464598#post464598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To creators:<br /> I never read Winter Mask and i discovered now that kith (i searched in ww wiki to be sure of that):<br /> Lilith was never recognized by the Church too, if you are ispired to semitic mithology I suggest to don't use latin term to identify their entities, you know, jews are really gelous of their stuff. Use a jewish/arab/aramaic term, it is even more exotic.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of what's made of the story of Lilith nowadays actually comes from a text called The Alef-Bet of Ben-Sira, which is basically a book satirizing 'those backwards Jews'. Lilith, in her original context, was solely the mother of demons and an entity that caused infant death/miscarriage; not the first wife of Adam.<br /> <br /> (Note: I'm a Jew myself, and have made extensive study on this topic.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":2192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","user":"Heu","date":". 04-01-2015, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T12:36:52-07:00","id":464973,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the information. I just wanted say that for me succubus/incubus should be used as generic term instead as an jewish ethnical fae, because those terms were used by romans before even enter in contact with jews to indicate the gods and the goddessess who entered in dreams to... well... have fun without asking permission as they were used to, but even bad dreams were associated to them (fun fact: incubus -that means &quot;male/thing that lies on&quot; means also nightmare -i don't know if is a common knowledge-). After the raise of Christianity those figures, that were not completely good, but neither completely evil, became &quot;demonized&quot; (another fun fact: &quot;incubus&quot; was usually used for the goat-god Faunus, who was considered the most responsible for those intrusions).<br /> <br /> I think that incubus/succubus are wonderful EPITHETs for True Faes, or Changelings with their attitude, usable in game instead to waste it randomly for a kith that is not really appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5535-priapo","name":"Priapo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T21:58:46-07:00","id":467000,"title":"","content":"&quot;What do you mean I can't be a Steepscrambler Wizened? My character concept is (Monkey with Typewriter). What do you mean I have to pick a Kith second and a Seeming first? Shouldn't it be the other way around? Fine I'll pick a Wizened kith to go with my Beast kith. at the cost of being in XP Debt by 10 exp.&quot;<br /> <br /> The above conversation happened all the way back in 2009 when I was talking with my Storyteller and I was a new player to the game. I honestly like this thread's proposal instead. Kith first, seeming second. If seemings are still a thing. In my six years of playing CTL I have seen plenty of new player's tripped up by this same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5554-psychic_monkey","name":"Psychic_Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T11:54:59-07:00","id":468610,"title":"","content":"Seemings are still a thing. I agree, I think this is far more natural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}